<script id="embedded-data" type="application/json">{"title":"Tara Seshan · AI's third era（Lenny's Podcast）","slug":"lennys-podcast-tara-seshan-ai-third-era","audio":"","mediaType":"audio","source":"lennys-podcast-tara-seshan-ai-third-era.bilingual.srt","hash":"f0a6a102","prevHashes":["530aee34"],"cues":[{"i":1,"s":0.04,"e":14.48,"en":"If you think about the first era of AI products as chat, the second era of these products working with agents, that third era that might come soon is how do you work with a persistent coworker who is able to get things done with you.","zh":"如果把 AI 产品的第一个时代看作聊天，第二个时代是与 agent 协作，那么很快可能到来的第三个时代，就是你如何与一位持续在线的同事一起把事情做成。"},{"i":2,"s":14.68,"e":19.36,"en":"There's this idea of the overhang of what AI is capable of and what we're actually doing with it.","zh":"有一种说法叫「能力过剩」——AI 能做到的，和我们实际用它做的，之间存在落差。"},{"i":3,"s":19.4,"e":23.96,"en":"So hard to understand what is going to emerge in the future.","zh":"太难判断未来会涌现出什么了。"},{"i":4,"s":24.24,"e":27.24,"en":"You fail if you build for where the models are now. You fail","zh":"如果你照着模型现在的水平做产品，你会失败。"},{"i":5,"s":27.38,"e":31.78,"en":"if you build for where you think the models will be in a year, both outcomes are equally wrong.","zh":"如果你照着你以为一年后模型的水平做产品，也会失败。这两种结果同样错。"},{"i":6,"s":31.86,"e":34.14,"en":"Only way to build is two to three months.","zh":"唯一可行的做法是按两到三个月来做。"},{"i":7,"s":34.14,"e":38.5,"en":"What have you had to most adapt to and adjust in how you operate as a PM in this world?","zh":"在这样的世界里，作为 PM，你最需要适应和调整的是什么？"},{"i":8,"s":38.62,"e":44.1,"en":"Being prolific and empirical is way more important than being academic or theoretical.","zh":"高产且注重实证，远比学术化或理论化更重要。"},{"i":9,"s":44.22,"e":51.54,"en":"Rather than writing out some long reasoning doc, instead it's like how do I get to something I can try out and test with users as fast as possible.","zh":"与其写一份长长的论证文档，不如想办法尽快做出一个能让用户试用和测试的东西。"},{"i":10,"s":51.78,"e":54.82,"en":"It feels like not only are we able to be more ambitious.","zh":"感觉不只是我们能够更有野心。"},{"i":11,"s":55.23,"e":58.43,"en":"We almost need to be more ambitious, which is not natural for a lot of people.","zh":"我们几乎是必须更有野心，而这对很多人来说并不自然。"},{"i":12,"s":58.47,"e":63.71,"en":"Elevating others' ambitions or reminding them of what's possible here is a huge part of the product management role.","zh":"拔高别人的野心，或者提醒他们这里还有多大可能性，是产品管理这个角色很重要的一部分。"},{"i":13,"s":63.71,"e":67.71,"en":"I'm curious what's most surprised you about what it's actually like to work at OpenAI.","zh":"我很好奇，在 OpenAI 工作的真实体验，最让你意外的是什么。"},{"i":14,"s":67.75,"e":87.27,"en":"I came into the company expecting that there was a treasure trove of OpenAI secret strategy and actually OpenAI is open. Today my guest is Tara Seshan. Tara leads product for both Codex and GPT work at OpenAI. I believe this is the fastest growing and arguably most important","zh":"我进公司时以为会有一批 OpenAI 秘密战略的宝藏，但其实 OpenAI 是开放的。今天我的嘉宾是 Tara Seshan。Tara 在 OpenAI 同时负责 Codex 和 ChatGPT for Work 的产品。我认为这是当今增长最快、也可以说最重要的"},{"i":15,"s":87.27,"e":89.19,"en":"AI product for knowledge workers today.","zh":"面向知识工作者的 AI 产品。"},{"i":16,"s":89.57,"e":93.25,"en":"Tara works alongside Andrea Ambrosino, who was a recent podcast guest.","zh":"Tara 与 Andrea Ambrosino 共事，他最近也上过这个播客。"},{"i":17,"s":93.49,"e":94.65,"en":"He's her engineering manager.","zh":"他是她的工程负责人。"},{"i":18,"s":94.77,"e":106.2,"en":"Prior to OpenAI, Tara spent 6 years at Stripe, where she joined as one of the first 5 product managers, and for many of those years, she was named one of the top three Stripes across the entire organization of Stripe.","zh":"来 OpenAI 之前，Tara 在 Stripe 工作了六年，是最早的五名产品经理之一，其中很多年里，她都被评为整个 Stripe 组织中最顶尖的三名产品经理之一。"},{"i":19,"s":106.44,"e":120.36,"en":"She also led product at Watershed, was a founder and a Thiel Fellow, and most importantly of all, Tara was one of the three Lenny's Newsletter Fellows, which is a program that I ran a few years ago to highlight some of the most amazing up and coming product leaders.","zh":"她还在 Watershed 负责产品，做过创始人，是 Thiel Fellow。最重要的是，Tara 是三位 Lenny's Newsletter Fellow 之一——那是我几年前办的一个项目，用来发掘一些最出色的新锐产品领导者。"},{"i":20,"s":120.68,"e":124.76,"en":"I am so excited to see Tara in this new incredibly important and impactful role.","zh":"看到 Tara 出任这个极其重要、极有影响力的新角色，我非常激动。"},{"i":21,"s":125.1,"e":136.42,"en":"Before we get into it, don't forget to check out Lenny's Product Pass dot com for a free year of the hottest and most beautifully crafted AI products in the world, available exclusively to Lenny's newsletter subscribers.","zh":"开始之前，别忘了去 Lenny's Product Pass dot com 领取一年免费的、全世界最火也最精致的 AI 产品，这是 Lenny's Newsletter 订阅者专属福利。"},{"i":22,"s":136.96,"e":138.4,"en":"With that, I bring you Tara Seshan.","zh":"好，下面有请 Tara Seshan。"},{"i":23,"s":141.92,"e":145.32,"en":"Tara, thank you so much for being here, welcome to the podcast.","zh":"Tara，非常感谢你来，欢迎做客播客。"},{"i":24,"s":145.6,"e":146.4,"en":"Thank you, Lenny.","zh":"谢谢你，Lenny。"},{"i":25,"s":146.44,"e":147.68,"en":"I'm so glad to be here.","zh":"我很高兴能来。"},{"i":26,"s":147.68,"e":148.64,"en":"It's so nice to see you.","zh":"见到你真好。"},{"i":27,"s":148.8,"e":149.76,"en":"I'm even more glad.","zh":"我更高兴。"},{"i":28,"s":150.24,"e":156.6,"en":"So, you've been at OpenAI for just about a year now, which in most places would be a very short amount of time.","zh":"你在 OpenAI 差不多刚满一年，这在大多数地方都算很短的时间。"},{"i":29,"s":157.18,"e":158.94,"en":"In AI time, that's like a lifetime.","zh":"但按 AI 的时间尺度，那简直像一辈子。"},{"i":30,"s":159.1,"e":159.5,"en":"Yes.","zh":"是的。"},{"i":31,"s":160.58,"e":166.38,"en":"I imagine when you joined OpenAI, you had a sense of what it was gonna be like to work at a frontier lab.","zh":"我猜你加入 OpenAI 时，对在前沿实验室工作是什么感觉已经有预期。"},{"i":32,"s":166.96,"e":172.92,"en":"I'm curious what's most surprised you about what it's actually like to work at OpenAI, and ideally both good and bad stuff.","zh":"我很好奇，真正在 OpenAI 工作最让你意外的是什么，最好好的坏的都讲讲。"},{"i":33,"s":173.12,"e":181.76,"en":"So many things about working at OpenAI felt familiar to me, cause I had worked at other places that were, you know, high growth, high talent, high intensity.","zh":"在 OpenAI 工作的很多方面对我来说都很熟悉，因为我之前待过的其他地方也是高速增长、人才密度高、强度大的。"},{"i":34,"s":182.45,"e":191.41,"en":"Hyper scaling mode places before, and so some of the things like, oh, my colleagues are so awesome, or the urgency is really high, felt very familiar.","zh":"以前也待过超高速扩张阶段的公司，所以像「同事都太厉害了」或者「紧迫感非常强」这些，我都很熟悉。"},{"i":35,"s":192.27,"e":201.83,"en":"The part to me that actually felt the most surprising is that many companies I've worked for, in fact, all the companies I've worked for in the past have been founder led.","zh":"对我来说最意外的部分是，我过去待过的很多公司，其实是我待过的所有公司，都是创始人主导的。"},{"i":36,"s":202.6,"e":214.68,"en":"And OpenAI is actually founders led, um, which is that everyone inside the company, especially in their area, is in essence kind of a f-, a founder to some extent.","zh":"而 OpenAI 是「众创始人」主导的，也就是说公司里每个人，尤其在自己负责的领域，某种程度上都算是一个创始人。"},{"i":37,"s":214.84,"e":232.72,"en":"The level of like top down direction at OpenAI is extremely limited relative to places I've worked for prior, and so I think when I first got to the company that was both delightful, in that I had come from like a founding journey before.","zh":"相比我之前待过的地方，OpenAI 的自上而下的指令非常有限，所以我刚到公司时，一方面觉得很惬意，因为我之前有过创业经历，"},{"i":38,"s":232.8,"e":238.08,"en":"and I was like, yes, I can continue to feel like the founder of this product area, or this or this uh team.","zh":"我当时想，太好了，我可以继续像这个产品领域或者这个团队的创始人一样去做事。"},{"i":39,"s":238.4,"e":242.16,"en":"And you know the the distance between me and the market is very very thin.","zh":"而且我和市场之间的距离非常非常近。"},{"i":40,"s":242.36,"e":248.61,"en":"You know, and sometimes that the larger company feel insulated from what users want or feel insulated from, like what the market demands.","zh":"你知道，有时候大公司会让你感觉与用户的需求隔离开，或者与市场的要求隔离开。"},{"i":41,"s":248.65,"e":251.29,"en":"But actually, at OpenAI that you do not at all.","zh":"但在 OpenAI，完全不会这样。"},{"i":42,"s":251.37,"e":257.81,"en":"You are doing everything it takes to get product market fit for your product akin to how a founder might.","zh":"你会像创始人那样，为了让产品拿到 product market fit 而不惜一切。"},{"i":43,"s":258.319,"e":272.65,"en":"But the the counter to this is that, or maybe the the the more uh surprising side of this is, I came into the company expecting that there was a treasure trove of like OpenAI secret strategy that I would be able to understand.","zh":"但另一面，或者说更让我意外的一面是，我进公司时以为会有一批 OpenAI 的秘密战略宝藏等着我去理解。"},{"i":44,"s":273.09,"e":279.73,"en":"akin to how you know, past companies you come in and you're like, oh yes, this is like the payments bible, and this is how we think about uh payments and operations.","zh":"就像你进过去那些公司时会想，太好了，这就是支付圣经，这就是我们对支付和运营的思考方式。"},{"i":45,"s":280.32,"e":282.28,"en":"And actually, OpenAI is open.","zh":"而实际上，OpenAI 是开放的。"},{"i":46,"s":282.8,"e":301.69,"en":"Like every sort of thought that exists in terms of this is how the world should look like, or this is how product should be built or this other model should operate very very quickly becomes a part of the public product or a part of like the public messaging. And so that to me.","zh":"比如「世界应该是什么样」「产品应该怎么做」「模型应该怎么运作」这类想法，都会非常非常快地变成公开产品的一部分，或者对外传播的一部分。所以这一点对我来说，"},{"i":47,"s":301.89,"e":309.0,"en":"was incredibly um both positively surprising, and just like a change in my operating mode for sure.","zh":"既是非常正面的意外，也确实改变了我的工作方式。"},{"i":48,"s":309.28,"e":314.48,"en":"Telling us there's not like the secret room with AGI running there with the master plan that has all the answers.","zh":"你是在告诉我们，并不存在一个密室，里面跑着 AGI，藏着一份有全部答案的总体规划。"},{"i":49,"s":314.52,"e":334.61,"en":"Or at least I'm not in that room for sure, but um I I think the the piece that is really inspiring to me is that so much of what OpenAI does immediately becomes something that users can touch and feel in the product, and that cycle is faster than anywhere else I've seen. This episode is brought to.","zh":"至少我肯定不在那个房间里。但我觉得真正让我受鼓舞的是，OpenAI 做的很多事情会立刻变成用户在产品里能摸到、能感受到的东西，这个循环比我见过的任何地方都快。本期节目由"},{"i":50,"s":334.61,"e":338.17,"en":"you by our season's presenting sponsor, WorkOS.","zh":"本季呈现赞助商 WorkOS 提供支持。"},{"i":51,"s":338.25,"e":344.89,"en":"What do OpenAI, Anthropic, Cursor, Replit, Sierra, Clay, and hundreds of other winning companies all have in common?","zh":"OpenAI、Anthropic、Cursor、Replit、Sierra、Clay 以及数百家成功公司有什么共同点？"},{"i":52,"s":345.52,"e":347.16,"en":"They are all powered by WorkOS.","zh":"它们背后都用了 WorkOS。"},{"i":53,"s":347.72,"e":356.76,"en":"If you're building a product for the enterprise, you've felt the pain of integrating single sign on, SAML, RBAC, audit logs, and other features required by large companies.","zh":"如果你在做面向企业的产品，你一定体会过接入单点登录、SAML、RBAC、审计日志以及大公司要求的各种功能有多痛苦。"},{"i":54,"s":357.24,"e":364.2,"en":"WorkOS turns those deal blockers into drop in APIs with a modern developer platform built specifically for B2B SaaS.","zh":"WorkOS 把这些卡住交易的门槛变成即插即用的 API，配上专为 B2B SaaS 打造的现代开发者平台。"},{"i":55,"s":364.47,"e":370.47,"en":"Literally every startup that I'm an investor in that starts to expand up market ends up working with WorkOS.","zh":"我投资的每一家开始向上拓展大客户市场的创业公司，最后都用上了 WorkOS。"},{"i":56,"s":370.79,"e":372.35,"en":"And that's because they are the best.","zh":"原因就是他们最好。"},{"i":57,"s":372.51,"e":377.99,"en":"Whether you are a seed stage startup trying to land your first enterprise customer, or a unicorn expanding globally.","zh":"无论你是想拿下第一个企业客户的种子轮创业公司，还是正在全球扩张的独角兽，"},{"i":58,"s":378.44,"e":382.6,"en":"WorkOS is the fastest path to becoming enterprise ready and unblocking growth.","zh":"WorkOS 都是最快达到企业级就绪、打开增长瓶颈的路径。"},{"i":59,"s":383.0,"e":385.16,"en":"It's essentially Stripe for enterprise features.","zh":"它本质上就是企业级功能领域的 Stripe。"},{"i":60,"s":385.6,"e":391.88,"en":"Visit WorkOS dot com to get started, or just hit up their Slack where they have actual engineers waiting to answer your questions.","zh":"访问 WorkOS dot com 开始使用，或者直接去他们的 Slack，那里有真的工程师等着回答你的问题。"},{"i":61,"s":392.46,"e":398.18,"en":"WorkOS allows you to build faster with delightful APIs, comprehensive docs, and a smooth developer experience.","zh":"WorkOS 让你用好用的 API、完善的文档和顺畅的开发体验更快地构建产品。"},{"i":62,"s":398.74,"e":402.14,"en":"Go to workos dot com to make your app enterprise ready today.","zh":"现在就去 workos dot com，让你的应用达到企业级就绪。"},{"i":63,"s":403.05,"e":406.69,"en":"You've been a PM at a lot of different places, so a long long time PM leader.","zh":"你在很多地方做过 PM，是资历很深的 PM 负责人。"},{"i":64,"s":406.93,"e":408.93,"en":"What do you lose in this new world?","zh":"在这个新世界里，你失去了什么？"},{"i":65,"s":409.05,"e":420.9,"en":"When a market is more static or a market is more slow moving, you have the chance to actually like do some grand strategy-esque work, because it's more predictable, or you can at least like understand all the pieces.","zh":"当市场更静态、变化更慢时，你有机会真正去做一些宏大战略性的工作，因为它更可预测，或者至少你能理解所有的组成部分。"},{"i":66,"s":421.26,"e":431.67,"en":"Like, as an example, payments is a certainly a dynamic market to some extent, it's also an established market, and you're able to say Oh, yes, if like I take this bet, my competitor might take this other bet.","zh":"举个例子，支付在某种程度上确实是个动态市场，但它也是个成熟市场，你可以说：如果我押这个赌注，我的竞争对手可能会押另一个赌注。"},{"i":67,"s":431.83,"e":437.07,"en":"or reason from first principles very rigorously through what all the next actions might be.","zh":"或者非常严谨地从第一性原理推演出接下来所有可能的动作。"},{"i":68,"s":437.15,"e":445.81,"en":"And in fact, um, the nature of that market mandates that you do that, like winners will think more rigorously than everybody else.","zh":"而且那个市场的性质要求你必须这么做，赢家就是比所有人想得更严谨。"},{"i":69,"s":445.81,"e":452.53,"en":"And if you aren't thinking rigorously, it shows up as sort of like carelessness, cause a lot of those decisions that you made could have been predicted.","zh":"如果你想得不够严谨，表现出来就像是粗心，因为你做的很多决策本来是可以预判的。"},{"i":70,"s":453.08,"e":460.88,"en":"But in this market, it's so hard to understand, like, what is going to emerge in the in the future.","zh":"但在这个市场里，太难判断未来会涌现出什么。"},{"i":71,"s":461.0,"e":468.1,"en":"It's very emergent, it's very fast changing, it's really dynamic, and most importantly, it's like very very important, stay tied to the research.","zh":"它高度涌现、变化极快、非常动态，而最重要的是，必须紧贴研究进展。"},{"i":72,"s":468.26,"e":479.26,"en":"And so, actually being prolific and being um more like empirical is way more important than being um like maybe more academic or theoretical.","zh":"所以，高产、注重实证，远比偏学术、偏理论重要得多。"},{"i":73,"s":480.02,"e":492.64,"en":"And I think lots of the past companies I've worked at have been very academic and theoretical places, and it was a real switch to go from, rather than writing out some like long reasoning doc.","zh":"我过去待过的很多公司都非常学术、非常理论化，所以这是一个真实的转变——不再是写一份长长的论证文档，"},{"i":74,"s":492.68,"e":497.72,"en":"almost like a PhD thesis of what I think should be the plan for the next like N amount of time.","zh":"那几乎像一篇博士论文，论证接下来一段时间的计划应该是什么。"},{"i":75,"s":498.0,"e":502.6,"en":"Instead, it's like, how do I get to something I can try out and test with users as fast as possible?","zh":"而是变成：我怎么能尽快做出一个可以让用户试用和测试的东西？"},{"i":76,"s":503.16,"e":507.28,"en":"And so, yeah, that that switch from theoretical to empirical felt very jarring at first.","zh":"所以，从理论到实证的这个转变，一开始让我很不适应。"},{"i":77,"s":507.4,"e":510.52,"en":"I was like, oh, am I not doing my due diligence here?","zh":"我会想，我是不是没做足功课？"},{"i":78,"s":510.6,"e":512.12,"en":"Am I not being thoughtful enough?","zh":"我是不是不够深思熟虑？"},{"i":79,"s":512.16,"e":514.64,"en":"Like, shouldn't I be like thinking through all of this?","zh":"我难道不该把这些都想清楚吗？"},{"i":80,"s":515.19,"e":519.15,"en":"In a ton of rigor, but actually, you gotta you gotta try stuff and learn as much as possible.","zh":"以极高的严谨度去想，但实际上，你得去试，尽可能多地去学。"},{"i":81,"s":519.75,"e":526.15,"en":"And what that means is the thinking you need to do is being as pointed as possible about what your core hypothesis is.","zh":"这意味着你需要做的思考，是尽可能精准地界定你的核心假设是什么。"},{"i":82,"s":526.49,"e":535.09,"en":"And that hypothesis definition is the most important thing, like what is actually uh to use the um Shishir Mehrotra phra- phrase like the eigenquestion.","zh":"而假设的定义是最重要的事，也就是——用 Shishir Mehrotra 的说法——那个「特征值问题」。"},{"i":83,"s":535.85,"e":542.85,"en":"What is like that specific most important thing to test, and everything else like any other grand strategy you concoct is not relevant.","zh":"那个最重要、最该被验证的具体问题是什么，其他的东西，你能编出来的任何宏大战略，都不相关。"},{"i":84,"s":543.22,"e":545.18,"en":"I'd love to hear more about that, cause that's really interesting.","zh":"我想多听听这个，因为这真的很有意思。"},{"i":85,"s":545.98,"e":549.22,"en":"It's almost like, here's the thing of the PM role that is not changing.","zh":"这几乎是在说，PM 这个角色里有一部分是不变的。"},{"i":86,"s":549.5,"e":554.14,"en":"So much is changing, the world is changing, but like there's still this piece that is even more important.","zh":"变的东西太多了，世界在变，但仍然有这么一块，而且变得更重要了。"},{"i":87,"s":554.54,"e":559.26,"en":"Speak more to that of wha- what specifically that uh you think people need to focus more on?","zh":"能不能再展开讲讲，你觉得大家具体该更聚焦在什么上？"},{"i":88,"s":559.38,"e":568.98,"en":"Yeah, there were so, there's so many trappings around the PM role of like, you know, running um like execution on time, and and writing all these specific docs and presentations, et cetera.","zh":"是的，PM 这个角色周围有太多花架子，比如按时推进执行、写各种具体的文档和演示材料等等。"},{"i":89,"s":569.32,"e":574.48,"en":"But the core of it has always been about what is like the most essential question you need to ask about your product.","zh":"但它的核心一直都是：关于你的产品，你需要问的那个最本质的问题是什么。"},{"i":90,"s":574.48,"e":578.8,"en":"Like what is the thing that will determine whether your product works or doesn't work?","zh":"决定你的产品成或不成的，究竟是什么？"},{"i":91,"s":579.32,"e":580.4,"en":"How do you test that?","zh":"你怎么去验证它？"},{"i":92,"s":580.44,"e":586.76,"en":"How do you look at the results, and how do you feed that back into a loop of like refining your hypothesis and running it again?","zh":"你怎么看结果，又怎么把结果反馈回一个循环里，去打磨你的假设，然后再跑一遍？"},{"i":93,"s":586.84,"e":589.56,"en":"Like that that truly has always been the PM job.","zh":"这才真正一直是 PM 的工作。"},{"i":94,"s":590.07,"e":595.59,"en":"um, and that involves of course, like trying to understand users, trying to understand the market, trying to understand the actual technology you're building.","zh":"这当然包括努力理解用户、理解市场、理解你正在构建的技术本身。"},{"i":95,"s":595.79,"e":601.07,"en":"Pulling those three things together to make the most sharp hypothesis you can.","zh":"把这三件事聚到一起，形成尽可能锋利的假设。"},{"i":96,"s":601.63,"e":605.43,"en":"And then, making the test as fast and effective as possible.","zh":"然后，让验证尽可能快、尽可能有效。"},{"i":97,"s":605.99,"e":612.11,"en":"And I think that is not only not changed, but it's become the most important thing.","zh":"我认为这一点不但没有改变，反而成了最重要的事。"},{"i":98,"s":613.21,"e":628.01,"en":"uh, the company to be able to do, like, EMs are like thinking this way, engineers are thinking this way, like data scientists are thinking this way, designers are thinking this way, like everyone has sort of moved to focus their efforts on this really really important like problem.","zh":"整个公司都要能这样做——工程经理这样思考，工程师这样思考，数据科学家这样思考，设计师也这样思考，所有人都把精力转向了这个非常非常重要的问题"},{"i":99,"s":628.33,"e":630.05,"en":"definition and and testing loop.","zh":"定义和验证循环。"},{"i":100,"s":630.05,"e":633.25,"en":"Like, what are we actually doing, and how do we know if it's working thing?","zh":"也就是：我们到底在做什么，我们怎么知道它是否有效？"},{"i":101,"s":633.53,"e":640.02,"en":"And from a PM standpoint, like it's great, because PMs have always ha been really focused on trying to get that stuff right.","zh":"从 PM 的角度看，这很棒，因为 PM 一直都特别专注于把这些事情做对。"},{"i":102,"s":640.38,"e":650.18,"en":"um, that has always been the core of the job, and actually, many of the other just trappings of the job have like fallen away, and that remains like the key thing to get right every time.","zh":"这一直是这份工作的核心，而实际上，工作中其他很多花架子都消失了，剩下的就是每次都必须做对的那个关键点。"},{"i":103,"s":650.66,"e":663.71,"en":"You mentioned this idea of a loop, and there's a lot of talk these days like loops were so hot, I don't know a few weeks ago on Twitter, and it feels like it continues to be a topic of discussion for knowledge work broadly.","zh":"你提到「循环」这个概念，最近关于循环的讨论特别多，大概几周前在 Twitter 上非常火，而且感觉它还在持续成为整个知识工作领域的一个话题。"},{"i":104,"s":664.23,"e":672.43,"en":"and the way I understand a loop essentially, AI, here's what success looks like, go off and build and figure it out, until you this is what this you achieve success.","zh":"我理解的循环大致是：告诉 AI 成功长什么样，让它自己去构建、去摸索，直到达成成功。"},{"i":105,"s":673.58,"e":680.94,"en":"How do you think about just this idea of loops expanding from just software engineering to product management to all knowledge work.","zh":"你怎么看这种循环从软件工程扩展到产品管理，再扩展到所有知识工作？"},{"i":106,"s":681.02,"e":682.34,"en":"Do you think that's gonna be a a thing?","zh":"你觉得这会成真吗？"},{"i":107,"s":682.66,"e":688.14,"en":"I do think that increasingly the future of work will look more like steering than rowing.","zh":"我确实认为，未来的工作会越来越像掌舵，而不是划桨。"},{"i":108,"s":688.83,"e":700.03,"en":"In the sense that there will be agents that you'll you'll be able to work with that do a lot of the rowing, and your role increasingly becomes steering the ship in the right direction and pointing it in the right direction.","zh":"也就是说，会有一些 agent 可以和你协作，替你完成大量划桨的活儿，而你的角色越来越变成把船导向正确的方向、指出正确的方向。"},{"i":109,"s":700.62,"e":705.82,"en":"And to that point, I think that that steering might grow higher and higher and higher level.","zh":"说到这里，我觉得掌舵的层级可能会越来越高。"},{"i":110,"s":706.06,"e":710.02,"en":"The steering used to be at the level of, I wrote this line of code, press Tab.","zh":"以前的掌舵是这种层级：我写了这一行代码，按 Tab。"},{"i":111,"s":710.14,"e":715.54,"en":"To, oh wait, now I'm directing something a little bit more comprehensive to maybe the goal level.","zh":"然后变成，等等，现在我在指挥一件更完整的事，可能到了目标的层级。"},{"i":112,"s":716.02,"e":721.9,"en":"Maybe to an even higher level, I think the steering will continue to um maybe go up layers of abstraction.","zh":"甚至更高的层级，我觉得掌舵会继续往上走抽象层次。"},{"i":113,"s":722.18,"e":729.86,"en":"But ultimately, I think it's still on a person to be able to find like which direction are we pointing this in, and given feedback and additional data.","zh":"但归根结底，我认为还是要靠人来判断：我们要把它指向哪个方向，以及在拿到反馈和更多数据之后，"},{"i":114,"s":730.32,"e":732.4,"en":"Where do I want to take this thing next?","zh":"我接下来想把这件事带向哪里？"},{"i":115,"s":732.6,"e":740.4,"en":"Some of steering, I think is about certainly like what the data tells you, but a lot of it is about making a opinionated call.","zh":"掌舵有一部分当然取决于数据告诉你什么，但很大一部分是做出一个有主张的判断。"},{"i":116,"s":740.98,"e":751.82,"en":"I think sometimes that we underrate like that power of like intuition, or even um sort of like positive like determinism of what we want the future to be like.","zh":"我觉得有时候我们低估了直觉的力量，甚至是那种对我们希望未来变成什么样的、积极的笃定。"},{"i":117,"s":752.15,"e":762.83,"en":"Like picturing, hey, I would like the product to look this way, not because the converse is not an equally viable strategy, but because I would like the world to look like the direction that I would I'm pushing it in.","zh":"比如去描绘：嘿，我希望产品是这个样子，不是因为反方向不是同样可行的策略，而是因为我希望世界变成我正在推动的那个方向。"},{"i":118,"s":763.16,"e":769.59,"en":"And that I think will always remain a, uh, opinion at least right now that is like required from a person.","zh":"而我认为这一点会一直是——至少现在是——必须由人来给出的判断。"},{"i":119,"s":769.79,"e":783.96,"en":"And so, I think that loops are awesome, running like running agents, and increasingly increasingly larger loops where they're doing more and more of that rowing for you is great, but right now, like, you really still need to to steer.","zh":"所以我觉得循环很棒，让 agent 跑起来，而且循环越来越大，它们替你划的桨越来越多，这很好，但现在你确实还是得掌舵。"},{"i":120,"s":784.52,"e":792.2,"en":"And I think work will also look like steering with other people over a group of agents that you guys work with together.","zh":"我还觉得，未来的工作会变成：你和其他人一起，共同为一群你们协作使用的 agent 掌舵。"},{"i":121,"s":792.96,"e":800.28,"en":"um, bringing in other teammates into that, like interaction between you and the agent where it's rowing and you're steering, feels also incredibly valuable.","zh":"把其他队友带进你和 agent 的这种互动里——它划桨、你掌舵——感觉也极有价值。"},{"i":122,"s":800.73,"e":802.37,"en":"That's such an interesting way of describing it.","zh":"这个说法太有意思了。"},{"i":123,"s":803.17,"e":805.57,"en":"There's also, like, there's two thoughts here that come up.","zh":"这里我也冒出两个想法。"},{"i":124,"s":805.61,"e":813.24,"en":"One is, if everybody has access to the same tools, the thing that will separate you is this as the hu- as human, the person basically.","zh":"一是，如果所有人都能用上同样的工具，那把你区分开来的就是人本身。"},{"i":125,"s":813.4,"e":821.96,"en":"Otherwise, we're all just gonna be building the same thing, and you could use it, you could, everyone could be asking how do we win, what do we do, and then the thing that almost the unfair advantage almost is the human brain.","zh":"否则我们做出来的东西都一样，谁都能用，谁都在问怎么才能赢、该做什么，而那种近乎不公平的优势，几乎就是人的大脑。"},{"i":126,"s":822.04,"e":825.28,"en":"Yeah, I I think it it runs through a lot of fashion actually, in in some ways.","zh":"是的，我觉得这在某些方面跟时尚是相通的。"},{"i":127,"s":825.73,"e":831.77,"en":"Like, there are certainly functional clothes that everybody can wear, and uh gets gets the job done.","zh":"确实有些功能性的衣服，人人都能穿，也够用了。"},{"i":128,"s":831.97,"e":841.49,"en":"But so much about what you wear, at least, or how I think about what I wear, is about what statement I want to make about my individuality, or what, how I wanna reflect to the rest of the world.","zh":"但你穿什么——至少我在想自己穿什么的时候——很大程度上是关于我想为我的个性表达什么，或者我想向外界呈现什么。"},{"i":129,"s":841.85,"e":845.69,"en":"and a lot of what makes that compelling is how it contrasts with other people's expression.","zh":"而其中很多吸引力，来自它和别人的表达形成的对比。"},{"i":130,"s":845.97,"e":857.17,"en":"Like, the shirt I make makes a statement only because it is maybe different than whatever else is doing or different than some cohort of people are doing, or make statement about my group membership or something of that kind.","zh":"比如我这件衬衫之所以能表达什么，是因为它可能跟别人穿的不一样，或者跟某一群人不一样，又或者它在表明我属于某个群体之类。"},{"i":131,"s":857.69,"e":863.13,"en":"I think a lot of the products that we build feel similarly opinionated and artistic.","zh":"我觉得我们做的很多产品，同样带着这种主张和艺术性。"},{"i":132,"s":863.45,"e":870.41,"en":"Like Patrick Collison has this really nice statement, or maybe it's John Collison has this really nice statement about software, which is that software is not like real estate.","zh":"Patrick Collison 有一句很妙的话，也可能是 John Collison 说的，关于软件的：软件不像房地产。"},{"i":133,"s":870.53,"e":872.89,"en":"You don't like put money in and get value out.","zh":"不是你投钱进去就能拿到价值。"},{"i":134,"s":873.09,"e":874.61,"en":"It is a little bit more like filmmaking.","zh":"它更像拍电影。"},{"i":135,"s":875.27,"e":880.83,"en":"Where you can put a lot of money into a film, but that doesn't guarantee that the film is successful or good.","zh":"你可以往一部电影里砸很多钱，但那并不保证这部电影成功或者好。"},{"i":136,"s":881.07,"e":885.03,"en":"There is some like auteur statement, there is some opinionation in artistry.","zh":"这里面有一种作者式的表达，有一种带着主张的艺术性。"},{"i":137,"s":885.53,"e":893.45,"en":"That goes along with it, and I think that relies on you having something interesting to say, or your team having something interesting to say about your product.","zh":"它跟这件事是相伴而来的，而这依赖于你、或者你的团队，对你的产品有一些有意思的东西可说。"},{"i":138,"s":893.77,"e":896.45,"en":"There's something um Marty Cagan is big on.","zh":"Marty Cagan 特别强调过一点。"},{"i":139,"s":896.76,"e":903.97,"en":"Which is this idea that when you have an idea for a product or feature, rarely is that idea the thing that ends up being.","zh":"就是当你对一个产品或功能有了想法时，那个想法很少就是最终成型的东西。"},{"i":140,"s":904.13,"e":908.33,"en":"There's this whole process you go through to kind of figure out what the hell actually it should be.","zh":"你得走完一整个过程，才能搞清楚它到底该是什么样。"},{"i":141,"s":909.13,"e":915.33,"en":"And it feels like that's kind of what you're saying here, is like you need to go through that process as a human to understand what it really is and what people actually want.","zh":"感觉你说的就是这个意思：你得作为人走完这个过程，才能明白它究竟是什么、人们真正想要什么。"},{"i":142,"s":915.61,"e":919.05,"en":"It's never gonna be like, okay, got it, go build this thing, I got it from the beginning.","zh":"绝不可能是「好，明白了，去把这个东西做出来吧」，一开始就想清楚了。"},{"i":143,"s":919.58,"e":920.9,"en":"Yeah, for sure, for sure.","zh":"是的，确实如此，确实如此。"},{"i":144,"s":921.02,"e":924.02,"en":"And that loop, those loops are moving faster and faster and faster.","zh":"而且那些循环转得越来越快、越来越快。"},{"i":145,"s":924.18,"e":935.71,"en":"And so, your ability to like form those intuitions, get the information you need to form those intuitions, and then use that with people and agents to put that into action is is the key.","zh":"所以你形成这些直觉的能力、拿到形成直觉所需信息的能力，再带着人和 agent 把它落地的能力，才是关键。"},{"i":146,"s":935.91,"e":940.91,"en":"I'm curious what you think the next shift will be in how we work just broadly as knowledge workers.","zh":"我很好奇，你觉得我们这些知识工作者的工作方式，下一个大转变会是什么。"},{"i":147,"s":941.67,"e":947.07,"en":"It feels like not only do you have access to the most advanced tools that'll, some people, that other people don't get.","zh":"感觉你们不仅能用上最先进的、别人还用不到的工具。"},{"i":148,"s":947.43,"e":952.11,"en":"Also, you work around the most AI-pilled, AI forward people in the world.","zh":"而且你身边都是世界上最信 AI、最激进拥抱 AI 的一群人。"},{"i":149,"s":952.86,"e":961.62,"en":"How are people working internally that you think will become kind of a more normal way we all work using these AI tools in the next, I don't know, 3~6 months?","zh":"你们内部现在的哪些工作方式，你觉得会在接下来——姑且说三到六个月吧——变成我们所有人用这些 AI 工具的常态？"},{"i":150,"s":961.98,"e":964.3,"en":"Yeah, I think there's there's two aspects to this.","zh":"我觉得这里有两个方面。"},{"i":151,"s":964.82,"e":977.12,"en":"One is continuing to work with agents at higher and higher levels of abstraction, so letting the agents do more and more for you independently, coming in providing that steering.","zh":"一是继续在越来越高的抽象层级上跟 agent 协作，让 agent 越来越多地独立替你做事，你进来给出掌舵的方向。"},{"i":152,"s":977.66,"e":979.9,"en":"And then letting the agent continue to cook.","zh":"然后让 agent 接着去发挥。"},{"i":153,"s":980.18,"e":991.54,"en":"Like, let the agent cook and provide details at higher or of orders of abstraction feels like the way people are increasingly thinking about agents that are persistent, that feel like teammates, that feel like coworkers.","zh":"让 agent 自己去做，你在更高的抽象层级上提供细节——大家越来越是这样看待那种持续在线、像队友、像同事的 agent 的。"},{"i":154,"s":992.17,"e":1001.85,"en":"Where you can work with them the way I might work with someone on my team, which is they do a whole bunch of work, I provide input, and then they do work again, and we sync up at different cadences.","zh":"你可以像跟团队里的同事那样跟它们协作：他们做一大堆工作，我给出输入，他们再接着做，我们按不同的节奏同步。"},{"i":155,"s":1002.09,"e":1005.76,"en":"look at each other's in progress work, and provide more and more feedback.","zh":"看彼此进行中的工作，给出越来越多的反馈。"},{"i":156,"s":1005.84,"e":1011.2,"en":"It feels like that that coworker model is the way that things are certainly going.","zh":"感觉这种「同事模式」确实是事情正在走的方向。"},{"i":157,"s":1011.2,"e":1017.6,"en":"Feels like a much more natural interface for us to be able to work with agents, so we already see a lot of that internally as well.","zh":"它像是我们跟 agent 协作更自然得多的界面，所以我们内部也已经大量看到这种做法。"},{"i":158,"s":1018.35,"e":1024.75,"en":"The second is that a lot of my work with agents thus far has been one on one.","zh":"第二点是，我到目前为止和 agent 的协作大多是一对一的。"},{"i":159,"s":1025.59,"e":1030.83,"en":"That I work with my agent, maybe it spawns some sub agents to get some task done, but it's me and my agent together.","zh":"我和我的 agent 一起干活，它也许会派生一些子 agent 去完成某些任务，但本质上是我和我的 agent 两个人。"},{"i":160,"s":1031.39,"e":1035.67,"en":"And that is potentially divorced from what my colleagues are doing with their agents.","zh":"而这可能跟我的同事们在用他们的 agent 做的事完全脱节。"},{"i":161,"s":1036.23,"e":1044.19,"en":"And so, there was a time where everyone internally was just like sending their Codex threads, screenshots of their Codex threads to each other.","zh":"所以有一阵子，内部所有人都在互相发自己的 Codex 会话、Codex 会话的截图。"},{"i":162,"s":1044.68,"e":1048.52,"en":"On Slack, we're like, OK, well, I wanted to share with you how I got to this number.","zh":"在 Slack 上，就像「好，我想让你看看我是怎么得出这个数字的」。"},{"i":163,"s":1048.64,"e":1049.68,"en":"Here's how I got to this number.","zh":"「这就是我得出这个数字的过程。」"},{"i":164,"s":1049.76,"e":1051.48,"en":"Here's a screenshot of of what I did.","zh":"「这是我具体做了什么的截图。」"},{"i":165,"s":1051.6,"e":1064.61,"en":"But that's also not quite the most natural way for someone to collaborate together, and so as more and more work gets done with our agents, shouldn't we be able to get work done with our agents together?","zh":"但这也不算是人们协作最自然的方式，所以随着越来越多的工作是靠 agent 完成的，我们难道不应该能够带着各自的 agent 一起协作吗？"},{"i":166,"s":1065.37,"e":1068.05,"en":"um, and what is the most natural interface to make that happen?","zh":"那么，让这件事发生的最自然的界面是什么？"},{"i":167,"s":1068.05,"e":1070.39,"en":"And those are some of the things that we're we're thinking about.","zh":"这些就是我们正在思考的一些问题。"},{"i":168,"s":1070.67,"e":1072.03,"en":"Chat is what I'm picturing.","zh":"我脑子里浮现的就是 chat。"},{"i":169,"s":1072.39,"e":1073.39,"en":"uh, that makes so much sense.","zh":"这太有道理了。"},{"i":170,"s":1073.47,"e":1081.15,"en":"It's like, okay, here's Tara's agent, here's my agent, she did some work on some analysis, I'd be, hey, my agent, Lenny's agent, go check, make sure this is legit.","zh":"就像：好，这是 Tara 的 agent，这是我的 agent，她做了些分析，我就说，嘿，我的 agent、Lenny 的 agent，去查一查，确认这个靠谱。"},{"i":171,"s":1081.7,"e":1083.3,"en":"And connects to the way I think about the world.","zh":"这也跟我看待世界的方式对得上。"},{"i":172,"s":1083.42,"e":1092.02,"en":"Ideally, work feels like a multiplayer game where all of us together are getting stuff done, steering our agents, as our agents continue to take care of more and more.","zh":"理想情况下，工作会像一场多人游戏，我们所有人一起把事情做成，为各自的 agent 掌舵，而 agent 继续承担越来越多——"},{"i":173,"s":1092.45,"e":1094.33,"en":"Of those like rowing tactical tasks.","zh":"——那些划桨式的战术性任务。"},{"i":174,"s":1094.53,"e":1104.49,"en":"It's interesting how it's just been this like slow progression of trust, and um just like awareness that this can be how we work, just this like, okay, go work for longer.","zh":"有意思的是，这一路就是信任在慢慢推进，还有那种逐渐生出的意识：原来我们可以这样工作，就是那种「好，你多干一会儿」。"},{"i":175,"s":1104.97,"e":1107.09,"en":"You can take on more, it's just like you feel.","zh":"「你可以多担一点」，就是那种感觉。"},{"i":176,"s":1107.45,"e":1110.53,"en":"There's been this talk of like the slow takeoff, the fast takeoff scenarios.","zh":"一直有人在谈慢起飞、快起飞这两种情形。"},{"i":177,"s":1110.57,"e":1114.97,"en":"And everyone was afraid of this fast AI takeoff, where it's like, way too smart, and we're in big trouble.","zh":"大家都害怕 AI 快速起飞，那种它聪明得离谱、我们就麻烦大了的情形。"},{"i":178,"s":1115.59,"e":1120.55,"en":"Feels very much like we're on a slow takeoff scenario, which is good, where it's just like slowly iterating.","zh":"感觉我们现在很像是走在慢起飞的路上，这是好事，就是慢慢迭代。"},{"i":179,"s":1120.83,"e":1127.07,"en":"Doesn't feel that slow, but in a sense, you know, we're not like to some 300 IQ a AI, like you know.","zh":"虽然也没觉得有多慢，但某种意义上，我们还没到那种 300 智商的 AI。"},{"i":180,"s":1127.56,"e":1137.96,"en":"I mean the models are the models are incredibly smart, but I think a lot of the things that have enabled us to then work with our agents together, or have the agents take care of higher and higher order abstraction things.","zh":"我是说模型确实聪明得惊人，但我觉得，让我们能带着 agent 一起协作、或者让 agent 处理越来越高抽象层级事情的很多因素——"},{"i":181,"s":1138.58,"e":1143.18,"en":"Certainly are about the intelligence, their ability to perform long running tasks, and how long they can stay on tasks.","zh":"——当然跟智能有关，跟它们执行长时间任务的能力、能在任务上坚持多久有关。"},{"i":182,"s":1143.5,"e":1154.03,"en":"But also actually, they're very meat and potatoes, tangible things that make this possible, like agents working locally are really convenient, cause they have access to all the data that's on your machine.","zh":"但其实也有很多很实在、很具体的东西让这一切成为可能，比如 agent 在本地运行就非常方便，因为它能访问你机器上的所有数据。"},{"i":183,"s":1154.31,"e":1159.55,"en":"To make an agent successful in the cloud, there is a ton of cloud infrastructure that you have to build to make that possible.","zh":"而要让一个 agent 在云端也能成功，你得建一大堆云基础设施才行。"},{"i":184,"s":1159.79,"e":1165.27,"en":"And just like access to your systems, like how can agents talk to all these third party systems that have all of your data?","zh":"还有对你各种系统的访问权限，agent 怎么跟那些装着你全部数据的第三方系统打交道？"},{"i":185,"s":1165.68,"e":1174.28,"en":"Just like a colleague who you hire, who you like lock into a room, never give them access to like Google Docs and Slack, and you know, the company database would not be that useful to you.","zh":"就像你雇了一位同事，把他锁在一个房间里，从不给他 Google Docs、Slack、公司数据库的权限，那他对你也没多大用。"},{"i":186,"s":1174.28,"e":1186.95,"en":"Similarly, like a cloud agent that is similarly isolated will will not be that effective, and so a huge part of making these agents useful and achieving some of these futures are are on the intelligence side, certainly.","zh":"同样，一个被这样隔离的云端 agent 也不会多有效，所以要让这些 agent 真正有用、实现这些未来图景，很大一部分当然在智能这一侧。"},{"i":187,"s":1186.95,"e":1189.79,"en":"But a lot of it is also just really tactical.","zh":"但也有很多其实非常琐碎实际。"},{"i":188,"s":1190.46,"e":1205.26,"en":"Like data access, like cloud infrastructure and reliability pieces that feel um yeah, they feel much more prosaic than some of the the the broader intelligence questions, but matter in some ways just as much for that effectiveness.","zh":"比如数据访问、云基础设施和可靠性这些部分，它们听起来比那些宏大的智能问题平淡得多，但在某种意义上，对效果同样重要。"},{"i":189,"s":1205.84,"e":1208.76,"en":"This touches on something else that has been coming up a bunch on this podcast.","zh":"这就说到了这档播客里反复冒出来的另一件事。"},{"i":190,"s":1208.88,"e":1209.76,"en":"This word ambition.","zh":"「雄心」这个词。"},{"i":191,"s":1211.15,"e":1212.71,"en":"I know you think a lot about this too.","zh":"我知道你也常常在想这个。"},{"i":192,"s":1213.87,"e":1223.03,"en":"It feels like not only are we able to be more ambitious because of these AI tools, we almost need to be more ambitious, which is not natural for a lot of people.","zh":"感觉我们不仅因为这些 AI 工具而能够更有雄心，我们几乎是必须更有雄心，而这对很多人来说并不自然。"},{"i":193,"s":1223.49,"e":1226.85,"en":"Because everybody can now do all these easy things really easily.","zh":"因为现在人人都能非常轻松地搞定那些简单的事。"},{"i":194,"s":1226.85,"e":1229.89,"en":"Like, the easy stuff is super easy, the hard stuff is easy.","zh":"简单的事变得超级简单，难的事变得简单。"},{"i":195,"s":1230.33,"e":1235.29,"en":"And the thing that separates people now and companies now is just how ambitious they can be.","zh":"现在把人和人、公司和公司区分开的，就是他们能有多大的雄心。"},{"i":196,"s":1236.14,"e":1241.3,"en":"Talk about what comes up when I talk about the the need and the kind of the emergence of this need for ambition.","zh":"说说当我谈到这种对雄心的需要、这种需求的浮现时，你会想到什么。"},{"i":197,"s":1241.7,"e":1251.94,"en":"Yeah, I think the people that we see who are most effective at using AI tools don't simply use it to automate rote tasks, but use it to expand the set of things that they are capable of doing.","zh":"是的，我觉得我们看到那些用 AI 工具最有成效的人，不只是拿它来自动化机械的活儿，而是用它来扩展自己能做的事情的范围。"},{"i":198,"s":1252.37,"e":1261.93,"en":"Like back in the day, you know, before before all this uh before all this AI stuff, the unicorn person was someone who is a really thoughtful product sense.","zh":"比如以前，在这些 AI 东西出现之前，那种独角兽式的人，是产品感非常好的人。"},{"i":199,"s":1262.76,"e":1266.52,"en":"Person who also happen to be an engineer, who may also have been a designer.","zh":"而且他碰巧还是个工程师，可能还当过设计师。"},{"i":200,"s":1266.6,"e":1279.64,"en":"That person was always the like unicorn hire, because they were able to really flatten the layers of translation needed between all these functions, and were able to like build something or ideate something really quickly and easily.","zh":"那种人永远是独角兽、是最抢手的招聘对象，因为他们能把各职能之间的翻译层大幅压平，能非常快、非常轻松地做出或者构思出一些东西。"},{"i":201,"s":1280.38,"e":1285.74,"en":"Themselves, and get it up and running, and then were able to like work with a team and collaborate with a team on it.","zh":"自己就能做出来、跑起来，然后还能跟团队一起协作把它推进下去。"},{"i":202,"s":1286.02,"e":1296.93,"en":"And I think the most compelling thing I found that certainly I try to be able to do with these tools, and I've seen to my like most successful like colleagues be able to do these tools.","zh":"而我发现最让人心动的一点——我自己一直想用这些工具做到，也在我那些最出色的同事身上看到——"},{"i":203,"s":1297.33,"e":1302.33,"en":"is really expand the set of things that are quote unquote within their range of possibilities.","zh":"——就是真正扩展了所谓「在他们可能性范围之内」的那一堆事情。"},{"i":204,"s":1302.91,"e":1311.99,"en":"So that they can start realizing more and more of what's in their head into the reality, the way that someone who was previously like Jack of all trades was able to do.","zh":"这样他们就能把脑子里越来越多的东西变成现实，就像以前那些「多面手」能做到的那样。"},{"i":205,"s":1312.31,"e":1318.79,"en":"We kind of all have that superpower now, that I can like spin up a set of designs on something, and I can like go build an initial prototype of it.","zh":"现在我们某种程度上都有了这种超能力：我可以就某个东西快速出一套设计，也可以去做出它的初版原型。"},{"i":206,"s":1319.1,"e":1323.62,"en":"And I can, you know, figure out the right pricing model for it, and model out all the scenarios.","zh":"我还能搞清楚合适的定价模型，把各种情形都建模一遍。"},{"i":207,"s":1323.62,"e":1327.18,"en":"Like, really the set of possibilities have widened dramatically.","zh":"可能性的范围真的大幅拓宽了。"},{"i":208,"s":1327.7,"e":1337.14,"en":"And actually, what that means in so many ways is that I have the ability to like be a to that point earlier about film, like be more of an auteur, as I try to get something done.","zh":"而这在很多方面意味着，我有能力——回到刚才电影那个说法——在做事的时候更像一个作者型导演。"},{"i":209,"s":1337.5,"e":1340.06,"en":"and like realize my vision maybe to higher fidelity.","zh":"并且能把我的愿景实现到更高的还原度。"},{"i":210,"s":1340.54,"e":1358.52,"en":"And that to me is part of what can elevate your ambitions while pursuing new ideas and new products, that because all of these things are now within reach, because this new set of capabilities is now within your reach to be able to try and access. You're not really limited, your ambitions are no longer.","zh":"对我来说，这正是能抬高你雄心的一部分原因——在追求新想法和新产品时，因为这些事情现在都触手可及，因为这一整套新能力现在都在你伸手可及的范围内，你并没有真正被限制住，你的雄心不再——"},{"i":211,"s":1358.72,"e":1363.44,"en":"limited by like what you're capable of executing yourself, what you're capable of communicating.","zh":"——被你自己能执行什么、能沟通什么所限制。"},{"i":212,"s":1364.29,"e":1365.97,"en":"It can be so much so much wider.","zh":"它可以宽广得多得多。"},{"i":213,"s":1366.89,"e":1370.29,"en":"I think the hardest part about doing this is simply just expanding your thinking.","zh":"我觉得做这件事最难的部分，其实就是拓宽你的思维。"},{"i":214,"s":1370.77,"e":1377.88,"en":"Actually, the capabilities have expanded so dramatically, it is is really expanding your thinking of what's possible in an unreasonably short time frame.","zh":"能力已经扩展得如此剧烈，真正难的是拓宽你对「在短得离谱的时间里能做成什么」的想象。"},{"i":215,"s":1378.16,"e":1393.55,"en":"And to me, the best way of trying to do that is um Patrick Collison has like, on his website PatrickCollison.com slash fast, I think, which is all of these projects that were unreasonably ambitious that were executed in a really really short time period. And what for me is now remarkable about.","zh":"而对我来说，做到这一点最好的办法是——Patrick Collison 的网站上有个页面，我记得是 PatrickCollison.com 斜杠 fast，上面全是那些雄心大得离谱、却在极短时间内完成的项目。现在让我觉得了不起的是——"},{"i":216,"s":1393.55,"e":1401.23,"en":"that list of projects is that they all existed before these tools made it possible for you to learn how to build something almost instantly, or ask it.","zh":"——那份项目清单上的所有项目，都发生在这些工具出现之前，而这些工具让你几乎可以瞬间学会怎么做一件事，或者直接去问它。"},{"i":217,"s":1401.58,"e":1405.66,"en":"With one question, hey, can you summarize this very complicated text or this very complicated book for me?","zh":"只要一个问题：嘿，你能帮我总结这段非常复杂的文字、或者这本非常复杂的书吗？"},{"i":218,"s":1406.1,"e":1419.05,"en":"um, immediately, or can I try to do all of these things were previously impossible to me, but now I'm able to do, like can I spin up a can you make for me like a CAD model of this idea that I might have? They really capabilities were truly.","zh":"马上就有答案。或者，我能不能试着做那些以前对我来说不可能、现在却能做到的事，比如我能不能快速搞出一个——你能不能帮我把我这个想法做成一个 CAD 模型？那些真正超出我能力范围的能力——"},{"i":219,"s":1419.37,"e":1420.81,"en":"beyond my reach are now in my reach.","zh":"——现在都在我能力范围之内了。"},{"i":220,"s":1421.17,"e":1427.94,"en":"And so, if those Fast projects were possible before, with the capabilities we used to have.","zh":"所以，如果那些 fast 清单上的项目，在我们过去那点能力下就已经能做成。"},{"i":221,"s":1428.06,"e":1434.66,"en":"Shouldn't we just see an exponential increase of the number of those types of unreasonably quickly and effectively executed things?","zh":"那我们难道不该看到这类快得离谱、又执行得极漂亮的事情呈指数级增长吗？"},{"i":222,"s":1435.37,"e":1437.21,"en":"um, with what AI has given us.","zh":"在 AI 给了我们这些之后。"},{"i":223,"s":1437.37,"e":1444.49,"en":"To your point, the hardest part is just remembering to even to try, just to be like, oh yeah, well let me see if Codex can do this for me.","zh":"照你说的，最难的部分就是记得去试一下，就是那种「哦对，我看看 Codex 能不能帮我做这个」。"},{"i":224,"s":1444.61,"e":1447.73,"en":"It's just like a new habit, and you like, thing we have to build in our brain.","zh":"这就像一个新习惯，是我们得在脑子里建立起来的东西。"},{"i":225,"s":1448.13,"e":1459.65,"en":"Tyler Cowen has this statement on his site, which is that you, most people underrate the impact of going to someone else and saying, hey, couldn't you what is like the more ambitious version of what you're doing?","zh":"Tyler Cowen 在他的网站上有句话，说大多数人低估了走到别人面前问「你难道不能——你在做的这件事，更有雄心的版本是什么？」的影响力。"},{"i":226,"s":1459.73,"e":1461.21,"en":"Or couldn't you try this faster?","zh":"或者「你不能试着做得更快吗？」"},{"i":227,"s":1461.33,"e":1463.49,"en":"Or couldn't you try this at a 10X bigger scale?","zh":"或者「你不能试着把规模放大十倍吗？」"},{"i":228,"s":1463.85,"e":1468.33,"en":"And in some ways, again, when I think of like what what do PMs do that is incredibly effective now?","zh":"某种意义上，再说回来，当我想「现在 PM 做什么是极其有效的？」"},{"i":229,"s":1468.37,"e":1470.41,"en":"Or what can they do that is incredibly effective now?","zh":"或者说，他们现在能做什么是极其有效的？"},{"i":230,"s":1470.87,"e":1476.83,"en":"I think elevating others' ambitions or reminding them of what's possible here is a huge part of the product management role.","zh":"我觉得抬高别人的雄心、提醒他们现在什么是可能的，是产品经理这个角色里非常重要的一部分。"},{"i":231,"s":1476.99,"e":1483.71,"en":"Like when folks say, hey, I think we can get this done in this way, or we can get this done by this timeline, or maybe this is the first version of it.","zh":"比如有人说，嘿，我觉得我们可以这样把这事做完，或者我们能在这个时间点前做完，又或者这可以是第一个版本。"},{"i":232,"s":1484.32,"e":1491.08,"en":"um, part of your job now is to elevate everyone's ambitions, and say actually, isn't the possibility ceiling meaningfully higher?","zh":"你现在工作的一部分，就是抬高所有人的雄心，说：其实，可能性的天花板不是高出一大截吗？"},{"i":233,"s":1491.24,"e":1494.04,"en":"Like, shouldn't we be more ambitious about what we're attempting here?","zh":"我们对正在尝试的这件事，难道不该更有雄心吗？"},{"i":234,"s":1494.04,"e":1495.8,"en":"Or like, couldn't we try this faster?","zh":"或者说，我们不能试着更快一点吗？"},{"i":235,"s":1496.44,"e":1500.48,"en":"And I think that's a, yeah, it's a it's a great place to be.","zh":"我觉得这是个很好的位置。"},{"i":236,"s":1500.52,"e":1508.04,"en":"It's a great place to be in terms of what you can build, what's possible, and in terms of um, yeah, how exciting the job becomes.","zh":"无论从你能造出什么、什么是可能的来看，还是从这份工作变得多有意思来看，都是很好的位置。"},{"i":237,"s":1508.36,"e":1509.36,"en":"It's just so interesting.","zh":"太有意思了。"},{"i":238,"s":1510.12,"e":1514.24,"en":"I remember uh Nick Turley was on the podcast, who is maybe had the role before you.","zh":"我记得 Nick Turley 上过这个播客，他大概是在你之前做这个岗位的。"},{"i":239,"s":1514.68,"e":1516.72,"en":"uh, I think he's working enterprise stuff now.","zh":"我想他现在在做企业业务那块。"},{"i":240,"s":1517.04,"e":1519.88,"en":"He had this uh meme internally, is this maximally accelerated?","zh":"他在内部搞出一个梗：这件事最大限度加速了吗？"},{"i":241,"s":1520.2,"e":1520.48,"en":"Yes.","zh":"是的。"},{"i":242,"s":1520.84,"e":1524.36,"en":"There's like an emoji I think inside the Slack, is this maximally accelerated?","zh":"我记得 Slack 里还有个对应的表情：这最大限度加速了吗？"},{"i":243,"s":1524.8,"e":1527.72,"en":"Is this maximally accelerated, is totally a OpenAI meme.","zh":"「这最大限度加速了吗」完全是 OpenAI 的梗。"},{"i":244,"s":1528.19,"e":1535.07,"en":"The other OpenAI meme that uh Andrea and Brazilino and I love to ask the team is like, are you mainlining it yet?","zh":"另一个 OpenAI 的梗，是我和 Andrea Ambrosino 最爱问团队的：你开始天天猛用它了吗？"},{"i":245,"s":1535.43,"e":1539.07,"en":"Which is like, are you using this product all day, every day to get your thing done?","zh":"意思是：你是不是每天一整天都在用这个产品来完成自己的工作？"},{"i":246,"s":1539.71,"e":1548.75,"en":"And I think that in combination with, are we being as ambitious as possible, which is about like the scope and the scale of what you're trying to do.","zh":"我觉得这一条再加上「我们是否足够有野心」——后者说的是你想做的事的范围和规模。"},{"i":247,"s":1549.75,"e":1551.27,"en":"Are are is this maximally accelerated?","zh":"还有：这最大限度加速了吗？"},{"i":248,"s":1551.43,"e":1553.31,"en":"Are we moving as fast as possible on it?","zh":"我们推进得已经够快了吗？"},{"i":249,"s":1553.51,"e":1555.23,"en":"And then, are you mainlining it yet?","zh":"然后是：你开始天天猛用它了吗？"},{"i":250,"s":1555.39,"e":1556.19,"en":"Are you using it?","zh":"你自己在用吗？"},{"i":251,"s":1556.19,"e":1561.79,"en":"And are you bringing all your taste to bear on whether this thing works and is something that people really want, and tightening that feedback loop as much as possible.","zh":"你有没有把自己全部的品味都用上，去判断这东西好不好使、是不是人们真正想要的，并把反馈闭环收得越紧越好。"},{"i":252,"s":1562.52,"e":1568.2,"en":"Those to me are like the three memes of product development, uh, that we we just have to spread as much as possible now.","zh":"在我看来，这就是产品开发的三个梗，我们现在必须尽可能把它们传播出去。"},{"i":253,"s":1568.8,"e":1569.48,"en":"I love that.","zh":"我很喜欢这个说法。"},{"i":254,"s":1569.72,"e":1571.12,"en":"That's like the new dogfooding.","zh":"这就像是新版的 dogfooding。"},{"i":255,"s":1571.28,"e":1573.92,"en":"Instead of dogfooding, you gotta mainline it.","zh":"不只是 dogfooding，你得天天猛用。"},{"i":256,"s":1573.92,"e":1574.68,"en":"Yeah, exactly.","zh":"对，没错。"},{"i":257,"s":1575.29,"e":1579.77,"en":"And that shows so deeply in the the tweets, ha ha.","zh":"这一点在推文里体现得特别明显，哈哈。"},{"i":258,"s":1579.77,"e":1587.09,"en":"This is mostly how I see your team communicate, of just like how obsessed they are with the product, and are just constantly asking what can we do better.","zh":"我看到你们团队主要就是这么交流的：他们对产品有多痴迷，一直在问我们还能哪里做得更好。"},{"i":259,"s":1587.54,"e":1588.5,"en":"What's bugging you now?","zh":"现在还有什么让你别扭的？"},{"i":260,"s":1588.58,"e":1589.38,"en":"Here's a thing we're building.","zh":"我们正在做这么个东西。"},{"i":261,"s":1589.54,"e":1597.3,"en":"It's like, it's very clear how to your point earlier that everyone is just the founder of their product, and it it's very clear how they act.","zh":"就像你刚才说的，每个人都是自己产品的创始人，这一点非常清楚，他们的做事方式也很清楚。"},{"i":262,"s":1598.0,"e":1599.16,"en":"As as an external observer.","zh":"从一个外部观察者的角度看。"},{"i":263,"s":1600.08,"e":1601.24,"en":"Are there any other memes internally?","zh":"内部还有别的梗吗？"},{"i":264,"s":1601.4,"e":1602.16,"en":"Those are so interesting.","zh":"这些太有意思了。"},{"i":265,"s":1602.16,"e":1602.64,"en":"Any others?","zh":"还有别的吗？"},{"i":266,"s":1603.52,"e":1604.28,"en":"uh, I don't know.","zh":"我也说不好。"},{"i":267,"s":1604.4,"e":1606.92,"en":"I'm trying to think of there's other good cultural memes.","zh":"我在想还有没有别的好的文化梗。"},{"i":268,"s":1608.34,"e":1614.86,"en":"Certainly a a really important one is like feeling the AGI, or just being conscious of of AGI coming.","zh":"肯定有一个很重要的是 feel the AGI，也就是时刻意识到 AGI 正在到来。"},{"i":269,"s":1615.66,"e":1630.01,"en":"um, there are so many outcomes for for what it could look like, or how one thinks about it, but a big huge part of what puts most people at this company is believing in that mission of AGI being beneficial.","zh":"它会是什么样子、每个人怎么理解它，可能的结果非常多，但大多数人来这家公司，很大一部分原因是相信「让 AGI 造福人类」这个使命。"},{"i":270,"s":1630.55,"e":1637.79,"en":"And trying to do whatever it takes to make that possible, both realization of AGI and ensuring that it is beneficial for for humanity.","zh":"并且愿意不惜一切让它成为可能——既实现 AGI，也确保它对人类有益。"},{"i":271,"s":1638.03,"e":1646.68,"en":"And in building products, another just constant refrain I have to keep in the back of my mind is are we building for where the models are going to be in two to three months?","zh":"在做产品的时候，我脑子里还有一句一直重复的话：我们做的东西，是面向两三个月后模型的水平吗？"},{"i":272,"s":1647.44,"e":1650.16,"en":"You fail if you build for where the models are now.","zh":"如果你按模型现在的水平来做，你就失败了。"},{"i":273,"s":1650.32,"e":1653.44,"en":"You fail if you build for where you think the models will be in a year.","zh":"如果你按你认为一年后模型会有的水平来做，你也失败了。"},{"i":274,"s":1653.52,"e":1659.4,"en":"Like both outcomes are equally wrong, and I'm sure many people have have talked about this, but both outcomes are really equally wrong.","zh":"这两种做法错得一样离谱，我相信很多人都讲过这一点，但它们真的错得一样离谱。"},{"i":275,"s":1659.88,"e":1661.44,"en":"If you're too early, you're wrong.","zh":"太超前，你就错了。"},{"i":276,"s":1661.56,"e":1666.68,"en":"If you build something that was overly focused on a past model's capabilities, you're entirely wrong.","zh":"如果你做的东西过度围绕过去某代模型的能力，你就彻底错了。"},{"i":277,"s":1666.76,"e":1670.08,"en":"The only way to build is two to three months.","zh":"唯一正确的做法，就是面向两三个月后。"},{"i":278,"s":1670.76,"e":1673.88,"en":"And having this belief of like, models are gonna get way better.","zh":"同时要抱着这样一个信念：模型会变得好得多。"},{"i":279,"s":1674.08,"e":1677.16,"en":"I need to think about the model capability as the center of this product.","zh":"我必须把模型能力当成这个产品的核心来思考。"},{"i":280,"s":1677.32,"e":1681.6,"en":"I need to get out of the way of the model in terms of the product constructs that I create.","zh":"在我搭建的产品结构上，我得给模型让路。"},{"i":281,"s":1682.29,"e":1684.81,"en":"How do I ensure this is right for the model in two or three months time?","zh":"我怎么确保它对两三个月后的模型也是合适的？"},{"i":282,"s":1685.09,"e":1687.09,"en":"How do you know what two or three months is like?","zh":"你怎么知道两三个月后会是什么样？"},{"i":283,"s":1687.25,"e":1692.69,"en":"It's like a challenging understanding, uh, especially while when we're on this in exponential.","zh":"这挺难判断的，尤其是我们正处在这条指数曲线上。"},{"i":284,"s":1693.41,"e":1694.57,"en":"Is it like it just a gut feeling?","zh":"是纯靠直觉吗？"},{"i":285,"s":1694.73,"e":1697.01,"en":"Is there anything, the researchers give you a sense, how does that work?","zh":"还是有什么依据，研究员会给你们一些感觉？这是怎么运作的？"},{"i":286,"s":1697.05,"e":1704.17,"en":"Yeah, certainly communicating really tightly with research on where they think things are going is incredibly important.","zh":"和研究团队紧密沟通、了解他们认为事情会往哪里走，这肯定极其重要。"},{"i":287,"s":1704.85,"e":1717.07,"en":"um, like these things aren't entirely a a like a black box, in that you kind of know, hey, we're focused on these particular things, like we would like models be better at at coding in these specific ways or better writing in these specific ways.","zh":"这些事并不完全是黑箱，你多少知道我们正专注在哪些具体方向上，比如希望模型在某些特定的编程能力上更强，或在某些特定的写作能力上更强。"},{"i":288,"s":1717.71,"e":1722.71,"en":"um, so we we certainly have focused efforts on making the model better at specific capabilities.","zh":"所以我们确实会集中投入去提升模型的特定能力。"},{"i":289,"s":1723.29,"e":1734.09,"en":"And so, knowing where that is, and ensuring that product development is as tied as possible to what research has as its agenda and its roadmap, is is really important.","zh":"因此，知道进展到哪一步，并让产品开发尽可能紧扣研究的议程和路线图，非常重要。"},{"i":290,"s":1734.86,"e":1737.46,"en":"A quote that I'll never forget is when Kevin Weil was on the podcast.","zh":"有一句话我永远忘不了，是 Kevin Weil 上这个播客时说的。"},{"i":291,"s":1737.66,"e":1739.58,"en":"He was chief product officer at that time.","zh":"他当时是首席产品官。"},{"i":292,"s":1740.3,"e":1743.42,"en":"uh, He said that this is the worst the models will ever be.","zh":"他说：今天的模型是它们以后最差的样子。"},{"i":293,"s":1744.64,"e":1751.84,"en":"And it sounds so simple, but it's just like, it's hard to just like wrap your head around that, that this is the worst they'll ever be.","zh":"这话听起来很简单，但真的很难想明白——今天已经是它们最差的时候了。"},{"i":294,"s":1752.2,"e":1756.1,"en":"Like, it's such a cliche almost now to say that, but it's it's true, it's absurd.","zh":"现在说这话几乎成了陈词滥调，但它是真的，也很荒唐。"},{"i":295,"s":1756.1,"e":1759.3,"en":"This is like, yeah, it's it's absurd, it's truly absurd.","zh":"对，很荒唐，真的很荒唐。"},{"i":296,"s":1761.01,"e":1761.41,"en":"Oh, man.","zh":"天啊。"},{"i":297,"s":1761.85,"e":1765.65,"en":"OK, um, I want to talk about ChatGPT the app briefly.","zh":"好，我想简单聊聊 ChatGPT 这个 app。"},{"i":298,"s":1766.25,"e":1768.37,"en":"uh, OK, so I have it open right now.","zh":"我现在就开着它。"},{"i":299,"s":1768.45,"e":1768.81,"en":"Yes.","zh":"好的。"},{"i":300,"s":1769.21,"e":1771.65,"en":"OK, so here's what I see in it.","zh":"我在里面看到的是这样。"},{"i":301,"s":1771.88,"e":1777.88,"en":"ChatGPT, and then there's a drop down, and there's ChatGPT and Codex, and then there's this toggle, Chat and Work.","zh":"ChatGPT，然后有个下拉菜单，里面有 ChatGPT 和 Codex，接着还有一个切换开关：Chat 和 Work。"},{"i":302,"s":1779.11,"e":1780.15,"en":"Tara, what is going on?","zh":"Tara，这是怎么回事？"},{"i":303,"s":1780.27,"e":1781.11,"en":"What are all these things?","zh":"这些都是什么？"},{"i":304,"s":1781.31,"e":1786.15,"en":"Help us understand which of these each of these things are for, and where does this, where do you think this goes?","zh":"帮我们理解一下这里每样东西分别是干什么的，还有你觉得这会走向哪里？"},{"i":305,"s":1786.31,"e":1787.23,"en":"Is it gonna stay like this?","zh":"会一直保持这个样子吗？"},{"i":306,"s":1787.51,"e":1789.75,"en":"What, what, is there like a next step that you're imagining already?","zh":"你们心里是不是已经有下一步的设想了？"},{"i":307,"s":1790.37,"e":1795.73,"en":"Our north star here is that users do not need to make decisions between picking between all these different options.","zh":"我们这里的北极星是：用户不需要在这些不同选项之间做决定。"},{"i":308,"s":1796.13,"e":1800.65,"en":"Ideally, there is no there is no toggle here, that you go to the box.","zh":"理想情况下这里根本没有切换开关，你直接进到输入框。"},{"i":309,"s":1801.41,"e":1810.81,"en":"You type in your task, like, I would like to build a really awesome app that um I don't know, helps my podcast guests like do research before episodes or something like that.","zh":"你输入你的任务，比如：我想做一个很棒的 app，帮我的播客嘉宾在录制前做调研之类的。"},{"i":310,"s":1812.62,"e":1818.06,"en":"It will just pick the right harness, it will pick the right model for you to be able to get that thing done.","zh":"它会直接选好合适的 harness、合适的模型，帮你把这件事做完。"},{"i":311,"s":1818.18,"e":1829.26,"en":"Ideally, the the choice here is like not on our users to have to pick between all these different concepts and understand not only what are they trying to do, but understand the limitations and capabilities of our products.","zh":"理想情况下，这个选择不该落在用户身上——不该让他们既要清楚自己想做什么，还得了解我们产品的能力和局限。"},{"i":312,"s":1829.77,"e":1832.09,"en":"So, that is certainly where we want to go.","zh":"所以那肯定是我们想去的方向。"},{"i":313,"s":1832.61,"e":1843.79,"en":"In the in the near term, picking between ChatGPT and Codex is really a choice for are you, do you wanna stay in sort of like more development oriented UI?","zh":"短期内，在 ChatGPT 和 Codex 之间做选择，其实是在问：你想不想待在更偏开发的界面里？"},{"i":314,"s":1843.87,"e":1848.83,"en":"Or do you want to have the same powering capabilities in the ChatGPT mode?","zh":"还是说你想在 ChatGPT 模式里拿到同样强大的能力？"},{"i":315,"s":1848.87,"e":1850.43,"en":"And so, if you're a Codex user.","zh":"所以，如果你是 Codex 用户。"},{"i":316,"s":1850.93,"e":1852.69,"en":"Keep using Codex, you're not missing out on anything.","zh":"继续用 Codex，你不会错过任何东西。"},{"i":317,"s":1852.85,"e":1854.49,"en":"Like continue using it as much as possible.","zh":"尽管接着用，能用多少用多少。"},{"i":318,"s":1854.85,"e":1861.25,"en":"But if you're a ChatGPT user who is like, what are these new agentic capabilities, you should probably be in ChatGPT mode.","zh":"但如果你是 ChatGPT 用户，想知道这些新的 agent 能力是什么，那你大概应该待在 ChatGPT 模式里。"},{"i":319,"s":1861.83,"e":1867.75,"en":"And then when you're in ChatGPT, if you wanna have conversations, if you wanna search, that's where chat mode is the right thing.","zh":"在 ChatGPT 里，如果你想对话、想搜索，那 chat 模式就是对的选择。"},{"i":320,"s":1867.83,"e":1873.47,"en":"It's the you know, same chat mode you know and love with better and better models and newer and newer capabilities every time.","zh":"就是你熟悉和喜欢的那个 chat 模式，只是模型一次比一次好、能力一次比一次新。"},{"i":321,"s":1873.97,"e":1878.17,"en":"But in work mode, that's where, under the covers, this is Codex.","zh":"而在 work 模式里，底层其实就是 Codex。"},{"i":322,"s":1878.61,"e":1888.35,"en":"We've removed some of like the coding UI, like you don't, you're not gonna see a work tree pop up all of a sudden in in work mode, but it is the same power to get things done.","zh":"我们去掉了一部分编程界面，比如你不会在 work 模式里突然看到一个 work tree 冒出来，但把事情做成的能力是一样的。"},{"i":323,"s":1888.75,"e":1899.63,"en":"to um for example generate like a really complex financial model, that's all possible in work mode, and we see people especially, I I mentioned our corporate finance team.","zh":"比如说，生成一个非常复杂的财务模型，这在 work 模式里完全做得到，我们也看到很多人这么用，尤其是我提到过的公司财务团队。"},{"i":324,"s":1900.23,"e":1915.91,"en":"um, use Work Mode to do incredible incredible things that were previously either manual or required deep expertise from one person on the team become things that the whole team can be able to execute, or just elevate the ambitions of everyone on the team in terms of timeline.","zh":"他们用 work 模式做出很多了不起的事，那些以前要么靠手工、要么需要团队里某个人的深厚专业能力才能做的事，现在整个团队都能执行，或者说在时间线上抬高了团队里每个人的野心。"},{"i":325,"s":1915.95,"e":1918.11,"en":"or capabilities or frontier of what they can get done.","zh":"还有能力上限，以及他们能做到的边界。"},{"i":326,"s":1918.62,"e":1919.46,"en":"OK, that's really helpful.","zh":"好，这很有帮助。"},{"i":327,"s":1919.62,"e":1921.42,"en":"So, there's kind of like these three modes currently.","zh":"所以现在大概有这三种模式。"},{"i":328,"s":1921.62,"e":1926.18,"en":"There's like the engineering mode, the chat mode, and then the do knowledge work mode.","zh":"工程模式、聊天模式，还有做知识工作的模式。"},{"i":329,"s":1926.78,"e":1933.23,"en":"And the knowledge work mode, it's actually Codex doing all that work, but people may not know what Codex is, may not, may may be afraid of it.","zh":"知识工作模式背后其实全是 Codex 在干活，但人们可能不知道 Codex 是什么，甚至可能有点怕它。"},{"i":330,"s":1934.07,"e":1936.43,"en":"Is there anything in that work mode that's not just Codex?","zh":"work 模式里有没有什么东西不只是 Codex？"},{"i":331,"s":1936.51,"e":1937.47,"en":"Cuz that's actually really interesting.","zh":"因为这其实挺有意思的。"},{"i":332,"s":1937.83,"e":1940.83,"en":"Is it like, is there like additional harness tweaks to make it feel a little different?","zh":"是不是在 harness 上做了额外调整，让它感觉有点不一样？"},{"i":333,"s":1940.91,"e":1942.71,"en":"Or is it just the same thing with a little different UI?","zh":"还是说就是同一个东西，只是界面稍有不同？"},{"i":334,"s":1943.44,"e":1945.16,"en":"It's it's really at the UI level.","zh":"差别真的就在界面这一层。"},{"i":335,"s":1945.8,"e":1957.55,"en":"um, so, work mode and Codex mode, if you go to Codex and ask it to generate a a amazing financial model to price your product or something like that, or like tell me predict my revenue for the next six months or something like that.","zh":"所以说 work 模式和 Codex 模式，如果你去 Codex 让它生成一个很棒的财务模型来给你的产品定价之类的，或者让它预测我未来六个月的收入之类的。"},{"i":336,"s":1957.55,"e":1959.35,"en":"Codex will do as good a job as work mode.","zh":"Codex 做得会和 work 模式一样好。"},{"i":337,"s":1960.19,"e":1964.79,"en":"It's like really about, whilst it's doing so, what kind of UI do you want to see in the chain of thought?","zh":"区别真的只在于：它在做这件事的时候，你想在思维链里看到什么样的界面？"},{"i":338,"s":1964.91,"e":1967.07,"en":"What kind of technical detail do you want exposed to you?","zh":"你希望向你暴露多少技术细节？"},{"i":339,"s":1967.99,"e":1973.51,"en":"The, it's like incredible, it's similarly powerful, and so, Codex users aren't missing out on anything by not switching modes.","zh":"它同样强大，所以 Codex 用户不切换模式并不会错过什么。"},{"i":340,"s":1973.55,"e":1977.27,"en":"In fact, we do not want them to, like, stay in Codex and do all the stuff you want to do in Codex.","zh":"事实上我们也不希望他们切——就待在 Codex 里，把你想做的事都在 Codex 里做完。"},{"i":341,"s":1977.67,"e":1980.91,"en":"And we will show you the appropriate UI based on the things you asked for.","zh":"我们会根据你提出的要求，给你展示合适的界面。"},{"i":342,"s":1981.15,"e":1986.63,"en":"Truly, our north star is to like merge all these things so that users don't have to make any of these decisions.","zh":"说真的，我们的北极星就是把这些东西合并起来，让用户不必做这些选择。"},{"i":343,"s":1987.19,"e":1991.67,"en":"The separation is really more about how can we meet people where they are?","zh":"现在这种区分，更多是为了尽量在用户当下所处的位置去接住他们。"},{"i":344,"s":1992.22,"e":2006.85,"en":"As much as possible, in terms of the products that they use, in terms of their familiarity with concepts, and make sure that we are enabling everyone to take advantage of working with agents, which has transformed entirely the way every single developer works.","zh":"尽可能贴合他们在用的产品、他们对这些概念的熟悉程度，并确保每个人都能用上与 agent 协作的能力——这已经彻底改变了每一位开发者的工作方式。"},{"i":345,"s":2007.25,"e":2008.73,"en":"We should do the same thing with knowledge work.","zh":"我们应该在知识工作上做同样的事。"},{"i":346,"s":2009.05,"e":2009.85,"en":"It makes sense.","zh":"这说得通。"},{"i":347,"s":2010.61,"e":2016.89,"en":"uh, there's this slight, because things move so fast, like it would, I imagine somebody's like, let's try Codex.","zh":"因为一切变化太快，我想象当时有人说：我们来试试 Codex 吧。"},{"i":348,"s":2017.09,"e":2017.85,"en":"This is gonna be awesome.","zh":"这肯定会很棒。"},{"i":349,"s":2018.22,"e":2020.86,"en":"And then it takes off, and there's 10 million monthly active users.","zh":"然后它火了，有了一千万月活用户。"},{"i":350,"s":2021.18,"e":2022.86,"en":"And then they're like, wait, what are we doing here?","zh":"接着大家就想：等等，我们这是在干什么？"},{"i":351,"s":2022.9,"e":2024.62,"en":"We got ChatGPT, we got Codex, how do we?","zh":"我们有 ChatGPT，又有 Codex，那要怎么办？"},{"i":352,"s":2024.86,"e":2033.05,"en":"So it makes sense why these things, you know, like it's not gonna feel obvious and perfect for a while, because you have to kind of adjust as things work and things don't work.","zh":"所以可以理解，这些东西有一段时间不会显得那么理所当然、那么完美，因为你得根据什么行得通、什么行不通不断调整。"},{"i":353,"s":2033.45,"e":2040.01,"en":"And there's these kind of transition periods of like, OK, cool, now let's get people moving towards this vision of the super app, let's say.","zh":"中间会有这样的过渡期：好，接下来让大家朝着这个愿景走，就叫它\"超级 App\"吧。"},{"i":354,"s":2041.17,"e":2059.28,"en":"um, OK, I imagine one of the hardest parts of your job is balancing this 1 billion MAU product ChatGPT, maybe the most successful consumer product in history, with Codex, which is this new thing, and other new things that you guys want to try.","zh":"我想你工作中最难的一部分，是要在 ChatGPT 这个十亿月活的产品——可能是史上最成功的消费级产品——和 Codex 这样的新东西、以及你们想尝试的其他新东西之间做平衡。"},{"i":355,"s":2060.89,"e":2061.85,"en":"How do you think about that?","zh":"你是怎么看这件事的？"},{"i":356,"s":2061.89,"e":2069.69,"en":"Just, I don't know, just balancing these very innovative, fast moving teams and products with this, like, OK, there's a billion people using this, we can't change this dramatically.","zh":"就是怎么在这些非常创新、跑得飞快的团队和产品，跟\"有十亿人在用，不能大改\"之间做平衡。"},{"i":357,"s":2070.13,"e":2082.98,"en":"Yeah, I think one of the most interesting things here is that we would we, one of the goals of launching work in ChatGPT Web, and launching it in the desktop app, and bringing these things together.","zh":"我觉得这里最有意思的一点是，我们把工作场景做进 ChatGPT 网页版、做进桌面 App，把这些东西整合起来，"},{"i":358,"s":2083.49,"e":2091.13,"en":"Was to look at those billion people who are using ChatGPT, and bring them more and more of the agents' power.","zh":"目的之一就是面向那十亿正在用 ChatGPT 的人，把 agent 的能力越来越多地带给他们。"},{"i":359,"s":2091.45,"e":2095.799,"en":"Like if you think about the first era of AI products as chat.","zh":"如果把 AI 产品的第一个时代看作 chat，"},{"i":360,"s":2096.479,"e":2104.519,"en":"The second era of these products is clearly working with agents, and you know, primarily has been coding agents.","zh":"那这些产品的第二个时代显然是与 agent 协作，而且到目前为止主要是编码 agent。"},{"i":361,"s":2104.599,"e":2113.52,"en":"We'd like to bring it to more more domain certainly like knowledge work, and that is part of the goal of giving all these billion chat users the power of work.","zh":"我们希望把它带到更多领域，尤其是知识工作，这也是把工作能力交给这十亿 chat 用户的目标之一。"},{"i":362,"s":2113.64,"e":2118.84,"en":"Certainly the product challenge that it, that's on us is how do we not only bring it to them?","zh":"当然，落在我们身上的产品挑战是，不只是把它送到他们面前，"},{"i":363,"s":2119.26,"e":2124.02,"en":"But make it natural and easy to adopt, make it not a decision they have to explicitly make.","zh":"还要让它自然、容易上手，让它不需要用户明确做一个决定。"},{"i":364,"s":2124.1,"e":2125.42,"en":"We can just help them do the right thing.","zh":"我们可以直接帮他们做对的事。"},{"i":365,"s":2125.5,"e":2133.48,"en":"How do we take, decomplexify it, so they don't need to think about things like harnesses, which feel like crazy concepts for uh a billion consumers to understand.","zh":"怎么把它去复杂化，让他们不必去想 harness 这种概念——对十亿消费者来说，那听上去太离谱了。"},{"i":366,"s":2133.96,"e":2136.72,"en":"So that that is primarily the the challenge.","zh":"所以这主要就是挑战所在。"},{"i":367,"s":2137.04,"e":2149.49,"en":"And then of course, like that third era that that might come soon is how do you work with a like persistent coworker, who is able to get things done with you, maybe collaboratively with other people.","zh":"当然，还有可能很快到来的第三个时代：你怎么和一个持续在线的同事协作，它能和你一起把事情做完，甚至和其他人协同完成。"},{"i":368,"s":2149.89,"e":2158.85,"en":"And so part of this challenge in the near term is we're introducing agents to a billion people who may not have experienced them yet.","zh":"所以短期内的挑战之一是，我们要把 agent 介绍给十亿可能还没体验过它的人。"},{"i":369,"s":2159.05,"e":2163.49,"en":"How do we do so in the easiest, most natural, and most usable way possible?","zh":"我们怎么用最简单、最自然、最好用的方式做到这一点？"},{"i":370,"s":2164.11,"e":2167.15,"en":"Certainly, there's a lot more for us to do to to make that happen.","zh":"当然，要做到这点我们还有很多事要做。"},{"i":371,"s":2167.59,"e":2176.59,"en":"But part of this is also a lesson I've had, maybe contrasting like pre AI era or past product experience with this one.","zh":"但这里面还有我学到的一课，算是把 AI 之前的时代、过去的产品经验，和现在做个对比。"},{"i":372,"s":2177.13,"e":2180.05,"en":"Which is, at previous companies like polish was king.","zh":"那就是：在以前的公司，打磨是王道。"},{"i":373,"s":2181.05,"e":2188.89,"en":"uh, getting every UI interaction or getting every little thing completely right was way more important than shipping something early.","zh":"把每一个 UI 交互、每一个小细节都做到完全正确，远比早点发布重要。"},{"i":374,"s":2189.44,"e":2202.74,"en":"Because time didn't make as much of a difference in terms of the outcome, and so as such, like, if every corner wasn't like perfectly polished and everything was wasn't exactly correct, you might as well not ship it.","zh":"因为时间对结果的影响没那么大，所以如果哪个角落没打磨到位、有哪里不完全对，那还不如别发。"},{"i":375,"s":2203.06,"e":2217.1,"en":"But I think what's been really compelling and interesting about this era and this product experience has been getting the product in the hands of users, when you have so much conviction that, hey, it's transformative, like, is way better than perfect.","zh":"但这个时代、这段产品经历里真正让我觉得有说服力、有意思的是：当你无比确信这东西是变革性的，那把产品交到用户手里，远胜过做到完美。"},{"i":376,"s":2217.74,"e":2223.36,"en":"And that urgency and that uh introduction of that product is is so important.","zh":"那种紧迫感、把产品推出去这件事，非常重要。"},{"i":377,"s":2223.52,"e":2234.45,"en":"So we have a lot to do to make it more usable and easier for chat users, certainly, especially for folks who are not maybe even using it for productivity, but using it for like consumer tasks.","zh":"所以要让 chat 用户用起来更顺手、更容易，我们还有很多要做，尤其是对那些可能不是拿它做生产力、而是做日常消费类任务的人。"},{"i":378,"s":2235.01,"e":2239.57,"en":"but um yeah, done is better than perfect, and we have so much more to do.","zh":"但是的，完成好过完美，我们要做的还有太多。"},{"i":379,"s":2240.01,"e":2249.74,"en":"Yeah, remember when uh this app first launched, there was a lot of uh, comments about the confusion, and seeing how quickly the team iterated and respond to the feedback is exactly what what I'm hearing here is.","zh":"记得这个 App 刚上线的时候，有很多关于\"看不懂、很困惑\"的评论，而看到团队迭代和回应反馈的速度，正好印证了我刚听到的这套思路："},{"i":380,"s":2249.94,"e":2253.94,"en":"get it out, figure out what the hell's, what what's not working, how people are using it, iterate quickly.","zh":"先发出去，搞清楚到底哪里不行、大家是怎么用的，然后快速迭代。"},{"i":381,"s":2254.1,"e":2255.74,"en":"Feels like that's the the model now.","zh":"感觉现在就是这个模式。"},{"i":382,"s":2256.0,"e":2263.88,"en":"And of course, there are things that you can continue to iterate and get that feedback prior to launching, and there's a lot that we can and should always do better.","zh":"当然，也有些东西是可以在上线前就持续迭代、拿到反馈的，我们也总有很多地方能做得、也该做得更好。"},{"i":383,"s":2264.36,"e":2268.32,"en":"But um iterating as quickly as possible, listening to the right signals.","zh":"但尽可能快地迭代，倾听正确的信号，"},{"i":384,"s":2269.39,"e":2272.83,"en":"Is regardless of whether that's pre launch, post launch, ideally pre launch.","zh":"不管是上线前还是上线后，理想情况当然是上线前，"},{"i":385,"s":2273.15,"e":2275.43,"en":"um, is is the is the key thing.","zh":"这才是关键。"},{"i":386,"s":2275.99,"e":2280.23,"en":"This episode is brought to you by Mercury, radically different banking now with Spend.","zh":"本集由 Mercury 赞助——彻底不一样的银行服务，现在还有 Spend。"},{"i":387,"s":2280.8,"e":2283.04,"en":"I've been a Mercury customer for so many years now.","zh":"我做 Mercury 的客户已经很多年了。"},{"i":388,"s":2283.32,"e":2287.64,"en":"I switched all my business banking to Mercury, and honestly I could not be happier.","zh":"我把所有企业银行业务都搬到了 Mercury，说实话我再满意不过。"},{"i":389,"s":2287.88,"e":2292.52,"en":"It's what online banking feels like when it's built by product people, not by bankers.","zh":"这就是网上银行由做产品的人、而不是由银行家来做出来的样子。"},{"i":390,"s":2293.09,"e":2303.85,"en":"And now with Spend, you can give your team individual cards, set spending limits per person or per team, and have expense receipts automatically pulled in from Gmail or over text.","zh":"现在有了 Spend，你可以给团队成员发各自的卡，按人或按团队设置支出上限，还能自动从 Gmail 或短信里抓取报销票据。"},{"i":391,"s":2304.33,"e":2307.77,"en":"You can even give your AI agents their own cards with their own limits and policies.","zh":"你甚至可以给你的 AI agent 发它们自己的卡，配上各自的额度和策略。"},{"i":392,"s":2308.17,"e":2312.13,"en":"Most founders start out the same way, one card used by everybody at the company.","zh":"大多数创始人一开始都是同一个套路：全公司共用一张卡。"},{"i":393,"s":2312.37,"e":2314.37,"en":"It works until it stops working.","zh":"一开始还行，直到有一天不行了。"},{"i":394,"s":2314.61,"e":2320.09,"en":"Someone goes over, a receipt disappears, you spend two days trying to figure out who spent what and why.","zh":"有人超支了，某张票据不见了，你要花两天去查谁花了多少、为什么花。"},{"i":395,"s":2320.43,"e":2323.87,"en":"Spend is expense management built directly into Mercury.","zh":"Spend 是直接内建在 Mercury 里的费用管理。"},{"i":396,"s":2324.19,"e":2329.23,"en":"All your team's cards, budgets, and reimbursements all live in the same place as your business banking.","zh":"团队所有的卡、预算和报销，都和你的企业银行账户在同一个地方。"},{"i":397,"s":2329.75,"e":2332.79,"en":"No chasing, no manual reviews, no end of month scramble.","zh":"不用追着人要，不用手工审核，月底不用手忙脚乱。"},{"i":398,"s":2333.19,"e":2337.19,"en":"The result is a team that can move fast, and a founder who is no longer the bottleneck.","zh":"结果就是：团队能跑得快，创始人不再是瓶颈。"},{"i":399,"s":2337.67,"e":2340.75,"en":"Learn more and get signed up at mercury dot com.","zh":"去 mercury.com 了解更多并注册。"},{"i":400,"s":2340.95,"e":2344.03,"en":"Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC insured bank.","zh":"Mercury 是一家金融科技公司，不是 FDIC 承保的银行。"},{"i":401,"s":2344.15,"e":2347.03,"en":"Banking services provided by Choice Financial Group, an FDIC member.","zh":"银行服务由 FDIC 成员机构 Choice Financial Group 提供。"},{"i":402,"s":2348.03,"e":2353.75,"en":"The IO card is issued by Patriot Bank, and a member FDIC, pursuant to a license from MasterCard International Incorporated.","zh":"IO 信用卡由 Patriot Bank 发行，该行为 FDIC 成员，依据 MasterCard International Incorporated 的授权发行。"},{"i":403,"s":2354.03,"e":2358.07,"en":"Something I've noticed on Twitter is there's definitely been this vibe shift.","zh":"我在 Twitter 上注意到一件事，风向明显变了。"},{"i":404,"s":2359.08,"e":2362.28,"en":"From Claude Code to Codex in the past few months.","zh":"过去几个月里，从 Claude Code 转向了 Codex。"},{"i":405,"s":2362.28,"e":2365.52,"en":"Used to be everyone was Claude Code, this Claude Code that.","zh":"以前所有人都是 Claude Code 这、Claude Code 那。"},{"i":406,"s":2365.84,"e":2369.12,"en":"More recently, it just feels like people are leaning now towards Codex.","zh":"最近感觉大家更倾向于 Codex 了。"},{"i":407,"s":2369.65,"e":2373.61,"en":"At least on Twitter, which is a bubble, but it's where a lot of tech people are.","zh":"至少在 Twitter 上是这样，那是个泡泡，但很多科技圈的人都在那儿。"},{"i":408,"s":2374.41,"e":2380.17,"en":"I'm curious what's shifted internally in the past, I don't know, 3~6 months, other than Tara joining and shaping up.","zh":"我很好奇过去，不知道，三到六个月里，内部有什么变化，除了 Tara 加入、把整个"},{"i":409,"s":2380.43,"e":2380.91,"en":"The ship?","zh":"队伍整顿了一番？"},{"i":410,"s":2381.71,"e":2393.34,"en":"uh, Is there anything that you can share that's just like, okay, we figured this thing out, we shifted this, we cut this thing, what what helped shift the vibes and uh, help Codex become as successful as it as is becoming.","zh":"有什么可以分享的吗，比如：好，我们把这件事想明白了、我们调整了这个、砍掉了那个——是什么让风向变了，让 Codex 变得像现在这么成功？"},{"i":411,"s":2393.74,"e":2405.1,"en":"You know, I think there's like this phrase which is uh before enlightenment, uh, carry wood or carry water chop wood, post enlightenment, uh, carry water chop wood sort of thing.","zh":"我觉得有句话是这么说的：开悟之前，砍柴挑水；开悟之后，还是砍柴挑水。"},{"i":412,"s":2405.52,"e":2419.36,"en":"And actually with the Codex app, um, the team who initially got it up and running, and were working on it, uh, were super, y, again user focus, tight iteration loop, really dogfooded the thing, like mainlined the app.","zh":"其实在 Codex App 这件事上，最早把它做起来、一直在做的那个团队，非常以用户为中心，迭代循环很紧，真的在吃自己的狗粮，把这个 App 当主力工具用，"},{"i":413,"s":2419.86,"e":2422.26,"en":"As much as possible to get get everything right.","zh":"尽可能地用，把每个细节都做对。"},{"i":414,"s":2422.5,"e":2428.06,"en":"Folks started to realize that was happening on externally and on Twitter, and users started to really notice.","zh":"外部和 Twitter 上的人开始意识到这件事在发生，用户也真的开始注意到了。"},{"i":415,"s":2428.58,"e":2444.32,"en":"But the team was always really focused on users, really focused on that iteration, and it was merely the, it's just how we said like the market catching up, that was the change, and that process has not changed internally.","zh":"但团队一直都非常聚焦用户、非常专注于迭代，变的只是我们刚才说的市场追上来了，而这个过程在内部并没有变。"},{"i":416,"s":2444.48,"e":2447.2,"en":"Everyone still constantly uses the app.","zh":"所有人还是天天都在用这个 App。"},{"i":417,"s":2447.28,"e":2459.36,"en":"Everyone in the who's building it obviously is a developer using it for development, and is constantly fixing not only their own problems, but trying to listen to other people in the company's problems, and user problems.","zh":"做这个产品的每个人当然都是开发者，都在用它来开发，而且不只在修自己遇到的问题，还在努力倾听公司里其他人的问题和用户的问题。"},{"i":418,"s":2459.52,"e":2469.19,"en":"Actually what's sort of remarkable is that the mode of operating hasn't changed, it's always been the same thing I'd mentioned earlier, like, are we, like, are we elevating our ambition sufficiently?","zh":"其实挺值得一提的是，运作方式根本没变，一直都是我前面说的那几件事：我们的野心是不是抬得足够高？"},{"i":419,"s":2469.43,"e":2471.07,"en":"Are we maximally accelerating progress?","zh":"我们是不是在最大限度地加速进展？"},{"i":420,"s":2471.35,"e":2473.03,"en":"And are we mainlining it as much as possible?","zh":"我们是不是在尽可能把它当主力来用？"},{"i":421,"s":2473.87,"e":2484.27,"en":"And I think it's great that uh users and folks on Twitter have noticed, but that that operation, like that full credit to the team, like that hasn't changed.","zh":"我觉得用户和 Twitter 上的人注意到了当然很好，但那套运作方式，这完全要归功于团队，那部分并没有变。"},{"i":422,"s":2484.59,"e":2489.15,"en":"What's really interesting about this answer is it's is the very human part of it.","zh":"这个回答里真正有意思的，是其中非常\"人\"的那一面。"},{"i":423,"s":2489.75,"e":2499.19,"en":"It's you, it's Andrew, it's Tebow, it's the team, just like being obsessed with the the customer, the product, and it's not like, it's not like AI was the answer, it's the humans that made the difference.","zh":"是你，是 Andrew，是 Tebow，是整个团队，就是对客户、对产品的那种执着；不是 AI 给出了答案，是这些人做出了差别。"},{"i":424,"s":2499.43,"e":2502.79,"en":"Yeah, I'll I'll give the the team deserves like full full credit here.","zh":"是的，这里完全应该把功劳记在团队头上。"},{"i":425,"s":2502.95,"e":2516.96,"en":"The everyone on the team is incredibly thoughtful and independent, and to the point of like, there are, you know, many founders at OpenAI, like almost everyone on that team, like the design team especially, like acts like founders.","zh":"团队里每个人都极其有想法、极其独立，甚至可以说，OpenAI 有很多创始人级别的人，那个团队里几乎每个人，尤其是设计团队，都像创始人一样在做事。"},{"i":426,"s":2517.8,"e":2520.36,"en":"And cares about every piece and every detail.","zh":"他们在意每一个部分、每一个细节。"},{"i":427,"s":2520.48,"e":2530.78,"en":"And when they notice an area that should be better, they go build it very independently, and and get the thing up and running, and if it doesn't test well internally, like people aren't using it.","zh":"当他们发现某个地方本可以更好，就非常独立地去把它做出来、跑起来，如果内部试用效果不好、大家不用，"},{"i":428,"s":2530.82,"e":2534.78,"en":"if people don't find it useful, they'll iterate on it, and then finally, like, ship it externally.","zh":"如果大家觉得没用，他们就继续迭代，最后才对外发布。"},{"i":429,"s":2534.94,"e":2540.22,"en":"But that loop is full credit to like people on the team and and individuals for making that happen.","zh":"这个循环完全要归功于团队里的人、归功于每个个体把它做成了。"},{"i":430,"s":2540.63,"e":2550.83,"en":"Something you touched on is this idea of roles overlapping, this idea of like, you know, engineers are doing a PM-y work, you're doing probably shipping prototypes and building, maybe shipping to production, I don't know.","zh":"你刚提到一点，就是角色边界在重叠：工程师在做 PM 的活儿，你自己大概也在做原型、在写东西，也许还发到线上，我不知道。"},{"i":431,"s":2551.29,"e":2553.73,"en":"Just, it feels like that also creates a lot of challenges.","zh":"感觉这也带来了很多挑战。"},{"i":432,"s":2554.17,"e":2557.09,"en":"I hear from a lot of people, like, what is my job now as a as a designer?","zh":"我听很多人说：我作为一个设计师，现在的工作到底是什么？"},{"i":433,"s":2557.17,"e":2558.65,"en":"What am I what am I responsible for?","zh":"我该为什么负责？"},{"i":434,"s":2558.77,"e":2559.85,"en":"What am I not responsible for?","zh":"我不该为什么负责？"},{"i":435,"s":2560.17,"e":2561.89,"en":"As a marketer, what am I what am I doing?","zh":"作为一个市场人员，我到底在干什么？"},{"i":436,"s":2562.45,"e":2563.21,"en":"Is that something you notice?","zh":"你有注意到这个现象吗？"},{"i":437,"s":2563.53,"e":2565.45,"en":"Is that something that you're dealing with?","zh":"这是你正在处理的问题吗？"},{"i":438,"s":2566.25,"e":2568.05,"en":"um, Just any thoughts along those lines.","zh":"这方面有什么想法？"},{"i":439,"s":2568.61,"e":2572.01,"en":"I think the thing I've always liked the most about working at startups.","zh":"我一直最喜欢在创业公司工作的一点是，"},{"i":440,"s":2572.8,"e":2586.36,"en":"And sometimes I've started at a startup that accidentally grew into a large company, but largely primarily working at startups is that there are very few boundaries around your role, that like everything and nothing is your responsibility, ultimately you're accountable for success.","zh":"虽然有时候我加入的创业公司不小心长成了大公司，但大体上主要还是在创业公司，那里角色边界非常少，一切都是你的责任、又什么都不是你的责任，最终你要对成功负责。"},{"i":441,"s":2586.99,"e":2596.79,"en":"Actually, like Stripe was very very much this way, where there are no boundaries around what a engineer could do, versus a product manager could do, versus a designer could do, everyone could do anything.","zh":"其实 Stripe 就非常是这个样子，工程师能做什么、产品经理能做什么、设计师能做什么，中间没有边界，谁都可以做任何事。"},{"i":442,"s":2597.39,"e":2605.35,"en":"And so, actually, it kind of feels like I've always really loved that mentality, and now finally capability is catching up to that.","zh":"所以其实感觉像是，我一直特别喜欢这种心态，而现在能力终于追上来了。"},{"i":443,"s":2605.71,"e":2617.95,"en":"But the thing I really care about is that someone needs to look after the or have core accountability for, is this product being used by users?","zh":"但我真正在意的是，得有人来照看、或者说对这件事有核心担责：这个产品真的有用户在用吗？"},{"i":444,"s":2617.95,"e":2619.23,"en":"Is it something that people want?","zh":"它是不是人们想要的东西？"},{"i":445,"s":2619.43,"e":2622.43,"en":"Is it uh high quality, is it effective?","zh":"它质量高吗？它有效吗？"},{"i":446,"s":2623.04,"e":2632.16,"en":"And whether that person is like an engineer, a designer, a PM, or whomever, like someone is the DRI, and then whatever work needs to be done to make that possible.","zh":"至于这个人是工程师、设计师、PM 还是别的什么，总得有一个 DRI，然后为了实现这件事该做的活儿，"},{"i":447,"s":2632.96,"e":2636.44,"en":"You know, certainly people can pick it up based on their affinity, based on their capability.","zh":"大家完全可以按各自的兴趣、按各自的能力去接。"},{"i":448,"s":2636.92,"e":2645.96,"en":"But I like a team that doesn't really mind what the boundaries are between individual roles, but everyone's just sort of focused on making the outcome happen.","zh":"但我喜欢那种不太在意角色之间边界的团队，所有人只是专注于把结果做出来。"},{"i":449,"s":2646.57,"e":2652.09,"en":"The converse of this is I also really love like the craft aspects of like being a PM.","zh":"反过来说，我也真的很喜欢当 PM 这门手艺本身。"},{"i":450,"s":2652.13,"e":2663.36,"en":"Like there are so many aspects to PM craft that I know folks like Shreyas or maybe Marty Cagan or Shishir, like all these people have really espoused that I think are are wonderful.","zh":"PM 这门手艺有太多方面，像 Shreyas、Marty Cagan、Shishir 这些人一直倡导的那些，我觉得都特别棒。"},{"i":451,"s":2663.8,"e":2670.91,"en":"And sometimes, um, maybe some of these questions or come from Wait, I I so love the craft of my domain.","zh":"有时候这些问题可能来自这样一种心情：等等，我这么热爱自己这个领域的手艺。"},{"i":452,"s":2671.39,"e":2679.47,"en":"By taking this more fluid approach to teamwork and collaboration to get something done, do I lose out on getting better and polishing my craft?","zh":"如果用这种更流动的方式做团队协作、把事情做成，我是不是就失去了把手艺练得更精、打磨得更好的机会？"},{"i":453,"s":2680.02,"e":2681.98,"en":"And I truly don't have an answer for that question.","zh":"这个问题我真的没有答案。"},{"i":454,"s":2682.1,"e":2695.91,"en":"I think it's like something we're all experiencing together, which is some pieces of our craft are actually getting abstracted by models being able to do it really effectively, maybe better than then individuals can, and your craft moves from.","zh":"我觉得这是我们所有人正在共同经历的：我们手艺里的某些部分，正在被模型抽象掉，因为模型做得非常好，也许比个人做得更好，于是你的手艺就从"},{"i":455,"s":2696.43,"e":2703.59,"en":"you know, being able to do that very specific task you did in the past, to now applying it to some other part of the product or the discipline.","zh":"过去能做那个非常具体的任务，变成把它应用到产品或这个专业的其他部分上。"},{"i":456,"s":2704.04,"e":2718.77,"en":"But yeah, that that is still a question I'm thinking about, which is how do I balance my desire to be part of a team and use these tools and feel so um compelled by how effective one can be now with all these products.","zh":"但是的，这仍然是我在想的问题：我怎么平衡——一方面我想成为团队的一员，用这些工具，为现在借助这些产品一个人能有多高效而感到振奋，"},{"i":457,"s":2718.93,"e":2728.09,"en":"with my love of like the, yeah, it's it's really fun handwriting code for an engineer all the time, and one doesn't really do that anymore.","zh":"另一方面又爱着那些东西，比如对工程师来说，一直手写代码其实很有意思，而现在大家基本不这么干了。"},{"i":458,"s":2728.48,"e":2729.84,"en":"Yes, that's where I was gonna go.","zh":"是的，我正想往这个方向说。"},{"i":459,"s":2729.84,"e":2734.68,"en":"It's just like unbelievable how different the engineering role is now.","zh":"工程师这个角色现在变得有多不一样，简直难以置信。"},{"i":460,"s":2734.68,"e":2735.52,"en":"Yeah.","zh":"是啊。"},{"i":461,"s":2735.52,"e":2739.4,"en":"It's like you used to write code all day, that was your job, and that is no longer your job.","zh":"以前你一整天都在写代码，那就是你的工作，而现在那不再是你的工作了。"},{"i":462,"s":2739.73,"e":2739.89,"en":"Yeah.","zh":"是的。"},{"i":463,"s":2739.89,"e":2740.81,"en":"And that happens so quickly.","zh":"而且发生得这么快。"},{"i":464,"s":2741.57,"e":2744.69,"en":"Like, I I think people mourn like the flow state of writing code.","zh":"我觉得有人会怀念写代码时的心流状态。"},{"i":465,"s":2744.85,"e":2745.21,"en":"Yeah.","zh":"是啊。"},{"i":466,"s":2745.21,"e":2748.33,"en":"Manually yourself versus now what what one does.","zh":"亲手一行行写，和现在做的事情相比。"},{"i":467,"s":2748.33,"e":2754.01,"en":"But I think it is a um, yeah, it's a it's a it's a tough transition.","zh":"但我觉得这是一个，是的，这是一个很难的转变。"},{"i":468,"s":2754.49,"e":2759.69,"en":"Yeah, and you know some people love it, some people don't, and that's a whole other topic.","zh":"是的，有人喜欢，有人不喜欢，那又是另一个话题了。"},{"i":469,"s":2759.93,"e":2763.53,"en":"Kind of along those lines, something I'd like to ask people at the frontier of AI is.","zh":"顺着这个思路，有个问题我很想问在 AI 前沿的人。"},{"i":470,"s":2764.0,"e":2768.52,"en":"Where do you think human brains will continue to be valuable in in the future?","zh":"你觉得未来人脑还会在哪些地方继续有价值？"},{"i":471,"s":2768.88,"e":2772.12,"en":"It's impossible to predict long term, will will we need humans?","zh":"长期没法预测，我们还会需要人类吗？"},{"i":472,"s":2772.52,"e":2778.12,"en":"Hopefully, but I'd say in the near, I don't know, next couple years, just like, where do you think human brains will continue to be most valuable?","zh":"希望会吧，但就说近期，比如未来这几年，你觉得人脑在哪些方面还最有价值？"},{"i":473,"s":2778.96,"e":2786.52,"en":"I think humans will continue being the most valuable, as a, certainly as a um like an entity of accountability.","zh":"我觉得人会继续是最有价值的，尤其是作为承担责任的那个主体。"},{"i":474,"s":2787.0,"e":2789.56,"en":"So, who ultimately owns the outcome here?","zh":"也就是说，最终谁对结果负责？"},{"i":475,"s":2789.92,"e":2794.96,"en":"In some ways, you can think of your agent that you're working with as like your your report.","zh":"某种程度上，你可以把一起工作的 agent 看成是你的下属。"},{"i":476,"s":2795.52,"e":2798.8,"en":"um, ultimately, who owns like what's what was the end product?","zh":"最终谁对成品负责？"},{"i":477,"s":2798.96,"e":2799.6,"en":"Was it high quality?","zh":"质量够不够好？"},{"i":478,"s":2799.8,"e":2802.16,"en":"Was it the thing that you wanted it to do and say like that?","zh":"它做出来、说出来的，是不是你想要的那样？"},{"i":479,"s":2802.78,"e":2815.86,"en":"That will certainly remain a a person, at least at least for now, and especially in industries and places that are um highly regulated or require like a direct human interface like that, that makes a ton of sense to me.","zh":"这一点肯定还会由人来承担，至少现在是这样，尤其在高度监管、或者需要人直接对接的行业和场合，这对我来说非常合理。"},{"i":480,"s":2816.44,"e":2819.52,"en":"I think the human brain is also really valuable for expression.","zh":"我觉得人脑在表达上也非常有价值。"},{"i":481,"s":2820.2,"e":2832.64,"en":"I'd mentioned earlier that analogy of uh software is not like real estate, it is more like a film where you could put money and a great film does not come out, like the greatest films are not the ones with the biggest budgets.","zh":"我前面提过那个类比：软件不像房地产，更像电影——你砸钱进去，未必出得来好片，最伟大的电影往往不是预算最大的那些。"},{"i":482,"s":2833.1,"e":2843.9,"en":"And given that there's a certain, there's a certain artistry and opinionation and expression in building software where you feel like there is some authorship by by a person or a group of people.","zh":"而做软件里有一种手艺感、观点和表达，你能感觉到背后有某个人或某群人的作者印记。"},{"i":483,"s":2844.34,"e":2846.7,"en":"And that part remains to me so human.","zh":"在我看来这部分太有人味了。"},{"i":484,"s":2846.98,"e":2852.7,"en":"Like what you choose to build and how it feels feels like such a such a human question.","zh":"你选择造什么、它给人什么感觉，这些都特别像是属于人的问题。"},{"i":485,"s":2853.46,"e":2859.96,"en":"um, I also think the human brain continues to be valuable, and like how we care for each other and relate to one another.","zh":"我还觉得人脑在我们怎么彼此关照、怎么相处这件事上会继续有价值。"},{"i":486,"s":2860.68,"e":2867.64,"en":"um, that piece of my work has remained so human, and remained actually, has actually become more important than ever.","zh":"我工作里的这部分一直很有人味，而且实际上变得比以往任何时候都重要。"},{"i":487,"s":2868.1,"e":2879.94,"en":"The part where you talk to other people on your team, and collectively figure out how you can be enthusiastic about a area, how you learn and work together, how you elevate each other's ambitions.","zh":"就是你跟团队里的人交流，一起弄明白怎么对某个领域保持热情、怎么一起学习和协作、怎么把彼此的抱负抬高。"},{"i":488,"s":2881.18,"e":2885.18,"en":"All of that feels and remains such a human thing to do.","zh":"所有这些一直都是很人性的事。"},{"i":489,"s":2885.3,"e":2889.7,"en":"Yeah, I think the human brain will will continue to be so valuable in that regard.","zh":"对，我觉得人脑在这方面会继续非常有价值。"},{"i":490,"s":2890.22,"e":2897.71,"en":"That said, I you know can't predict I don't know what'll happen with the models, but those pieces feel to me to be incredibly incredibly human.","zh":"话虽如此，我也预测不了模型会走到哪一步，但这些部分在我看来是极其极其属于人的。"},{"i":491,"s":2897.91,"e":2898.63,"en":"Mm hmm.","zh":"嗯。"},{"i":492,"s":2898.83,"e":2899.51,"en":"I love that answer.","zh":"我很喜欢这个回答。"},{"i":493,"s":2900.71,"e":2907.7,"en":"There's this idea that you talked about this idea of the this overhang of what AI is capable of and what we're actually uh, doing with it.","zh":"你之前谈到过一个想法，就是 AI 的能力和我们实际用它做的事之间有很大落差。"},{"i":494,"s":2907.9,"e":2911.94,"en":"People are always, like it feels like one of the biggest gaps is like, OK, what should I do with it?","zh":"大家好像总觉得最大的差距之一就是：好，那我到底该拿它做什么？"},{"i":495,"s":2912.3,"e":2916.86,"en":"I'm curious, what are some ways that you use AI in your work?","zh":"我很好奇，你在工作中有哪些用 AI 的方式？"},{"i":496,"s":2917.44,"e":2920.32,"en":"That may inspire people like, oh wow, I didn't think about using it that.","zh":"可能会给大家一些启发，让人觉得，哇，我没想过还能这么用。"},{"i":497,"s":2920.72,"e":2922.2,"en":"Like, there's kind of two buckets here.","zh":"这里大概分两类。"},{"i":498,"s":2922.2,"e":2929.2,"en":"One is just like, what's like the most, how your PM job has changed most, thanks to AI, that you're just like, okay, now I use AI for the stuff.","zh":"一类是，因为 AI，你的 PM 工作变化最大的地方是什么，就是那种「现在这些活我都交给 AI 了」。"},{"i":499,"s":2929.73,"e":2933.61,"en":"And then what's like, is there any like super interesting creative uses of AI recently?","zh":"另一类是，最近有没有什么特别有意思、很有创意的 AI 用法？"},{"i":500,"s":2933.61,"e":2935.05,"en":"They're like, oh yeah, you should try this.","zh":"就是那种「对，你真该试试这个」。"},{"i":501,"s":2935.45,"e":2943.37,"en":"One of the most exciting ways that I use AI in work is um, actually build sites all the time now.","zh":"我在工作中用 AI 最让我兴奋的方式之一，是我现在一直在做 sites。"},{"i":502,"s":2943.53,"e":2944.85,"en":"I don't know if you've tried building sites.","zh":"不知道你有没有试过做 sites。"},{"i":503,"s":2945.17,"e":2945.57,"en":"I haven't.","zh":"没试过。"},{"i":504,"s":2945.57,"e":2946.13,"en":"Talk about sites.","zh":"讲讲 sites 吧。"},{"i":505,"s":2946.29,"e":2949.57,"en":"Sites is a really fun amazing product.","zh":"Sites 是个特别好玩、特别棒的产品。"},{"i":506,"s":2950.17,"e":2954.01,"en":"um, you can basically build a site, certainly in work as a presentational artifact.","zh":"你基本上可以做一个 site，工作里当然可以当成展示用的产物。"},{"i":507,"s":2954.39,"e":2957.11,"en":"But I also build sites for literally anything.","zh":"但我做 site 也真的什么都做。"},{"i":508,"s":2957.35,"e":2964.91,"en":"I built a site um for the team as like a as a game, um, where we all played a a game together using a site, cause sites have a database.","zh":"我给团队做过一个 site，当成一个游戏，我们一起用这个 site 玩，因为 site 是带数据库的。"},{"i":509,"s":2965.39,"e":2968.75,"en":"uh, you can build site, I actually built site, because I went on a backpacking trip recently.","zh":"你可以做 site，我最近就做了一个，因为我前阵子去徒步旅行了。"},{"i":510,"s":2969.19,"e":2972.99,"en":"I built a site of the route that like tracked the elevation of everywhere we were going.","zh":"我做了个路线的 site，能追踪我们要去的每个地方的海拔。"},{"i":511,"s":2973.15,"e":2975.55,"en":"Everyone on our our trip like inputted all their food.","zh":"同行的每个人都把自己带的吃的录了进去。"},{"i":512,"s":2976.21,"e":2978.33,"en":"um, it was like super fast and effective.","zh":"特别快，也特别有效。"},{"i":513,"s":2978.53,"e":2987.97,"en":"Sites kind of realized the dream of like valuable personal software that Alan Kay, you know, flagged in the in the sixties of like the true personal computer is one that has personal software.","zh":"Sites 某种程度上实现了 Alan Kay 在六十年代提出的那个梦想——有价值的个人软件，真正的个人电脑应该是有个人软件的。"},{"i":514,"s":2988.42,"e":2991.9,"en":"In some ways, sites are like the tangible way to make that possible.","zh":"某种意义上，sites 就是让这件事变成现实的具体方式。"},{"i":515,"s":2992.5,"e":2999.82,"en":"We'd all once dreamed of like making personal software, and certainly people with tools like Notion, et cetera, try with all these blocks to configure.","zh":"我们都曾梦想过做个人软件，当然用 Notion 之类工具的人也在拿各种 block 去拼、去配置，"},{"i":516,"s":3000.34,"e":3003.26,"en":"What that could be, but with a site, it is literally a prompt.","zh":"看看能配出什么来，但用 site 的话，真的就是一句 prompt。"},{"i":517,"s":3003.54,"e":3010.46,"en":"I literally with a prompt say like build me this exact tool that I need to get this thing done, and it just does it.","zh":"我就用一句 prompt 说：给我做一个能把这件事搞定的工具，它就直接做出来了。"},{"i":518,"s":3011.12,"e":3012.0,"en":"um, they're shareable.","zh":"而且可以分享。"},{"i":519,"s":3012.72,"e":3019.84,"en":"uh, they can use, they can auto update, you can use like internal data to build like a dashboard, for example, with lots of metrics.","zh":"它们还能自动更新，你也可以用内部数据做个仪表盘，比如放上很多指标。"},{"i":520,"s":3020.44,"e":3029.29,"en":"And rather than like painstakingly laboring over some sort of like slide deck, a site is just a way more dynamic surface for presentation.","zh":"与其吭哧吭哧折腾一份 slide deck，site 是一个动态得多的展示载体。"},{"i":521,"s":3029.57,"e":3030.77,"en":"How to use a site?","zh":"怎么用 site？"},{"i":522,"s":3030.81,"e":3032.85,"en":"Do you have to do anything special, or you tell it make create a site?","zh":"需要做什么特别的操作吗，还是直接跟它说「创建一个 site」？"},{"i":523,"s":3032.85,"e":3038.95,"en":"In Codex, be like create a site that, create a site, um, is a I know, is a mafia game for my team?","zh":"在 Codex 里就说：创建一个 site，做一个给我团队玩的杀人游戏。"},{"i":524,"s":3039.03,"e":3040.15,"en":"And it will just do it.","zh":"它就直接做出来了。"},{"i":525,"s":3040.55,"e":3043.83,"en":"And like like I'm thinking capital S site, but it doesn't matter, I imagine.","zh":"我脑子里想的是大写 S 的 Site，不过我猜这不重要。"},{"i":526,"s":3044.27,"e":3045.35,"en":"It just knows what sites are.","zh":"它就知道 sites 是什么。"},{"i":527,"s":3045.35,"e":3050.51,"en":"So, yeah, cause it used to be, here's a here's some source code, go figure out where to deploy it.","zh":"对，因为以前是：这是一段源码，你自己去想办法找地方部署。"},{"i":528,"s":3050.59,"e":3050.91,"en":"Yeah.","zh":"对。"},{"i":529,"s":3050.91,"e":3053.27,"en":"And what you're saying here is it just hosted for you.","zh":"而你说的是，它直接帮你托管好了。"},{"i":530,"s":3053.47,"e":3054.19,"en":"Hosted for you.","zh":"直接帮你托管。"},{"i":531,"s":3054.27,"e":3058.94,"en":"You can choose whether it's public, you can choose whether it's with your team, or choose whether it's private to you.","zh":"你可以选择它是公开的、还是团队内可见的、还是只有你自己能看。"},{"i":532,"s":3059.5,"e":3060.3,"en":"uh, they're great.","zh":"它们很棒。"},{"i":533,"s":3060.42,"e":3075.32,"en":"Dave, the easy reach of building a site all the time has changed what my day to day looks like, which often in in previous worlds used to look like creating lots of artifacts, like docs and sheets and whatever it might be. Now I just make sites all the time.","zh":"随手就能做 site 这件事，改变了我每天的工作样貌，以前多半是产出一堆东西，文档啊表格啊之类的，现在我就一直在做 sites。"},{"i":534,"s":3075.48,"e":3080.28,"en":"And you could do that through, I imagine, work or can you do it through through all the surfaces?","zh":"我猜通过 work 也能做？还是所有界面都能做？"},{"i":535,"s":3080.44,"e":3081.88,"en":"Codex, work chat, you can do it through work.","zh":"Codex、work chat，通过 work 就可以做。"},{"i":536,"s":3082.04,"e":3087.28,"en":"You can do it through Codex, you can do it in the web, you can do it on mobile, you can do it anywhere.","zh":"可以在 Codex 里做，可以在网页上做，可以在手机上做，怎么都行。"},{"i":537,"s":3087.28,"e":3090.12,"en":"OK, I just kicked off a create a site about Tara Seshan.","zh":"好，我刚让它做了一个关于 Tara Seshan 的 site。"},{"i":538,"s":3091.0,"e":3091.12,"en":"Great.","zh":"很好。"},{"i":539,"s":3091.16,"e":3092.56,"en":"Is that how you pronounce your last name by the way?","zh":"顺便问一句，你的姓是这么读吗？"},{"i":540,"s":3092.64,"e":3093.28,"en":"I haven't asked.","zh":"我一直没问过。"},{"i":541,"s":3093.32,"e":3096.08,"en":"uh, Tara sta- station like station.","zh":"Tara Se-shan，那个音像 station。"},{"i":542,"s":3096.4,"e":3098.16,"en":"Station, OK, cool, OK, cool.","zh":"像 station，好，明白了，明白了。"},{"i":543,"s":3098.16,"e":3098.68,"en":"hmm-hmm.","zh":"嗯嗯。"},{"i":544,"s":3098.88,"e":3101.52,"en":"um, Sites, OK, any other quick tips?","zh":"Sites，好，还有别的快捷小技巧吗？"},{"i":545,"s":3102.43,"e":3107.19,"en":"uh, while we're on this topic for people, because that was a great tip, because I don't think a lot of people know about sites, that's um very useful.","zh":"趁着聊这个话题给大家讲讲，因为刚才那个技巧很棒，我觉得很多人还不知道 sites，非常有用。"},{"i":546,"s":3107.19,"e":3108.19,"en":"Yeah, sites are awesome.","zh":"对，sites 很棒。"},{"i":547,"s":3108.43,"e":3112.03,"en":"um, the other thing I really love is using Visualize in Codex.","zh":"我另外特别喜欢的是在 Codex 里用 Visualize。"},{"i":548,"s":3112.07,"e":3113.15,"en":"Have you use slash Visualize?","zh":"你用过斜杠 Visualize 吗？"},{"i":549,"s":3114.43,"e":3114.79,"en":"No.","zh":"没有。"},{"i":550,"s":3114.95,"e":3116.95,"en":"Oh, slash visualize is incredibly exciting.","zh":"哦，斜杠 visualize 特别让人兴奋。"},{"i":551,"s":3117.15,"e":3122.27,"en":"Ask, you can just do slash visualize, visualize my ChatGPT usage until now or something like that.","zh":"你可以直接打斜杠 visualize，比如「可视化我到目前为止的 ChatGPT 使用情况」之类的。"},{"i":552,"s":3122.63,"e":3127.35,"en":"And it will pull in like all the things that you've done, and create like an amazing visualization for it.","zh":"它就会把你做过的所有事情都拉进来，然后生成一个特别棒的可视化。"},{"i":553,"s":3127.79,"e":3139.23,"en":"The number of times that I've been thinking about how do I not only pull in a bunch of charts and data, but present them in a way that is understandable and useful for the story I'm trying to tell, has been infinite.","zh":"我无数次在想，怎么才能不光是把一堆图表和数据拉进来，还能用一种别人看得懂、对我要讲的故事有用的方式呈现出来。"},{"i":554,"s":3139.75,"e":3141.91,"en":"And visualize makes that incredibly simple.","zh":"而 visualize 让这件事变得极其简单。"},{"i":555,"s":3142.15,"e":3145.03,"en":"It is like surprisingly delightful to use visualize.","zh":"用 visualize 的体验意外地让人愉快。"},{"i":556,"s":3145.63,"e":3152.76,"en":"It's just like, it's just these are such good examples of there's so much power here we don't even know about or understand, and that's the challenge you have here.","zh":"这些都是特别好的例子，说明这里面有太多能力我们根本不知道、也不理解，而这正是你们面临的挑战。"},{"i":557,"s":3152.84,"e":3154.12,"en":"Help us, for sure, for sure.","zh":"帮帮我们，确实确实。"},{"i":558,"s":3154.12,"e":3155.12,"en":"Help us know all these things.","zh":"帮我们了解这些东西。"},{"i":559,"s":3155.2,"e":3157.24,"en":"That's why podcast like this are also useful.","zh":"所以这样的播客也很有用。"},{"i":560,"s":3157.68,"e":3158.72,"en":"Can't put it all in the product.","zh":"没法把所有东西都塞进产品里。"},{"i":561,"s":3159.44,"e":3161.0,"en":"uh, I'm gonna go in a totally different direction.","zh":"我要换个完全不同的方向。"},{"i":562,"s":3161.2,"e":3162.04,"en":"I wanna talk about writing.","zh":"我想聊聊写作。"},{"i":563,"s":3162.98,"e":3166.5,"en":"I asked uh Brie Wolfson who knows you well, what to ask you.","zh":"我问了很了解你的 Brie Wolfson，该问你点什么。"},{"i":564,"s":3166.86,"e":3172.82,"en":"uh, funny enough, she suggested questions for the previous podcast, uh, conversation I did with Adam Group, Adam Ward from Gusher.","zh":"有意思的是，上一期我跟 Gusto 的 Adam Ward 那次播客对谈，她也帮我出过问题。"},{"i":565,"s":3173.25,"e":3176.65,"en":"uh, so she said, OK, you should ask her about writing slash thinking.","zh":"她说，好，你应该问问她写作和思考的事。"},{"i":566,"s":3176.97,"e":3178.81,"en":"A Tara brief is iconic.","zh":"Tara 的 brief 堪称经典。"},{"i":567,"s":3180.59,"e":3191.35,"en":"Help us understand just uh what makes your writing your briefs iconic, and any tips that might be helpful for people that are maybe trying to get better at writing and writing.","zh":"帮我们理解一下，是什么让你的写作、你的 brief 这么经典，以及对那些想提升写作、想写好文档的人有什么建议。"},{"i":568,"s":3191.94,"e":3192.46,"en":"Documents.","zh":"写文档。"},{"i":569,"s":3193.06,"e":3196.06,"en":"I really strongly believe that I do two types of writing at work.","zh":"我非常坚信，我在工作中写的是两类东西。"},{"i":570,"s":3196.14,"e":3199.54,"en":"One is writing as thinking, and the other is writing as reporting.","zh":"一类是把写作当作思考，另一类是把写作当作汇报。"},{"i":571,"s":3199.78,"e":3209.12,"en":"Writing as thinking is me writing a like a brief about why we should build certain product, or why we should take a certain strategy, or why like maybe a a spicy take.","zh":"写作当思考，是我写一份 brief，讲我们为什么该做某个产品、为什么该采取某个策略，或者抛出一个比较尖锐的观点。"},{"i":572,"s":3209.68,"e":3221.76,"en":"um, but writing as reporting is things like, oh, I'm summarizing the status of what our team has been up to this week, and I'm sending over a report about it, or this is our plan for this particular launch or announcement or something like that.","zh":"而写作当汇报，是比如我总结团队这周的进展、发一份报告出去，或者说这是我们某次发布或公告的计划之类的。"},{"i":573,"s":3222.26,"e":3229.82,"en":"Writing as reporting, I happily automate, or I use I use the models all the time to make that as as simple as it can be.","zh":"写作当汇报，我很乐意自动化，我一直用模型把它做得尽可能省事。"},{"i":574,"s":3229.98,"e":3233.7,"en":"But writing as thinking is something I never will automate.","zh":"但写作当思考，我永远不会自动化。"},{"i":575,"s":3234.37,"e":3245.25,"en":"I really strongly believe that the, at least for me, the act of going through and outlining something, turning it into some level of prose, cutting it and editing it.","zh":"我非常坚信，至少对我来说，把一件事列成提纲、写成像样的文字、再删减和打磨的这个过程，"},{"i":576,"s":3245.95,"e":3252.39,"en":"Continuing to iterate on it is one of the most important steps for me to get my ideas in line.","zh":"以及不断迭代它，是我把自己的想法理顺最重要的步骤之一。"},{"i":577,"s":3252.75,"e":3258.36,"en":"I think most people actually uh will paint with a really broad brush.","zh":"我觉得大多数人其实会一刀切。"},{"i":578,"s":3258.48,"e":3262.6,"en":"Like, I will never use thos- use the models for writing, or I always use the models for writing.","zh":"比如：我绝不用模型写作，或者我写作永远用模型。"},{"i":579,"s":3262.6,"e":3265.2,"en":"And actually to me, like that bro- both those broad brushes are wrong.","zh":"而在我看来，这两种一刀切都是错的。"},{"i":580,"s":3265.64,"e":3269.04,"en":"I think you should use the models as much as possible for writing as reporting.","zh":"我觉得写作当汇报时，应该尽可能多用模型。"},{"i":581,"s":3269.62,"e":3276.06,"en":"And in as much as you think with writing, as I really do, and I think a lot of people do, you should not use it.","zh":"而只要你像我一样是靠写作来思考的——我确实是，我觉得很多人也是——那就不该用它。"},{"i":582,"s":3276.06,"e":3277.86,"en":"Yeah, you shouldn't replace your thinking with it.","zh":"对，不该用它来替代你的思考。"},{"i":583,"s":3278.14,"e":3282.38,"en":"But my briefs in the past, um, because I write so much, um, as a way of thinking.","zh":"但我过去写的那些 brief，因为我写得很多，是把写作当成思考的方式。"},{"i":584,"s":3283.11,"e":3293.47,"en":"uh, is that I will write a, I will like go into a hole, write a brief for a new idea or a or a product, spend a ton of time refining.","zh":"就是我会一头扎进去，为一个新想法或新产品写一份 brief，花大量时间打磨"},{"i":585,"s":3294.06,"e":3300.5,"en":"That particular idea, shop it around with people, and have them attack the ideas in it as much as possible and poke holes.","zh":"那个具体的想法，然后拿去跟人交流，让他们尽可能地攻击里面的观点、挑毛病。"},{"i":586,"s":3300.54,"e":3304.14,"en":"Make it stronger, and then take it to the next person, and do the same thing.","zh":"把它变得更强，然后再拿给下一个人，重复同样的过程。"},{"i":587,"s":3304.6,"e":3315.0,"en":"And so, at Stripe, this is something I did many many many many times over, whether that was like to kick off a new product area, or to suggest a big change in direction.","zh":"在 Stripe，这件事我做过很多很多次，无论是要启动一个新的产品方向，还是要提议一次大的方向调整。"},{"i":588,"s":3315.9,"e":3319.38,"en":"Or to analyze a problem, and suggest a path forward.","zh":"或者是分析一个问题，然后给出一条推进路径。"},{"i":589,"s":3319.94,"e":3331.16,"en":"And Stripe is incredibly oriented as a writing culture, and there are many people like Jeff Weinstein, who are also very into writing and sharing briefs at Stripe.","zh":"Stripe 极其崇尚写作文化，公司里有很多人，比如 Jeff Weinstein，也非常热衷于写 brief、分享 brief。"},{"i":590,"s":3331.16,"e":3334.88,"en":"Stripe is one of the few places where like a brief will go viral um inside the company.","zh":"Stripe 是少有的那种、一份 brief 会在公司内部刷屏的地方。"},{"i":591,"s":3335.04,"e":3342.78,"en":"And so writing is thinking there is really prized, and that's where I did like the majority of of that writing work.","zh":"所以「写作即思考」在那里非常被看重，我大部分的写作工作也是在那儿完成的。"},{"i":592,"s":3343.62,"e":3349.82,"en":"um, at OpenAI, I think I wou-, I still write as thinking all the time.","zh":"在 OpenAI，我现在依然一直在用写作来思考。"},{"i":593,"s":3350.5,"e":3360.3,"en":"um, but the shareable artifact here is not really a long doc or a sort of proof of work in that way.","zh":"但这里可以拿出去分享的产物，并不是一份长文档，也不是那种意义上的「工作量证明」。"},{"i":594,"s":3360.78,"e":3371.38,"en":"um, partially because times have changed, and a long doc is not a signal that you thought through something, because you can easily produce a long doc that indicates that you haven't.","zh":"一部分原因是时代变了——长文档已经不能证明你想清楚了，因为你可以轻松产出一份长文档，反而暴露你没想清楚。"},{"i":595,"s":3371.69,"e":3383.13,"en":"And so, actually, the the point, maybe one of the biggest changes I've experienced personally in my day to day, which has been a a big jar- jarring change, is that I used to think in a document.","zh":"所以我个人日常里体验到的最大变化之一，一个相当冲击性的变化，就是：我以前是在文档里思考。"},{"i":596,"s":3383.41,"e":3391.57,"en":"and then do some translation of that into a presentation artifact, and that would be my indication that I thought through a problem, and this is what we're gonna do, and the team moves in that direction.","zh":"然后把它翻译成一份演示材料，那就是我想清楚了一个问题的证明——这就是我们要做的事，团队照这个方向走。"},{"i":597,"s":3392.11,"e":3396.63,"en":"And now I am way more on Mocks Not Docs or Prototypes Not Docs.","zh":"而现在我更信奉「要 mock 不要 doc」，或者说「要原型不要文档」。"},{"i":598,"s":3397.39,"e":3402.19,"en":"And if I have something that people can try and interact with, or even better, I have like results.","zh":"如果我拿得出一个别人可以试用、可以交互的东西，或者更好——我手上有结果。"},{"i":599,"s":3402.84,"e":3404.64,"en":"Where we tried this, we ran an A/B.","zh":"比如我们试过了，跑了个 A/B。"},{"i":600,"s":3404.68,"e":3405.56,"en":"Here's like the results.","zh":"这是结果。"},{"i":601,"s":3405.72,"e":3407.32,"en":"This is why I think we should like go in this direction.","zh":"这就是我认为我们该往这个方向走的原因。"},{"i":602,"s":3407.96,"e":3412.2,"en":"That is a way better communication tool than like the the doc itself.","zh":"那比文档本身要好用得多，是更好的沟通工具。"},{"i":603,"s":3412.69,"e":3417.85,"en":"And so, I still write hundreds of docs all the time, but I do it for me.","zh":"所以我还是一直在写几百份文档，但我是写给自己的。"},{"i":604,"s":3418.41,"e":3423.93,"en":"um, And I no longer do it for other people really, like that no longer is the best way to to talk and communicate.","zh":"我基本上不再为别人写了，因为那已经不再是最好的表达和沟通方式。"},{"i":605,"s":3424.37,"e":3430.13,"en":"That is probably the biggest change I've experienced personally in um this era versus the previous era.","zh":"这大概是我个人在这个时代相比上一个时代所经历的最大变化。"},{"i":606,"s":3430.41,"e":3431.33,"en":"It is so interesting.","zh":"太有意思了。"},{"i":607,"s":3432.01,"e":3445.77,"en":"I really like your tip of getting tons of feedback on a doc, like, you know, it sounds obvious, but you know, you can get to an iconic doc slash brief by just cheating almost, and getting lots of feedback on it as you're iterating it. Yes. To make it stronger.","zh":"我很喜欢你说的那招——就一份文档收集大量反馈。听起来好像是废话，但你确实可以靠这种近乎「作弊」的方式做出一份标杆级的文档或 brief：一边迭代一边收集大量反馈。是的。让它变得更强。"},{"i":608,"s":3445.81,"e":3446.53,"en":"and stronger and stronger.","zh":"越来越强。"},{"i":609,"s":3446.97,"e":3457.85,"en":"Versus like, cool, here it is first time, and it's barely gonna be— I previously had a manager who told me that the right thing to always do is write a doc to 70 percent completion, and then take it to the people that you need buy in from.","zh":"而不是说，好，第一版就这样了，还没打磨过就——我以前有位主管跟我说，正确的做法永远是：把文档写到 70% 的完成度，然后拿去找那些你需要争取支持的人。"},{"i":610,"s":3458.2,"e":3460.08,"en":"And get it from seventy percent to a hundred percent.","zh":"让他们帮你把它从 70% 推到 100%。"},{"i":611,"s":3460.76,"e":3468.84,"en":"And that still is like a thing that I I do all the time, because very few great people want to interact with like a perfectly polished.","zh":"这件事我到现在还一直在做，因为很少有厉害的人愿意面对一份打磨得完美无缺的东西。"},{"i":612,"s":3469.42,"e":3473.14,"en":"Finished idea, like a perfectly polished idea, their new ideas just like bounce off of it.","zh":"一个成型的想法——一个打磨得完美的想法，他们的新点子会直接被弹开。"},{"i":613,"s":3473.38,"e":3480.06,"en":"Versus something that has more cracks and more um rough edges that they too can polish with you together.","zh":"相比之下，一个还有裂缝、还有毛边的东西，他们才能跟你一起打磨。"},{"i":614,"s":3480.52,"e":3488.2,"en":"And I think that um like bringing people into the process that way, where like a doc is like an underlying artifact for that, is one of the best ways to collaborate that I found.","zh":"我觉得用这种方式把人拉进过程里、把文档当作底层载体，是我找到的最好的协作方式之一。"},{"i":615,"s":3488.32,"e":3496.58,"en":"How do you think about uh AI brain rot, and starting to over rely on AI, this just a challenge everybody's gonna have.","zh":"你怎么看 AI 带来的「脑子退化」，以及开始过度依赖 AI？这大概是每个人都会遇到的挑战。"},{"i":616,"s":3496.58,"e":3503.1,"en":"Why not use this magic to help look at something, and then we start to lose our ability to write.","zh":"为什么不用这个魔法帮我们看东西呢——然后我们就开始丧失写作的能力。"},{"i":617,"s":3503.66,"e":3504.38,"en":"Read long documents.","zh":"还有读长文档的能力。"},{"i":618,"s":3504.66,"e":3507.9,"en":"Is there anything you do that you are trying to avoid that?","zh":"你有做什么事情来避免这一点吗？"},{"i":619,"s":3508.3,"e":3518.99,"en":"Yeah, I think this writing is thinking discipline is one of the main pieces that I employ in my day to day to make sure I'm not overly atrophy my my thinking abilities.","zh":"有，我觉得「写作即思考」这条纪律，就是我日常中确保自己的思考能力不过度退化的主要手段之一。"},{"i":620,"s":3519.39,"e":3526.15,"en":"I think I will again outsource all writing is reporting as much as possible to the model, but writing is thinking, I have to do myself.","zh":"所有「写作即汇报」的部分，我会尽量外包给模型；但「写作即思考」的部分，我必须自己做。"},{"i":621,"s":3526.84,"e":3536.76,"en":"And I have this like personal um belief that if I'm going to make someone read my document, I have to at least read it first that number of times.","zh":"我还有一个个人信条：如果我要让别人读我的文档，那我自己至少得先读那么多遍。"},{"i":622,"s":3537.55,"e":3547.83,"en":"um, or I I think about this in meetings too, that if I'm gonna call a meeting with with a set of people, I need to have prepped the collective amount of time that people are going to spend in that meeting before the meeting.","zh":"开会也一样——如果我要召集一群人开会，我得在会前投入的准备时间，等于大家在这场会上花掉的时间总和。"},{"i":623,"s":3548.39,"e":3560.87,"en":"And so, when it comes to like keeping my thinking sharp, like I do that writing for the document myself first, and make sure I've invested like the collective amount of time I expect people to read it at least in writing it and producing it.","zh":"所以说到保持思考锋利，我会先自己把文档写出来，并确保我在写和产出它上面投入的时间，至少等于我预期大家读它所花的总时间。"},{"i":624,"s":3561.21,"e":3571.73,"en":"And I don't really rely on the model either for polishing my prose, which I don't think it it really it really does, or um especially not in like generating the the first version.","zh":"我也基本不靠模型来润色我的文笔——我觉得它其实做得并不好——尤其不会让它生成第一版。"},{"i":625,"s":3572.2,"e":3581.44,"en":"But I do the, I do of course have the model help me a lot, when it's like summarization or like translation of content from one format to the other all the time.","zh":"但我当然会让模型帮我很多忙，比如做总结，或者把内容从一种格式转换成另一种，这类事一直在用。"},{"i":626,"s":3582.14,"e":3588.94,"en":"So what I'm hearing is uh write the idea, the brief, the plan yourself as a human.","zh":"所以我听到的是：想法、brief、方案，作为人类自己写。"},{"i":627,"s":3589.06,"e":3594.66,"en":"Write it yourself, don't start with AI, don't, and us, and even don't use it to improve on the writing.","zh":"自己写，不要从 AI 开始，甚至也不要用它来改进文字。"},{"i":628,"s":3595.08,"e":3596.12,"en":"Just keep that all human.","zh":"这部分全部保持人类完成。"},{"i":629,"s":3596.36,"e":3601.08,"en":"Yeah, at least at least for me, I start myself and I end myself.","zh":"对，至少对我来说是这样：开头是我，结尾是我。"},{"i":630,"s":3601.68,"e":3607.52,"en":"I might use AI in the middle to research specific elements or drop in some data or go pull some data or help me.","zh":"中间我可能会用 AI 去研究某些具体细节、补一些数据、去拉点数据，或者帮我。"},{"i":631,"s":3607.52,"e":3608.6,"en":"Push back on some ideas.","zh":"帮你挑战一些想法。"},{"i":632,"s":3608.84,"e":3615.69,"en":"Yeah, push back on some ideas, but start yourself and end yourself with a piece of writing, and that doesn't deteriorate your thinking.","zh":"对，挑战一些想法。但一篇写作要自己开头、自己收尾，这样才不会让你的思考退化。"},{"i":633,"s":3616.25,"e":3619.21,"en":"OK, one last uh question I want to ask about Sutter Hill.","zh":"好，最后一个问题，我想问问 Sutter Hill。"},{"i":634,"s":3619.53,"e":3633.47,"en":"You had this very unusual career step, you went to Here, PM, PM founder person, and then just like, okay, EIR at Sutter Hill Ventures, which is a iconic VC, oh, people can look it up, a lot of amazing companies came out of Sutter Hill.","zh":"你有过一段很不寻常的职业转折：你先是做 PM、做那种 PM 兼创始人的角色，然后就直接去 Sutter Hill Ventures 做 EIR 了，那是一家标志性的 VC——大家可以去查一下，很多了不起的公司都出自 Sutter Hill。"},{"i":635,"s":3633.71,"e":3637.95,"en":"it was, it has a very unique way of approaching founding, where basically they incubate companies.","zh":"它有一套非常独特的创办公司的方式，基本上是他们自己孵化公司。"},{"i":636,"s":3637.95,"e":3639.47,"en":"Snowflake is an example.","zh":"Snowflake 就是一个例子。"},{"i":637,"s":3640.35,"e":3642.87,"en":"um, what was that, what was that about?","zh":"那到底是怎么回事？"},{"i":638,"s":3643.03,"e":3644.11,"en":"What would you learn from that experience?","zh":"你从那段经历里学到了什么？"},{"i":639,"s":3644.97,"e":3649.49,"en":"Sutter Hill is an iconic firm, and is intentionally a very illegible firm.","zh":"Sutter Hill 是一家标志性的机构，而且是刻意让自己「难以被读懂」的机构。"},{"i":640,"s":3649.73,"e":3653.17,"en":"Like, if you go to the Sutter Hill website, you will see nothing on the website.","zh":"比如你去 Sutter Hill 的官网，上面基本什么都看不到。"},{"i":641,"s":3653.25,"e":3666.72,"en":"It is a spe- a firm that doesn't operate loudly, it tries to operate as under the radar as possible, as modestly as possible, yet is somehow responsible for some of the most iconic successes that Silicon Valley has seen.","zh":"它是一家不张扬的机构，尽可能低调地运作、尽可能不惹眼，但又不知怎么地，硅谷一些最具标志性的成功案例都出自他们手里。"},{"i":642,"s":3667.04,"e":3679.52,"en":"And they have this very unusual incubation model, which Mike Speiser who is the like one of the amazing partners there, started and um has rolled out success after success.","zh":"他们有一套非常特别的孵化模式，是 Mike Speiser——那里最了不起的合伙人之一——开创的，并且一次又一次地做出成功案例。"},{"i":643,"s":3680.04,"e":3686.32,"en":"I think the thing that was most iconic to me about Sutter Hill is that people look at pro-, finding product market fit as a dark art.","zh":"我觉得 Sutter Hill 最让我印象深刻的一点是：大家都把找到产品市场契合当成一门玄学。"},{"i":644,"s":3686.81,"e":3689.97,"en":"Or building like a tens of billion dollar company as a dark art.","zh":"或者把做出一家几百亿美元的公司当成玄学。"},{"i":645,"s":3690.25,"e":3695.01,"en":"Like, oh, it's luck, oh it's chance, oh it's all these like things that must come together.","zh":"好像它全靠运气、全靠机缘，全靠各种条件恰好凑到一起。"},{"i":646,"s":3695.17,"e":3698.49,"en":"Yet Mike Speiser has done it multiple times.","zh":"可是 Mike Speiser 已经做成过很多次了。"},{"i":647,"s":3699.27,"e":3702.15,"en":"And so, there is there is like clearly a way to do it.","zh":"所以显然是有方法可循的。"},{"i":648,"s":3702.27,"e":3704.47,"en":"There is clearly a road map for making that possible.","zh":"显然是有一份路线图能让这件事成为可能的。"},{"i":649,"s":3704.79,"e":3707.59,"en":"There is like a set of things one can do to get this repeatedly.","zh":"显然有一套动作，可以让人反复做成这件事。"},{"i":650,"s":3707.75,"e":3708.59,"en":"It's not just luck.","zh":"它不只是运气。"},{"i":651,"s":3709.15,"e":3710.11,"en":"It's not just a dark art.","zh":"它不只是玄学。"},{"i":652,"s":3710.59,"e":3722.59,"en":"There is a there is a playbook as it were, and that playbook lives inside of the firm Sutter Hill, and they have figured out how to be right a lot in terms of like calling shots and making bets.","zh":"确实存在一套打法，而那套打法就活在 Sutter Hill 这家机构内部，他们琢磨出了怎样在判断和下注上大概率正确。"},{"i":653,"s":3723.06,"e":3730.38,"en":"And they've learned how to be right a lot in terms of the like daily compounding things that one does to create a successful company.","zh":"他们也学会了在那些日复一日复利式的动作上大概率正确——就是那些造就一家成功公司的日常动作。"},{"i":654,"s":3730.58,"e":3735.34,"en":"Whether that's how you set up your enterprise sales team, how you position your product.","zh":"无论是怎么搭建你的企业销售团队，还是怎么给产品做定位。"},{"i":655,"s":3735.85,"e":3743.33,"en":"How you like build the initial founding team, the recruiting at Sutter Hill is like an unparalleled excellent thing.","zh":"还是怎么组建最初的创始团队——Sutter Hill 的招聘水平是无与伦比的。"},{"i":656,"s":3743.41,"e":3745.21,"en":"They have a secret tool called Radicle.","zh":"他们有个秘密工具，叫 Radicle。"},{"i":657,"s":3746.02,"e":3752.58,"en":"Where they have a map of you know everyone and uh that they've interacted with, and the 10 best people that those people have interacted with.","zh":"里面有一张图谱，记录了他们打过交道的所有人，以及那些人打过交道的最优秀的十个人。"},{"i":658,"s":3753.02,"e":3755.34,"en":"um, That helps them be so so effective at this.","zh":"这让他们在这件事上极其高效。"},{"i":659,"s":3756.06,"e":3766.66,"en":"um, so, I went to Sutter Hill because in some way, my career has been about how do I try to find product market fit as many times as possible, whether that was as a founder or in starting new products at Stripe.","zh":"我去 Sutter Hill，某种程度上是因为我的职业生涯一直围绕着一个问题：怎样尽可能多次地找到产品市场契合——无论是作为创始人，还是在 Stripe 做新产品。"},{"i":660,"s":3767.32,"e":3769.36,"en":"Or in like joining a startup like Watershed.","zh":"或者是加入 Watershed 这样的创业公司。"},{"i":661,"s":3769.36,"e":3776.64,"en":"And so, Sutter Hill is a place where they've figured out how to find product market fit on B to B products, and I wanted to learn what I could from them.","zh":"而 Sutter Hill 正是一个搞明白了怎样在 B2B 产品上找到产品市场契合的地方，我想从他们那里学到我能学的东西。"},{"i":662,"s":3777.04,"e":3777.48,"en":"What'd you learn?","zh":"你学到了什么？"},{"i":663,"s":3777.48,"e":3780.36,"en":"What's one thing you took away from that experience other than they know how to do it?","zh":"除了「他们确实会做」之外，你从那段经历里带走的一件事是什么？"},{"i":664,"s":3780.44,"e":3782.2,"en":"They they definitely know how to do it.","zh":"他们是真的会做。"},{"i":665,"s":3782.6,"e":3788.8,"en":"I think um one thing that was very surprising to me that I learned there is that product market fit is sure important.","zh":"我在那里学到的一件让我非常意外的事是：产品市场契合当然重要。"},{"i":666,"s":3789.26,"e":3792.18,"en":"But actually, I really underrated product marketing fit.","zh":"但其实我严重低估了「产品营销契合」。"},{"i":667,"s":3792.54,"e":3799.02,"en":"The idea that the way you talk about the product and the way you market it can precede actually even building the product.","zh":"也就是说，你如何谈论这个产品、如何做市场表达，其实可以先于产品的构建。"},{"i":668,"s":3799.66,"e":3811.06,"en":"It should probably come from some sort of bringing together of understanding the technology deeply, and then understanding like the enterprise sales process, and then that product marketing fit, that narrative, that positioning.","zh":"它大概应该来自几件事的结合：深入理解技术，理解企业销售流程，然后是产品营销契合、叙事、定位。"},{"i":669,"s":3811.62,"e":3815.3,"en":"Is actually even before you build the product experience the right thing to test.","zh":"在你真正打造产品体验之前，这才是应该先去验证的东西。"},{"i":670,"s":3815.86,"e":3823.66,"en":"So you should go like pitch 100 people, figure out how to refine that pitch as much as possible, get the marketing narrative of why this thing is transformative.","zh":"所以你应该去给 100 个人做 pitch，尽可能打磨这套说法，把「这东西为什么是颠覆性的」这条营销叙事跑通。"},{"i":671,"s":3824.26,"e":3829.06,"en":"Right, and then and only then, go commit the, okay, this is exactly the product shape.","zh":"对，到那时候、也只有到那时候，才去定下来：好，产品就长这个形态。"},{"i":672,"s":3829.46,"e":3832.78,"en":"And my advisor is like unbeatable at this art.","zh":"而我那位导师在这门手艺上简直无人能敌。"},{"i":673,"s":3833.1,"e":3839.91,"en":"Previously, I had always kind of underrated PMM work, I was like, yeah, it's whatever, like, it's the glue between these functions, it's fine.","zh":"以前我一直有点低估 PMM 的工作，觉得，哎，也就那样吧，就是各个职能之间的黏合剂，还行吧。"},{"i":674,"s":3840.03,"e":3851.36,"en":"And then I realized how transformative that work done excellently is to a company's outcome, and in fact, can be the element that makes a company successful.","zh":"然后我才意识到，这项工作做到极致时有多大的颠覆性，它对一家公司结果的影响，甚至可以成为让公司成功的那个决定性要素。"},{"i":675,"s":3851.72,"e":3853.64,"en":"Amazing, uh, I so agree with that.","zh":"太棒了，我完全同意。"},{"i":676,"s":3853.64,"e":3855.76,"en":"Positioning, we talk a lot about that on this podcast.","zh":"定位——我们在这个播客里聊过很多。"},{"i":677,"s":3855.96,"e":3856.36,"en":"Mm-hmm.","zh":"嗯。"},{"i":678,"s":3856.73,"e":3859.49,"en":"OK, I'm gonna show you what uh sites got created real quick.","zh":"好，我快速给你看看刚才生成出来的网站。"},{"i":679,"s":3859.69,"e":3861.25,"en":"Ha, it was running while we were talking.","zh":"哈，我们聊天的时候它一直在跑。"},{"i":680,"s":3861.53,"e":3862.53,"en":"Check this out, look at this.","zh":"来看看这个，看这个。"},{"i":681,"s":3862.65,"e":3863.01,"en":"Oh, man.","zh":"哇。"},{"i":682,"s":3863.49,"e":3866.25,"en":"I was like, I was like, make it more awesome, and it made it more awesome.","zh":"我就说了句「让它更酷一点」，它就真的更酷了。"},{"i":683,"s":3867.41,"e":3868.13,"en":"Multi product.","zh":"多产品。"},{"i":684,"s":3869.53,"e":3871.73,"en":"Beautiful, look at this, this is like vintage design.","zh":"太漂亮了，看这个，这有点复古设计的感觉。"},{"i":685,"s":3871.93,"e":3876.73,"en":"Look at that, quotes, big conviction, small teams, sure, direct the buyer.","zh":"看那儿，引言：强信念、小团队，还有，直面买家。"},{"i":686,"s":3876.89,"e":3879.97,"en":"How do you feel about this being your website, your new website?","zh":"把这个当成你的网站、你的新网站，你感觉怎么样？"},{"i":687,"s":3880.65,"e":3885.05,"en":"I do think of the picture of me at maybe 19 years old at the top is really funny.","zh":"我确实觉得最上面那张我大概 19 岁时的照片挺搞笑的。"},{"i":688,"s":3885.65,"e":3888.61,"en":"But yeah, otherwise, I love love the site.","zh":"不过除此之外，我非常非常喜欢这个网站。"},{"i":689,"s":3889.09,"e":3889.77,"en":"OK, good job.","zh":"好，干得漂亮。"},{"i":690,"s":3889.77,"e":3890.33,"en":"Looking good.","zh":"看着不错。"},{"i":691,"s":3890.73,"e":3893.53,"en":"I think that was that's my, that was my badge photo from Stripe.","zh":"我想那是我在 Stripe 的工牌照片。"},{"i":692,"s":3893.81,"e":3894.97,"en":"Oh, wow, amazing.","zh":"哇，太赞了。"},{"i":693,"s":3895.37,"e":3899.81,"en":"I I love that it built, already, unsheathed it, but I love that it built the whole like little thing it's around your head.","zh":"我喜欢它已经做出来了、还把图抠了出来，但我更喜欢它在你脑袋周围做的那个小造型。"},{"i":694,"s":3900.45,"e":3900.93,"en":"So cute.","zh":"太可爱了。"},{"i":695,"s":3901.81,"e":3908.37,"en":"uh, Tara, is there anything else that you wanted to share, anything else you wanna uh touch on before we get to a very exciting lightning round?","zh":"Tara，在我们进入非常精彩的快问快答之前，你还有什么想分享、想聊的吗？"},{"i":696,"s":3908.61,"e":3915.33,"en":"Yeah, one thing that we've been thinking about a lot in product building, especially with ChatGPT for Work in this new era, is how knowledge work and coding.","zh":"有，我们在做产品时想得很多的一件事，尤其是在这个新时代做 ChatGPT for Work 的时候，就是知识工作和编程。"},{"i":697,"s":3915.82,"e":3917.3,"en":"are actually fundamentally different.","zh":"其实是根本不同的。"},{"i":698,"s":3917.74,"e":3931.01,"en":"And one of the surprising things we learned as a part of that is that coding is so output oriented that when you um, ask it to do a coding task, you can verify whether it did the task correctly or well via tests.","zh":"我们从中学到的一个意外发现是：编程非常以产出为导向，当你让它做一个编程任务时，你可以通过测试来验证它做得对不对、好不好。"},{"i":699,"s":3931.49,"e":3933.29,"en":"You can try it out and see if it works.","zh":"你可以跑一下，看它能不能跑通。"},{"i":700,"s":3933.29,"e":3936.97,"en":"Like there is a way to validate it based on the output.","zh":"也就是说，存在一种基于产出来验证的方法。"},{"i":701,"s":3937.31,"e":3943.19,"en":"But knowledge work is different, in that, I can't simply look at the deck in the end, and see the numbers.","zh":"但知识工作不一样——我没法只看最后那份 deck、看看里面的数字。"},{"i":702,"s":3943.31,"e":3947.03,"en":"Oh, oh, it's like 90 percent success or whatever in the deck, and actually believe that.","zh":"哦，deck 里写着 90% 的成功率之类的，然后就真的相信它。"},{"i":703,"s":3947.19,"e":3952.73,"en":"I really need to think about the process and the inputs and the reasoning and how it went along the way.","zh":"我真的需要去思考它的过程、输入、推理，以及它一路是怎么走过来的。"},{"i":704,"s":3952.77,"e":3960.65,"en":"And so in terms of how that looks in the product, like a lot of work that we have done and have to continue to do.","zh":"所以落到产品上，我们已经做了、并且还要继续做的很多工作。"},{"i":705,"s":3961.09,"e":3971.09,"en":"Is continue to adapt the product to knowledge work, which means way more focus on making ChatGPT your collaborator, allowing you to see all the in progress work.","zh":"就是继续把产品适配到知识工作上，也就是要更聚焦于让 ChatGPT 成为你的协作者，让你能看到所有正在进行中的工作。"},{"i":706,"s":3971.5,"e":3981.86,"en":"See its citations and inputs, help you go on the journey with the model to get to that end output, such that you know in the end, oh wait, this thing is right, this thing is good.","zh":"看到它的引用和输入，帮你和模型一起走完通往最终产出的整个过程，这样你最后才会觉得，等等，这个东西是对的，是好的，"},{"i":707,"s":3982.02,"e":3982.78,"en":"this thing is useful.","zh":"是有用的。"},{"i":708,"s":3983.24,"e":3990.24,"en":"And that shows up certainly in the UX of the product quite a bit, but also should show up in things like reasoning in the chain of thought.","zh":"这一点当然会大量体现在产品的交互体验上，但也应该体现在思维链的推理过程这类地方。"},{"i":709,"s":3990.28,"e":3995.32,"en":"Like, should I, should you see more citations along the way, for example of how it got to that end state in that data.","zh":"比如说，你是不是应该在过程中看到更多引用，看到它是怎么一步步得出那个结论、用了哪些数据。"},{"i":710,"s":3995.93,"e":4003.45,"en":"um, is the surface of a thread, which is so s- suited to coding, the right place for you to see all of that for knowledge work as well.","zh":"还有，对话线程这种界面形态非常适合写代码，但它是不是也适合让你在知识工作里看到这一切？"},{"i":711,"s":4003.53,"e":4006.41,"en":"There's so many big important product questions.","zh":"有太多重要的产品问题了。"},{"i":712,"s":4006.95,"e":4017.47,"en":"And so, as we think of um maybe bringing in human collaborators into your work, we also need to think about how we can make the model more of a collaborator with you as you get things done together.","zh":"所以，当我们在考虑把人类协作者引入你的工作时，我们也需要考虑怎么让模型更像一个和你一起把事情做完的协作者。"},{"i":713,"s":4018.04,"e":4018.96,"en":"That is such a good point.","zh":"这个点说得太好了。"},{"i":714,"s":4019.08,"e":4027.92,"en":"I'm imagining an exec meeting where you are trying to pitch the exec on, here's what the plan is, here's the six, here's what I think we should be doing.","zh":"我在想象一个高管会议的场景，你要向高管们推销你的方案：这是计划，这是那六个要点，这是我认为我们应该做的事。"},{"i":715,"s":4028.34,"e":4042.66,"en":"So much of that is helping them see, here's the work I did to get there, here's all the steps, and and so it make sense that you need the AI to show you that same sort of uh work that it did the proof of work essentially.","zh":"这里面很大一部分是让他们看到，这是我为此做的工作，这是所有的步骤，所以你确实需要 AI 也把它做的这些工作展示给你，本质上就是工作量的证明。"},{"i":716,"s":4043.26,"e":4048.9,"en":"Versus engineering, we're like, okay, I don't need to know all of the little architectural decisions you made, just what does it look like?","zh":"而工程那边就不一样，我们会说，好，我不需要知道你做的每一个架构小决策，就看它长什么样？"},{"i":717,"s":4048.98,"e":4050.26,"en":"Is it passing all the tests that we have?","zh":"它能通过我们所有的测试吗？"},{"i":718,"s":4050.74,"e":4053.98,"en":"So, that is a really good point, just how different those two models are.","zh":"所以这个点真的很好，这两种模式差别有多大。"},{"i":719,"s":4054.46,"e":4059.78,"en":"um, and also, there's like the context, does it have the context it needs to do the thing that you wanted to do?","zh":"另外还有上下文的问题，它有没有拿到完成你想让它做的事所需要的上下文？"},{"i":720,"s":4059.9,"e":4060.3,"en":"Does it know?","zh":"它知道吗？"},{"i":721,"s":4060.42,"e":4062.74,"en":"Does it, can it see your email, can it see all your Notion docs?","zh":"它能不能看到你的邮件，能不能看到你所有的 Notion 文档？"},{"i":722,"s":4063.54,"e":4064.46,"en":"uh, such a good point.","zh":"这个点太好了。"},{"i":723,"s":4064.7,"e":4068.26,"en":"So, I see the challenge in your job, make all this work as one product.","zh":"所以我能看出你工作的难点，就是要把这一切做成一个统一的产品。"},{"i":724,"s":4068.46,"e":4069.22,"en":"Tricky tricky.","zh":"很棘手，很棘手。"},{"i":725,"s":4070.46,"e":4071.5,"en":"uh, amazing.","zh":"太精彩了。"},{"i":726,"s":4071.66,"e":4073.66,"en":"Anything else before you get to our very exciting lightning round?","zh":"在进入我们非常刺激的快问快答之前，还有什么要补充的吗？"},{"i":727,"s":4074.12,"e":4075.48,"en":"Yeah, let's just get to it.","zh":"没有了，直接开始吧。"},{"i":728,"s":4075.6,"e":4078.32,"en":"With that, we've reached our very exciting lightning round.","zh":"那么，我们就进入非常刺激的快问快答环节。"},{"i":729,"s":4078.32,"e":4079.88,"en":"I've got five questions for you.","zh":"我有五个问题要问你。"},{"i":730,"s":4079.92,"e":4080.36,"en":"Are you ready?","zh":"准备好了吗？"},{"i":731,"s":4080.64,"e":4081.0,"en":"Yes.","zh":"准备好了。"},{"i":732,"s":4082.28,"e":4085.76,"en":"What are two or three books that you find yourself recommending most to other people?","zh":"有哪两三本书是你最常推荐给别人的？"},{"i":733,"s":4086.51,"e":4090.19,"en":"One book I really recommend to people is Barbarian Days by William Finnegan.","zh":"我特别推荐给大家的一本书是 William Finnegan 的《Barbarian Days》。"},{"i":734,"s":4090.63,"e":4096.87,"en":"I don't know if you read it, it's about a life of a man who is a New Yorker reporter, but how he fell in love with surfing.","zh":"不知道你有没有读过，它讲的是一个《纽约客》记者的人生，讲他怎么爱上了冲浪。"},{"i":735,"s":4097.35,"e":4097.79,"en":"As his passion.","zh":"把冲浪当成自己的热爱。"},{"i":736,"s":4098.19,"e":4106.19,"en":"The thing I took away from the book is that uh one can be deeply passionate and dedicated and have something be your life purpose without you being good at it.","zh":"我从这本书里得到的是：一个人可以对某件事深深热爱、全身心投入，把它当作人生目的，哪怕自己并不擅长它。"},{"i":737,"s":4106.67,"e":4109.35,"en":"And it is about the art of like falling in love with surfing.","zh":"它讲的是爱上冲浪这件事本身的艺术。"},{"i":738,"s":4109.91,"e":4114.95,"en":"And his striving for excellence and perfection, whilst knowing that he will like never reach it.","zh":"以及他对卓越和完美的追求，同时又清楚自己永远达不到。"},{"i":739,"s":4114.95,"e":4124.26,"en":"It is such a compelling and transformative story for for how I think one should continue to to live our lives.","zh":"对于我认为一个人应该怎样继续过好自己的人生，这是一个非常有感染力、非常有改变力量的故事。"},{"i":740,"s":4124.54,"e":4127.46,"en":"I I I really really love that book.","zh":"我真的非常非常喜欢这本书。"},{"i":741,"s":4128.18,"e":4133.7,"en":"um, another book that I might recommend as a, as like a book that people should read.","zh":"另一本我会推荐的书，作为那种大家都应该读一读的书。"},{"i":742,"s":4134.57,"e":4138.49,"en":"um, I really love uh Anna Karenina.","zh":"我非常喜欢《安娜·卡列尼娜》。"},{"i":743,"s":4138.49,"e":4155.54,"en":"I've been rereading the classics lately, and I love Anna Karenina because it's like a book of layers, and I think that such a huge part of what we're gonna have to do in this new era is like transform ourselves or like take ourselves on a journey to do different things than what we were used to. And when I.","zh":"我最近在重读经典，我喜欢《安娜·卡列尼娜》是因为它像一本有很多层次的书，而我觉得在这个新时代，我们要做的很大一部分事情就是改造自己，或者说带着自己走一段旅程，去做那些和过去习惯的完全不同的事。当我"},{"i":744,"s":4155.82,"e":4161.64,"en":"think about that book I think about when I was thirteen, and I read it, I understood basically the plot.","zh":"想到那本书时，我会想起十三岁读它的时候，我基本上只读懂了情节。"},{"i":745,"s":4162.08,"e":4167.04,"en":"When I read it at like seventeen, I understood the European history dynamics, and like the class warfare.","zh":"十七岁左右再读，我读懂了欧洲的历史脉络，还有阶级冲突。"},{"i":746,"s":4167.51,"e":4172.27,"en":"And then when I read it at 30, I was like, oh, this is like a story about like a woman and uh humans.","zh":"而三十岁再读时，我才发现，哦，这原来是一个关于一个女人、关于人性的故事。"},{"i":747,"s":4172.47,"e":4180.79,"en":"And it just reminds me of like growth, and that it is possible to look at the same thing through multiple different lenses as you continue to grow.","zh":"它让我想到成长，想到随着你不断成长，是有可能用很多不同的视角去看同一件事的。"},{"i":748,"s":4181.37,"e":4186.69,"en":"um, which I think is kind of the challenge that's ahead all of us, ahead for all of us as we consider our careers as well.","zh":"我觉得这也差不多是摆在我们所有人面前的挑战，包括我们思考自己职业的时候。"},{"i":749,"s":4187.01,"e":4190.93,"en":"It's interesting on both these, like I could connect to AI in the time we're living in now too.","zh":"有意思的是，这两本书我都能联系到 AI 和我们现在所处的时代。"},{"i":750,"s":4191.45,"e":4193.93,"en":"uh, I also read recently read Anna Karenina.","zh":"我最近也读了《安娜·卡列尼娜》。"},{"i":751,"s":4194.13,"e":4195.01,"en":"What did you think?","zh":"你觉得怎么样？"},{"i":752,"s":4195.05,"e":4196.25,"en":"Early, early this year, amazing.","zh":"就是今年年初读的，太棒了。"},{"i":753,"s":4196.25,"e":4197.25,"en":"I've never read it before.","zh":"我之前从来没读过。"},{"i":754,"s":4197.41,"e":4204.73,"en":"I saw on a book list of like, here's what the smartest people in the world have read, and it's like a whole list of books, and that was one that I hadn't read, so I'm like, I gotta read that.","zh":"我在一个书单上看到的，那种「世界上最聪明的人都读过什么」的书单，一长串书，那本是我没读过的，所以我想，我得读一下。"},{"i":755,"s":4205.17,"e":4207.05,"en":"Yeah, uh, it was amazing.","zh":"读完觉得太棒了。"},{"i":756,"s":4207.45,"e":4210.53,"en":"uh, someone gave away the ending, which kind of made it less like surprising.","zh":"不过有人把结局剧透给我了，所以惊喜感少了一些。"},{"i":757,"s":4210.81,"e":4212.37,"en":"I don't want to give anything away, no spoilers.","zh":"我不剧透，绝不剧透。"},{"i":758,"s":4213.17,"e":4219.96,"en":"um, and I also felt like it was very long, and then I'm reading The Power Broker, which is like set the set the new precedent for a long.","zh":"我也觉得它非常长，然后我又开始读《The Power Broker》，那本书直接刷新了「长」的标准。"},{"i":759,"s":4220.16,"e":4222.88,"en":"Been reading it for half my life at this point.","zh":"到现在为止，我已经读了半辈子了。"},{"i":760,"s":4223.12,"e":4224.36,"en":"I love the I love The Power Broker.","zh":"我太爱《The Power Broker》了。"},{"i":761,"s":4224.36,"e":4230.0,"en":"Another thing I highly recommend to people is if if anyone follows the Substack, um, like Simon Haisell's Substack.","zh":"还有一件我强烈推荐的事：如果有人关注 Substack，比如 Simon Haisell 的 Substack。"},{"i":762,"s":4230.47,"e":4233.31,"en":"Where he does a slow read of important books.","zh":"他在上面带着大家慢读重要的书。"},{"i":763,"s":4233.47,"e":4241.23,"en":"So, he did one of War and Peace, and he's doing one of Wolf Hall, I think, or he did one of Wolf Hall, which is the Hilary Mantel book, like take it chapter by chapter.","zh":"他做过《战争与和平》，现在在做《狼厅》，我记得是，或者他已经做完了《狼厅》，就是 Hilary Mantel 那本，一章一章地读。"},{"i":764,"s":4241.59,"e":4246.99,"en":"That's like the only way to read something like The Power Broker or War and Peace or Ulysses, it's like chapter by chapter.","zh":"读《The Power Broker》《战争与和平》或者《尤利西斯》这种书，唯一的办法就是一章一章来。"},{"i":765,"s":4247.5,"e":4258.94,"en":"Speaking of that, there's uh, someone, I forget who told me this, there is a uh 99% Invisible book club breakdown of The Power Broker, where it's 13 episodes an hour to each.","zh":"说到这个，有人跟我说过，我忘了是谁，有一个 99% Invisible 的读书会做过《The Power Broker》的拆解，一共 13 期，每期一小时。"},{"i":766,"s":4259.26,"e":4263.46,"en":"And they go through a couple chapters of the book one at a time, and talk about it.","zh":"他们每次讲书里的几章，一次讲一点，然后展开讨论。"},{"i":767,"s":4263.5,"e":4273.73,"en":"And they have special guests like, Pete Buttigieg and AOC, and folks that lived in that area, and they talk about every you know the story, and it was so, it's so fun to read and listen to their analysis of it.","zh":"还请来特别嘉宾，比如 Pete Buttigieg 和 AOC，还有住在那一带的人，他们会聊每一个，你知道的，那些故事，特别有意思，边读边听他们的分析太好玩了。"},{"i":768,"s":4273.73,"e":4276.45,"en":"And then they have Robert Caro come on a couple times, I guess.","zh":"而且我记得他们还请 Robert Caro 上过几次节目。"},{"i":769,"s":4276.45,"e":4277.61,"en":"Wow, that's amazing.","zh":"哇，太棒了。"},{"i":770,"s":4278.01,"e":4279.37,"en":"Yeah, hot tip.","zh":"对，小贴士送上。"},{"i":771,"s":4279.75,"e":4281.83,"en":"OK, we'll keep going with our very lightning round.","zh":"好，我们继续快问快答。"},{"i":772,"s":4282.23,"e":4286.19,"en":"uh, favorite recent movie or TV show you've really enjoyed, if you've had time to watch anything.","zh":"最近最喜欢的电影或剧集，如果你有时间看的话。"},{"i":773,"s":4286.47,"e":4287.67,"en":"Of course, I watched the Odyssey.","zh":"当然，我看了《奥德赛》。"},{"i":774,"s":4288.31,"e":4291.51,"en":"I found it to be an incredible incredible film.","zh":"我觉得那是一部非常非常了不起的电影。"},{"i":775,"s":4292.09,"e":4296.21,"en":"It is about AI, as or my hot take is that it's about AI.","zh":"它讲的是 AI，或者说我的暴论是它讲的是 AI。"},{"i":776,"s":4296.33,"e":4299.53,"en":"um, or Christopher Nolan's view on how AI transforms society.","zh":"或者说是 Christopher Nolan 对 AI 如何改变社会的看法。"},{"i":777,"s":4300.33,"e":4303.53,"en":"um, which I I loved and I highly recommend watching The Odyssey.","zh":"我非常喜欢，强烈推荐去看《奥德赛》。"},{"i":778,"s":4303.89,"e":4313.72,"en":"He is like the he's just incredible director, and has bridged artistry and commercial success in a way that I think no other modern director has like done.","zh":"他就是那种，他就是个不可思议的导演，把艺术性和商业成功结合到了我认为没有其他现代导演做到的程度。"},{"i":779,"s":4314.32,"e":4317.2,"en":"I also recently watched the film Rashomon.","zh":"我最近还看了电影《罗生门》。"},{"i":780,"s":4317.69,"e":4328.17,"en":"Which is the Kurosawa film, um, that did for the first time, did that technique of telling a story through multiple people's perspectives, where you never know what was true in the end.","zh":"就是黑泽明那部，它第一次用了那种手法：通过多个人的视角讲同一个故事，而你到最后永远不知道真相是什么。"},{"i":781,"s":4328.52,"e":4335.24,"en":"Like that technique in film was pioneered by Kurosawa, and it reminds me what one can do under constraints.","zh":"电影里的这种手法是黑泽明开创的，它提醒我，人在受限的条件下能做出什么。"},{"i":782,"s":4335.88,"e":4341.2,"en":"That film was made in like the fifties, it was black and white, that like you can, you know there's a guy holding the camera.","zh":"那部电影大概是五十年代拍的，黑白片，你甚至能感觉到有个人举着摄影机。"},{"i":783,"s":4341.58,"e":4358.65,"en":"And yet it is so perfect, and it is such a tasteful, innovative, amazing example of creativity, and what I'm reminded of watching that film is like, I have a hundred times the power and tools that he had making that film in my iPhone.","zh":"但它却如此完美，是一个如此有品位、有创新、了不起的创造力范例，看那部电影时我想到的是，我的 iPhone 里就有比他拍那部片时强一百倍的能力和工具。"},{"i":784,"s":4358.69,"e":4362.09,"en":"And like, what's my excuse for not elevating my ambitions and making better stuff?","zh":"那我还有什么借口不去抬高自己的野心、做出更好的东西呢？"},{"i":785,"s":4362.49,"e":4363.65,"en":"All comes back to ambition.","zh":"一切又回到野心上。"},{"i":786,"s":4364.77,"e":4367.49,"en":"uh, on the Odyssey, I'm still trying to get tickets.","zh":"说到《奥德赛》，我还在想办法搞到票。"},{"i":787,"s":4367.53,"e":4368.25,"en":"It's so hard.","zh":"太难了。"},{"i":788,"s":4368.77,"e":4372.13,"en":"I slept on it, and now it's like, no, impossible, for like a month.","zh":"我错过了时机，现在完全不可能，接下来一个月都没戏。"},{"i":789,"s":4372.25,"e":4373.33,"en":"There's no seats anywhere.","zh":"哪儿都没有座位了。"},{"i":790,"s":4373.41,"e":4377.65,"en":"Kevin Cox got us tickets at 10:00 PM at the Metreon earlier this week.","zh":"Kevin Cox 这周早些时候帮我们搞到了 Metreon 晚上十点的票。"},{"i":791,"s":4377.77,"e":4378.37,"en":"It was so good.","zh":"太好看了。"},{"i":792,"s":4378.81,"e":4380.53,"en":"Next time call me, I mean.","zh":"下次叫上我啊。"},{"i":793,"s":4380.69,"e":4381.69,"en":"Let me see.","zh":"我看看。"},{"i":794,"s":4382.21,"e":4387.29,"en":"Oh, man, I have like bots running on it, I have a person working on it, I have a friend who's trying, I'll try to find it.","zh":"天哪，我都开了机器人在抢票，还找了个人帮我盯着，还有个朋友在帮忙，我会想办法搞到的。"},{"i":795,"s":4387.29,"e":4394.27,"en":"It's amazing, you're gonna love it, and I can't wait to hear what you think after you see it, and if you agree with me that it is about AI and the collapse of morality.","zh":"太棒了，你会喜欢的，我迫不及待想听你看完之后的想法，看你是否同意我说的，它讲的是 AI 与道德的崩塌。"},{"i":796,"s":4394.87,"e":4395.83,"en":"OK, no spoilers.","zh":"好，不剧透。"},{"i":797,"s":4396.43,"e":4401.27,"en":"uh, hopefully by the time this comes out, I have seen it, but if not, if anyone has hookups, please tell me.","zh":"希望这期节目上线的时候我已经看过了，如果还没看，谁有门路，请告诉我。"},{"i":798,"s":4401.63,"e":4404.51,"en":"uh, and I'm trying to do like the IMAX full power matrix sort of thing.","zh":"我想搞成 IMAX 满配那种体验。"},{"i":799,"s":4405.03,"e":4406.63,"en":"Yeah, OK, next question.","zh":"好，下一个问题。"},{"i":800,"s":4406.79,"e":4415.79,"en":"uh, favorite or interesting AI product they recently discovered, if ideally not uh OpenAI product, but you know, you can also go there if you want.","zh":"最近发现的最喜欢或者最有意思的 AI 产品，最好不是 OpenAI 的产品，不过你想说的话也可以说。"},{"i":801,"s":4416.32,"e":4425.6,"en":"Ooh, um, I mean, of course, my favorite AI product is ChatGPT, and using cool sites and visualize stuff in in Codex, which is amazing.","zh":"哦，我最喜欢的 AI 产品当然是 ChatGPT，还有用 Codex 做很酷的网站、把东西可视化出来，那个太棒了。"},{"i":802,"s":4425.6,"e":4427.91,"en":"But outside of OpenAI products.","zh":"但要说 OpenAI 之外的产品的话。"},{"i":803,"s":4428.27,"e":4433.59,"en":"um, my favorite AI products are are products of my friends make for me, cause now actually people can do that.","zh":"我最喜欢的 AI 产品是我朋友们为我做的产品，因为现在人们真的能做到这件事了。"},{"i":804,"s":4433.79,"e":4434.75,"en":"I think that's so cool.","zh":"我觉得这太酷了。"},{"i":805,"s":4434.83,"e":4441.03,"en":"I'm such a huge fan of like the Cozy Software movement, where you like make software tools for like five of your friends, and you guys use it together.","zh":"我特别喜欢所谓的 Cozy Software 运动，就是你为五个朋友做一个软件工具，然后你们一起用。"},{"i":806,"s":4441.48,"e":4452.99,"en":"And so, I have a friend named Sebastian, who um made a really cool uh AI app that turns anything into a podcast, and puts it in your like a little little podcast app for you.","zh":"我有个朋友叫 Sebastian，他做了一个特别酷的 AI 应用，能把任何东西变成播客，然后放进你的，就像一个小小的播客应用里。"},{"i":807,"s":4452.99,"e":4456.91,"en":"and he also made a really great private social network for our friends.","zh":"他还给我们这群朋友做了一个特别棒的私密社交网络。"},{"i":808,"s":4457.71,"e":4459.23,"en":"And it's called Gatz.","zh":"它叫 Gatz。"},{"i":809,"s":4459.23,"e":4466.11,"en":"It is exactly what I think the future should be, which is people should make software that exactly meets their and their friends' needs.","zh":"这正是我认为未来该有的样子：人们应该做出恰好满足自己和朋友需求的软件。"},{"i":810,"s":4466.27,"e":4467.35,"en":"What does Gatz stand for?","zh":"Gatz 是什么意思的缩写？"},{"i":811,"s":4467.43,"e":4468.27,"en":"Is that some inside joke?","zh":"是什么内部梗吗？"},{"i":812,"s":4469.08,"e":4473.12,"en":"It is not, or at least if it is an inside joke, I don't know it.","zh":"不是，或者至少如果是内部梗，我也不知道。"},{"i":813,"s":4473.76,"e":4474.12,"en":"Ha ha ha.","zh":"哈哈哈。"},{"i":814,"s":4474.44,"e":4482.24,"en":"But it is the place that I, it's it's like private Twitter maybe for like a a group of a small group of friends, and I I learn the most interesting things on that product.","zh":"但它就是那个地方，有点像一小群朋友之间的私人 Twitter，我在那个产品上学到的东西最有意思。"},{"i":815,"s":4482.79,"e":4484.03,"en":"It's like a WhatsApp but not.","zh":"有点像 WhatsApp，但又不是。"},{"i":816,"s":4484.03,"e":4485.67,"en":"Yes, exactly, exactly.","zh":"对，完全正确，完全正确。"},{"i":817,"s":4486.15,"e":4492.91,"en":"uh, the podcast app is interesting, but I'm, like, I feel like the version that I would love is, it's actually like podcasts in your feed of podcasts.","zh":"那个播客应用挺有意思的，不过我感觉我会喜欢的版本是，它其实是把播客直接放进你的播客订阅流里。"},{"i":818,"s":4493.29,"e":4493.45,"en":"Yeah.","zh":"对。"},{"i":819,"s":4493.45,"e":4496.05,"en":"And then it just new episodes get added of things you wanna read or whatever.","zh":"然后新一期就自动加进来，都是你想读的那些东西。"},{"i":820,"s":4496.29,"e":4497.53,"en":"Yeah, that's that's what it does.","zh":"对，它就是这么做的。"},{"i":821,"s":4498.09,"e":4500.49,"en":"It's a, it drops it in your Apple Podcast feed.","zh":"它会直接把内容丢进你的 Apple Podcasts 订阅源。"},{"i":822,"s":4500.49,"e":4501.69,"en":"Oh, amazing.","zh":"哦，太棒了。"},{"i":823,"s":4501.93,"e":4502.41,"en":"I want this.","zh":"我也想要这个。"},{"i":824,"s":4502.41,"e":4502.77,"en":"It's great.","zh":"非常好用。"},{"i":825,"s":4503.39,"e":4505.03,"en":"Help me help me subscribe to this.","zh":"帮我订阅一下这个。"},{"i":826,"s":4505.15,"e":4505.51,"en":"For sure.","zh":"没问题。"},{"i":827,"s":4505.55,"e":4506.55,"en":"OK, amazing.","zh":"好，太棒了。"},{"i":828,"s":4506.75,"e":4507.75,"en":"OK, two more questions.","zh":"好，还有两个问题。"},{"i":829,"s":4507.95,"e":4512.75,"en":"Do you have a favorite life motto that you find yourself coming back to often in work or in life?","zh":"你有没有一句人生格言，在工作或生活中经常回想起来？"},{"i":830,"s":4512.87,"e":4518.61,"en":"Ooh, my life motto that I come back to all the time in work is actually Toni Morrison's three takes on work.","zh":"哦，我在工作中一直会回想的人生格言，其实是 Toni Morrison 关于工作的三条心得。"},{"i":831,"s":4518.69,"e":4520.33,"en":"Let me like pull it up really quickly.","zh":"我快速把它翻出来。"},{"i":832,"s":4520.61,"e":4520.97,"en":"Amazing.","zh":"太好了。"},{"i":833,"s":4521.69,"e":4523.61,"en":"um, OK, it's four things.","zh":"好，其实是四条。"},{"i":834,"s":4523.77,"e":4526.41,"en":"It's from her essay, the work you do, the person you are.","zh":"出自她的那篇文章《你做的工作，你成为的人》。"},{"i":835,"s":4527.05,"e":4532.09,"en":"The first one is Whatever the work is, do it well, not for the boss, but for yourself.","zh":"第一条是：不管做什么工作，都要做好，不是为了老板，而是为了你自己。"},{"i":836,"s":4533.17,"e":4536.33,"en":"The second is, you make the job, it doesn't make you.","zh":"第二条是：是你成就了这份工作，而不是工作成就了你。"},{"i":837,"s":4537.33,"e":4539.37,"en":"The third is, your real life is with your family.","zh":"第三条是：你真正的生活在家人身边。"},{"i":838,"s":4540.34,"e":4544.02,"en":"And the fourth is you are not the work you do, you are the person that you are.","zh":"第四条是：你不是你做的工作，你是你这个人本身。"},{"i":839,"s":4545.7,"e":4546.42,"en":"I got tingles.","zh":"我起鸡皮疙瘩了。"},{"i":840,"s":4546.5,"e":4547.42,"en":"Ha ha ha.","zh":"哈哈哈。"},{"i":841,"s":4547.9,"e":4549.3,"en":"Wow, so good.","zh":"哇，太好了。"},{"i":842,"s":4549.58,"e":4552.38,"en":"And I think that's what you have pinned to your um your Twitter profile.","zh":"我记得这就是你置顶在 Twitter 个人主页上的内容。"},{"i":843,"s":4552.42,"e":4552.5,"en":"Yes.","zh":"是的。"},{"i":844,"s":4552.54,"e":4553.98,"en":"Because I remember seeing that.","zh":"因为我记得看到过。"},{"i":845,"s":4554.38,"e":4554.74,"en":"So cool.","zh":"太酷了。"},{"i":846,"s":4554.86,"e":4554.98,"en":"OK.","zh":"好。"},{"i":847,"s":4555.82,"e":4557.86,"en":"uh, maybe we'll show that on the screen as we're talking about that.","zh":"也许我们聊到这里的时候可以在屏幕上放出来。"},{"i":848,"s":4557.94,"e":4558.38,"en":"I love that.","zh":"我很喜欢。"},{"i":849,"s":4558.86,"e":4563.86,"en":"uh, I love that's a great way to remember something, just stick it to the top of your Twitter, because it's every time I go to Twitter, oh there it is again.","zh":"我觉得这是记住一件事的好办法，就把它置顶在你的 Twitter 上，因为每次我上 Twitter，哦，它又出现了。"},{"i":850,"s":4564.06,"e":4564.34,"en":"hmm-hmm.","zh":"嗯嗯。"},{"i":851,"s":4564.74,"e":4565.78,"en":"uh, OK, final question.","zh":"好，最后一个问题。"},{"i":852,"s":4566.35,"e":4568.51,"en":"uh, you were a Thiel Fellow back in the day.","zh":"你早年是 Thiel Fellow。"},{"i":853,"s":4568.79,"e":4570.55,"en":"Thiel Fellow, Teal or Thiel?","zh":"Thiel fellow，读作 Teal 还是 Thiel？"},{"i":854,"s":4570.63,"e":4571.63,"en":"Thiel, Thiel, Thiel.","zh":"Thiel，Thiel，Thiel。"},{"i":855,"s":4571.63,"e":4572.15,"en":"Yeah.","zh":"对。"},{"i":856,"s":4572.15,"e":4573.75,"en":"What an alumni group!","zh":"那批校友阵容太强了！"},{"i":857,"s":4573.95,"e":4577.47,"en":"Holy moly, just like, so it's such a great idea and program.","zh":"天哪，这真是个特别棒的点子和项目。"},{"i":858,"s":4577.95,"e":4583.11,"en":"uh, any story from that time that might be fun to share, something that's like, wow, that was crazy.","zh":"那段时间有什么好玩的故事可以分享吗，那种「哇，这太疯狂了」的事。"},{"i":859,"s":4583.71,"e":4588.11,"en":"I don't know any other Thiel Fellow that you're proud of, any other What was the interview like?","zh":"或者你欣赏的某位 Thiel Fellow，或者面试是什么样的？"},{"i":860,"s":4588.19,"e":4589.47,"en":"I don't know anything along those lines.","zh":"类似这样的都行。"},{"i":861,"s":4590.39,"e":4594.67,"en":"Yeah, I, the Thiel Fellowship was an inflection point in my life.","zh":"嗯，Thiel Fellowship 是我人生的一个转折点。"},{"i":862,"s":4595.15,"e":4597.15,"en":"I wouldn't be where I am without it.","zh":"没有它我不会走到今天。"},{"i":863,"s":4597.15,"e":4602.78,"en":"It maybe to the point of like, there are key moments where you can tell people to elevate their ambitions, and they do, and that changes them.","zh":"大概是说，人生有一些关键时刻，你可以让一个人把野心放大，他真的照做了，这就改变了他。"},{"i":864,"s":4602.78,"e":4609.3,"en":"Like, that was a moment where someone came to me and elevated my ambitions, and said, no, you can do this, you don't have to, you know, take the path that you were on.","zh":"那就是这样一个时刻，有人来找我，抬高了我的野心，说，不，你能做到，你不必走原来那条路。"},{"i":865,"s":4609.84,"e":4613.84,"en":"And truly, I'm eternally grateful for for them being able to do that.","zh":"说真的，我永远感激他们能做到这一点。"},{"i":866,"s":4614.44,"e":4623.68,"en":"One of the Thiel Fellows that I get to work with all the time now is Ari Weinstein, who uh founded a company called Sky that was acquired by OpenAI.","zh":"我现在天天一起共事的 Thiel Fellow 之一是 Ari Weinstein，他创办了一家叫 Sky 的公司，后来被 OpenAI 收购了。"},{"i":867,"s":4624.39,"e":4629.59,"en":"um, and prior to this, he founded um and worked at Apple for a while because they acquired his previous company.","zh":"在这之前他创办过公司，还在 Apple 工作了一段时间，因为 Apple 收购了他上一家公司。"},{"i":868,"s":4629.75,"e":4633.63,"en":"Ari is just one of the most creative thinkers I've ever seen.","zh":"Ari 是我见过最有创造力的思考者之一。"},{"i":869,"s":4634.19,"e":4640.51,"en":"And is truly the expert on what are all the cool things you can do on a Mac.","zh":"而且他是真正的专家，知道在 Mac 上能玩出的所有酷东西。"},{"i":870,"s":4641.03,"e":4652.93,"en":"um, and so, Ari leads a lot of our computer use stuff at OpenAI, and he's like shipped a whole bunch of great things for for computer use, but yeah, his his creativity and his like joy in what he does.","zh":"所以 Ari 在 OpenAI 负责我们很多 computer use 相关的工作，他做出了一堆很棒的 computer use 功能，但真正打动我的是他的创造力，还有他做事时的那种快乐。"},{"i":871,"s":4653.05,"e":4657.65,"en":"and his love of his craft really inspires me, and like Ari Ari is a cool guy.","zh":"他对自己手艺的热爱真的很激励我，Ari 是个很酷的人。"},{"i":872,"s":4658.24,"e":4664.48,"en":"um, but I'm trying to think what it's like a good story from that time that feels uh.","zh":"不过我在想那段时间有什么好故事……"},{"i":873,"s":4664.48,"e":4669.16,"en":"As you think about it, I'll explain the Thiel Fellowship for people that don't know this, and correct me if I'm wrong.","zh":"你想的时候，我先给不了解的人介绍一下 Thiel Fellowship，说错了你纠正我。"},{"i":874,"s":4669.59,"e":4673.07,"en":"Basically, Peter Thiel is like, uh, people shouldn't go to college.","zh":"基本上，Peter Thiel 的想法是，人们不该去上大学。"},{"i":875,"s":4673.51,"e":4678.91,"en":"Instead, they should just try building something that they want, and and you get 100 thousand dollars.","zh":"他们应该去做点自己真正想做的东西，然后你能拿到十万美元。"},{"i":876,"s":4679.61,"e":4682.21,"en":"To not do college, and instead just go follow your ambition.","zh":"条件是不上大学，去追求你的野心。"},{"i":877,"s":4683.13,"e":4683.97,"en":"Is that roughly correct?","zh":"大致是这样吗？"},{"i":878,"s":4683.97,"e":4685.53,"en":"Yeah, that is that is exactly right.","zh":"对，完全正确。"},{"i":879,"s":4685.81,"e":4686.33,"en":"um, cool.","zh":"酷。"},{"i":880,"s":4686.41,"e":4690.69,"en":"And you're with nineteen other people at the time, it was like twenty people every year, cause it's twenty under twenty.","zh":"当时和你一起的还有另外十九个人，每年大概二十个人，因为项目叫「二十岁以下二十人」。"},{"i":881,"s":4691.39,"e":4693.03,"en":"And, how many years did it go on for?","zh":"那这个项目办了多少年？"},{"i":882,"s":4693.15,"e":4693.43,"en":"Is it still going?","zh":"现在还在办吗？"},{"i":883,"s":4693.79,"e":4700.43,"en":"I think it's still going, but I think it was like that constrained at the 20 number for like the first four or five years or something like that.","zh":"我想还在办，但我记得只有最初四五年左右是严格限制在 20 人这个数字上的。"},{"i":884,"s":4702.0,"e":4706.88,"en":"Yeah, I think a really crazy thing that happened my year is that I was the second ever year of the fellowship.","zh":"对，我那一年发生的一件很疯狂的事是，我是这个项目的第二届。"},{"i":885,"s":4707.12,"e":4720.02,"en":"They decided to make it all a documentary on CNBC, and so our whole uh my pitch for the fellowship, uh, getting up on stage and presenting the idea I was going to do, all of that is unfortunately live on YouTube.","zh":"他们决定把整个过程拍成 CNBC 的纪录片，所以我为这个项目做的全部路演，上台讲我要做的想法，很不幸这些都还挂在 YouTube 上。"},{"i":886,"s":4720.02,"e":4725.74,"en":"So if you really wanna see me as a nineteen year old doing something embarrassing, it's there.","zh":"所以如果你真想看十九岁的我做点尴尬的事，那儿就有。"},{"i":887,"s":4726.4,"e":4737.0,"en":"um, of course, one of the most amazing and successful people who came out of that batch of the fellowship is Dylan Field, who is not only a incredible talent, but also like a very kind person.","zh":"当然，那一届里最了不起、最成功的人之一是 Dylan Field，他不仅才华横溢，人也非常善良。"},{"i":888,"s":4737.71,"e":4742.47,"en":"um, and yeah, feel very lucky to to be able to work with those folks.","zh":"是啊，能和这些人共事，我觉得非常幸运。"},{"i":889,"s":4743.07,"e":4743.83,"en":"Amazing, yeah.","zh":"太棒了，是啊。"},{"i":890,"s":4743.87,"e":4747.75,"en":"So interesting that Dylan's like the guy, I think everyone thinks of when they think of Thiel Fellows.","zh":"很有意思，一提到 Thiel Fellowship，我觉得大家想到的就是 Dylan。"},{"i":891,"s":4747.75,"e":4748.11,"en":"Yeah, yeah.","zh":"对，对。"},{"i":892,"s":4748.43,"e":4750.48,"en":"What if What a brand!","zh":"多好的招牌！"},{"i":893,"s":4750.64,"e":4752.72,"en":"OK, Tara, this was incredible.","zh":"好，Tara，这期太精彩了。"},{"i":894,"s":4753.28,"e":4757.68,"en":"uh, is there anything you want to plug, anything you want to point people to, and how can listeners be useful to you?","zh":"你有什么想推荐的、想让大家去看的吗？听众可以怎么帮到你？"},{"i":895,"s":4762.66,"e":4765.06,"en":"um, they should use ChatGPT in the web and try Work.","zh":"他们应该在网页版用 ChatGPT，试试 Work。"},{"i":896,"s":4765.18,"e":4766.86,"en":"It's like unfortunately a little toggle.","zh":"很遗憾它现在只是个小开关。"},{"i":897,"s":4767.46,"e":4770.62,"en":"um, they can toggle over to it and try out Work.","zh":"他们可以切换过去，试用 Work。"},{"i":898,"s":4770.7,"e":4773.66,"en":"Ask it to do some cool thing, ask it to build a site about you.","zh":"让它做点酷的事，比如让它给你做一个网站。"},{"i":899,"s":4774.18,"e":4779.7,"en":"uh, maybe to start, or ask it to make a little visualize a block of your ChatGPT usage.","zh":"可以先从这个开始，或者让它把你的 ChatGPT 使用情况做个小可视化。"},{"i":900,"s":4779.94,"e":4785.7,"en":"It's a really cool way to start like experiencing the power of this stuff.","zh":"这是非常好的入口，能让你非常直接地体验到这东西的威力。"},{"i":901,"s":4786.43,"e":4793.11,"en":"Very intimately, and the li- list of use cases they can do from that, you know, are infinite, and I'm happy.","zh":"从那之后你能想到的用例是无穷无尽的，我很乐意——"},{"i":902,"s":4793.11,"e":4794.67,"en":"Here's a better idea, here's a better idea.","zh":"我有个更好的主意，我有个更好的主意。"},{"i":903,"s":4794.87,"e":4794.99,"en":"Yes.","zh":"你说。"},{"i":904,"s":4795.31,"e":4797.75,"en":"Ask it to build a site to tell you what you could do with.","zh":"让它做个网站，告诉你能用什么做什么——"},{"i":905,"s":4798.16,"e":4798.28,"en":"work.","zh":"用 Work。"},{"i":906,"s":4798.56,"e":4799.2,"en":"Great.","zh":"很好。"},{"i":907,"s":4799.2,"e":4801.24,"en":"That will that will work.","zh":"那样就行。"},{"i":908,"s":4802.76,"e":4803.52,"en":"Solve all the problems.","zh":"所有问题都解决了。"},{"i":909,"s":4803.64,"e":4805.96,"en":"OK, ha, I interrupted you, I apologize.","zh":"好，哈，我打断你了，抱歉。"},{"i":910,"s":4806.12,"e":4807.96,"en":"uh, what else we gonna add or say?","zh":"你还想补充或者说点什么？"},{"i":911,"s":4808.08,"e":4814.84,"en":"Yeah, my main plug is yeah, go go download the ChatGPT app, go use it on web, even more transformatively, go try it on mobile.","zh":"嗯，我主要想推荐的就是，去下载 ChatGPT app，在网页上用，更有颠覆感的是，去手机上试试。"},{"i":912,"s":4815.35,"e":4822.59,"en":"Then take like a long subway ride or something like that or a Muni ride, and when you pop out after having no service, the thing is done for you.","zh":"然后去坐一趟长途地铁之类的，或者坐 Muni，等你从没信号的地方出来时，事情已经替你做完了。"},{"i":913,"s":4823.07,"e":4825.27,"en":"That's the part that feels super super magical.","zh":"那部分感觉超级超级神奇。"},{"i":914,"s":4825.35,"e":4831.01,"en":"You're not like wandering around your laptop open the entire time, you've finally got these things running in the cloud doing real work.","zh":"你不用全程守着笔记本电脑，你终于让这些东西在云端跑起来，真正干活了。"},{"i":915,"s":4831.45,"e":4838.37,"en":"Yeah, that last piece I was gonna bring up, but that's, I think it's a really underappreciated element of the product today.","zh":"对，最后这点我正想提，我觉得这是今天这个产品里非常被低估的一面。"},{"i":916,"s":4838.77,"e":4842.77,"en":"On mobile, it, and it's most, it that that's just a mobile only feature, the cloud piece.","zh":"在手机上……那个云端的部分只是手机端独有的功能吗？"},{"i":917,"s":4842.89,"e":4843.29,"en":"No, it's everywhere.","zh":"不，到处都有。"},{"i":918,"s":4843.37,"e":4844.29,"en":"It's everywhere.","zh":"所有端都有。"},{"i":919,"s":4844.33,"e":4845.89,"en":"OK, so amazing.","zh":"好，太棒了。"},{"i":920,"s":4846.13,"e":4848.73,"en":"So, on your mobile app, you can go to ChatGPT, toggle work.","zh":"所以在手机 app 上，你可以打开 ChatGPT，切到 Work。"},{"i":921,"s":4849.05,"e":4854.01,"en":"Ask it to do some work, and you don't need to actually have the, it's not running locally, it's running in the cloud.","zh":"让它去干活，你不需要一直开着，它不是在本地跑，是在云端跑。"},{"i":922,"s":4854.57,"e":4857.81,"en":"It'll go keep doing work until it's done, and then you could check to it.","zh":"它会一直做到做完，然后你回来看结果就行。"},{"i":923,"s":4857.89,"e":4861.75,"en":"So, like, it feels like really simple, but that's a massively powerful thing.","zh":"所以，这听起来很简单，但其实是一件威力巨大的事。"},{"i":924,"s":4863.11,"e":4866.99,"en":"OK, uh, anything else, Tara, before we let you go?","zh":"好，Tara，在结束之前还有什么要说的吗？"},{"i":925,"s":4867.11,"e":4868.15,"en":"No, that's it.","zh":"没有了，就这些。"},{"i":926,"s":4868.19,"e":4869.19,"en":"OK, thanks, Tara.","zh":"好，谢谢你，Tara。"},{"i":927,"s":4869.31,"e":4870.87,"en":"This was awesome, thank you so much for doing this.","zh":"这期太棒了，非常感谢你来。"},{"i":928,"s":4870.91,"e":4871.47,"en":"It's such a pleasure.","zh":"非常荣幸。"},{"i":929,"s":4871.63,"e":4873.71,"en":"uh, what a journey since the fellowship.","zh":"从 Thiel Fellowship 到现在，真是一段不小的旅程。"},{"i":930,"s":4874.06,"e":4876.5,"en":"Back in back in the day, I'll talk about that more in the intro.","zh":"从早年那会儿开始，我会在开场里多讲一些。"},{"i":931,"s":4876.58,"e":4876.98,"en":"Yeah.","zh":"好的。"},{"i":932,"s":4877.02,"e":4878.74,"en":"uh, all right, well, thanks for being here.","zh":"好，那么，谢谢你来。"},{"i":933,"s":4878.74,"e":4879.3,"en":"Thank you.","zh":"谢谢。"},{"i":934,"s":4879.82,"e":4880.58,"en":"Bye everyone.","zh":"大家再见。"},{"i":935,"s":4881.3,"e":4882.58,"en":"Thank you so much for listening.","zh":"非常感谢你的收听。"},{"i":936,"s":4882.9,"e":4888.78,"en":"If you found this valuable, you can subscribe to the show on Apple Podcasts, Spotify, or your favorite podcast app.","zh":"如果你觉得有价值，可以在 Apple Podcasts、Spotify 或你常用的播客应用上订阅本节目。"},{"i":937,"s":4889.1,"e":4895.06,"en":"Also, please consider giving us a rating or leaving a review, as that really helps other listeners find the podcast.","zh":"另外，也请考虑给我们评分或写条评论，这真的能帮助其他听众发现这档播客。"},{"i":938,"s":4895.62,"e":4902.1,"en":"You can find all past episodes or learn more about the show at Lenny's Podcast dot com. See you in the next episode.","zh":"你可以在 Lenny's Podcast dot com 上找到所有往期节目或了解更多。下期见。"}],"structure":{"chapters":[{"title":"开场：预告与嘉宾介绍","cues":[1,22],"sections":[{"title":"开场预告：AI 产品的第三个时代","kind":"intro","cues":[1,13],"paragraphs":[{"cues":[1,6],"speaker":"Tara"},{"cues":[7,7],"speaker":"Lenny"},{"cues":[8,12],"speaker":"Tara"},{"cues":[13,13],"speaker":"Lenny"}]},{"title":"嘉宾介绍：Tara Seshan 的履历","kind":"intro","cues":[14,22],"paragraphs":[{"cues":[14,15],"speaker":"Lenny"},{"cues